{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy","id":34987,"title":"Ask The Deadguy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-22T10:12:47-08:00","id":34987,"title":"Ask The Deadguy","content":"Hi, folks. Rich Dansky, Wraith 20th developer here. I just wanted to pop in and say hello, and let you know that I'll be on the forums going forward for questions, updates, and all sorts of other goodness. So by all means, say hello, ask questions, tell me what you want to see in Wraith going forward, and generally keep the conversation going. In return, I promise to answer questions (eventually - the day job is kind of time consuming), listen, post updates, and share fearsome anecdotes of old-school Wraith development. <br /> <br /> It's good to be back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T10:19:29-08:00","id":34998,"title":"","content":"What do the wraiths think about demons. their existance etc..<br /> <br /> Also, Does EVERY SINGLE HUMAN THAT DIES becomes a wraith?.<br /> <br /> On my campaing im using Wolfman Jack as a Wraith DJ who contacts the players through a Ghost Frecuence and gives them hints through music tracks. How pausible is this in the cannon of wraith (im recently starting to read the books)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T12:37:55-08:00","id":35077,"title":"","content":"BTW:, <b>thank you Rich for being an active developer for the game</b>. I really think that the games show a greater depth and connection with the players and fans when the developers interact with those who've invested their own time, money, and lives into the game from the player-side as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Even if I know nothing about W:tO (other than Sam Haight was soul-forged into an ash tray), I know that others really enjoy this game as much as I love W:tA, and I'm glad to see that they are getting great treatment. <br /> <br /> So, again, thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:47:07-08:00","id":35139,"title":"","content":"Like Fry said, &quot;Here, take my money!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm thrilled we're getting a Wr20. I look forward to seeing what's going to be going into things. Thank you much, Rich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T17:31:49-08:00","id":35216,"title":"","content":"Hi Rich! I'd like to direct your attention to the Forum thread titled Is The Wraith Setting Too Punishing? For your take or simply feedback from players. (Can't make a link, I'm posting from my phone) also, if this is really you Rich, wouldn't you have Mod status?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T17:59:51-08:00","id":35228,"title":"","content":"OK, fast answers today :-)<br /> <br /> Crowley:<br /> 1-Depends on the individual wraith :-)<br /> 2-Nope. Most humans don't have enough unfinished business worth sticking around for. <br /> 3-I heartily approve of the use of Wolfman Jack under any and all circumstances.<br /> <br /> Darling_Rose:<br /> It really is me. Honest. I suppose I'll worry about mod status at some point, but I'm more interested in just talking to folks. As for the thread, I've been lurking in it for a while, and I confess, I'm disappointed the original ranter spelled my name wrong. And in debating the point, I think it's important to remember 3 things: 1-Not every bad thing that can happen to a wraith is always happening to every wraith all the time 2-Wraiths are people, which means that they act according to individual motivations, not Big Rules Handed Down From Above and 3-Missing middle interpretations tend skip a lot of the good stuff. I think Wraith can be very punishing if all you focus on is the punishing aspects; I also think there's an awful lot of room for moments of human kindness and hope in there that are just as important to the setting. I would hope so, at least - it's why I put them in there in 2nd Edition. <br /> <br /> Big Brother, Torakhan: <br /> Thanks for the kind words. I'm very much looking forward to the challenge of the book, and to hopefully making something that folks can enjoy!<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:08:59-08:00","id":35234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=35216#post35216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, if this is really you Rich, wouldn't you have Mod status?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the authors and developers don't have mod status on the forums. Rose and I do because I also run the website, and she's in charge of the mod team.<br /> <br /> I can, however, guarantee that RealDeadGuy is Rich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:19:26-08:00","id":35238,"title":"","content":"Thanks Rich. (AND IAN!) I'm convinced. Just asking cuz no one can argue with Mod status that they belong to or are at least approved by OPP. It also means we can ignore anyone turning up with a name like MRein\u2022Hagen telling us &quot;Rocks fall everyone dies!&quot; :3<br /> <br /> Thanks for your input. I do agree that Wraith can have elements of hope. I just find it very hard to make use of them in game unless the ST just ignores making use of the 101 ways to die (AGAIN) that are the prevalent to the setting of Wraith. And that the other players are playing nice people with strong enough will to ignore their Shadows telling them to screw you over. That being said, in my history and cultural research I've found the Wraith setting to have more in common with the real worldwide multi-cultural depiction's of Hell than as a neutral Purgatory. The Shadowlands seems to be an ambiguous inoffensive PC term without coming right out and using the word 'Hell'. Was this intentional or were you actually going for a purgatory setting that has been turned into a hell, but is not supposed to be the actual place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  Fixed typos and added acknowledgements. 12-23-2013, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:20:46-08:00","id":35240,"title":"","content":"thanks for the help deadguy! awesome :P , i wish i could see a cameo the wolfman on the next book. keep an awesome job !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:30:18-08:00","id":35248,"title":"","content":"I'm very excited for Wraith 20th and glad to see that you're reaching out to the community during its development. I only got to play 2nd Ed Wraith briefly; a handful of sessions before the game fell apart due to scheduling conflicts. I never got a hold of the core rulebook. While I'm familiar with the basics of the game and enjoyed it, I don't have in-depth knowledge. There are a few big things I'd enjoy seeing from Wraith 20th:<br /> <br /> One, enough setting, background and basic material that a new player can learn the game and play fully from the main book. I'm rusty, and I hope to introduce Wraith to many friends who have never seen it before. V20 was a very crunch-heavy book. While I have no complaints about getting comprehensive rules, I feel it's especially important for Wraith20 to be detailed and illustrative about the setting and mood of the game.<br /> <br /> Two, Revised/V20-era system update.<br /> <br /> Finally, Shadowguiding. This was an aspect of Wraith that I thoroughly enjoyed and I really would like it to remain a part of the game. However, I've heard from a large number of people that they found it off-putting or difficult to include in their play. Maybe an alternative approach could be provided in a sidebar or something, for the players who are uncomfortable with the normal shadow guide rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":10,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","user":"Demon Cat","date":". 12-22-2013, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T21:48:54-08:00","id":35370,"title":"","content":"Rose:<br /> I always thought of it more as being in line with the classical Greek afterlife than a &quot;hell&quot;. Find the happy medium between &quot;Our Town&quot; and Hesiod's Theogony and you've got it :-)<br /> And I think you've nailed one of the main issues of Shadowguiding, which was getting people to get a sense of it as a way to enhance play, not grease the skids for other players. After all, the Shadow is self-destructive; it's not necessarily overtly suicidal, and it's got things it wants and fears, too. Pulling the conception of Shadowguiding back from the precipice of MUST DESTROY CHARACTER IMMEDIATELY to a more interesting place with broader gameplay options is something I definitely want to do.<br /> <br /> Demon Cat:<br /> Have you been listening in on the phone calls I've been having with Rich Thomas? Just curious :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T00:24:42-08:00","id":35423,"title":"","content":"I would love to pick your brain at length Rich. I've been studying archaeology and myths of ancient cultures as a hobby for years now and there's just so much that could be discussed and compared between the theoretical origins of greek mythos in history and the fantastical setting of Wraith in the WoD. We might need a new Wraith sub-foum if we were to explore that discussion. *Bats eyes*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T00:42:23-08:00","id":35431,"title":"","content":"We'll create a subforum when it's a little closer to Wraith20's release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T00:53:10-08:00","id":35436,"title":"","content":"It's excellent to see you here, Richard. One question for you, if I may, and it's a rather general one - if you could see one more Guildbook completed, which would you go for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T01:56:58-08:00","id":35461,"title":"","content":"A general question for you:<br /> <br /> How do you view Orpheus as you're working on Wr20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T04:45:00-08:00","id":35503,"title":"","content":"I guess the thing that I find challenging is understanding the nature of the shadowlands. For all intents and purposes, the shadowlands is an alien world which shares some of its living space with our own.<br /> <br /> If I were a wraith walking around your typical necropolis, what would I see?<br /> <br /> Do wraiths often move among the quick, or do they tend to avoid them?<br /> <br /> Would I see a lot of shadowlands buildings crammed in between skinlands ones?<br /> <br /> What happens when one of the quick takes a stroll through an area where a wraith has built a building? Does the quick just pass through the building, or does he crash through the wall?<br /> <br /> If I saw two objects in front of me, could I tell quickly which object was a shadowlands object, and which was a skinlands object?<br /> <br /> Can I tell the difference between an object made out of plasm, or whether it is a relic, artifact, or something else by looking at it?<br /> <br /> I hate to ask, but how does the Stygian economy work? What are they paying all these legionnaires to make them do what they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T04:50:30-08:00","id":35504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=35503#post35503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the thing that I find challenging is understanding the nature of the shadowlands. For all intents and purposes, the shadowlands is an alien world which shares some of its living space with our own.<br /> <br /> If I were a wraith walking around your typical necropolis, what would I see?<br /> <br /> Do wraiths often move among the quick, or do they tend to avoid them?<br /> <br /> Would I see a lot of shadowlands buildings crammed in between skinlands ones?<br /> <br /> What happens when one of the quick takes a stroll through an area where a wraith has built a building? Does the quick just pass through the building, or does he crash through the wall?<br /> <br /> If I saw two objects in front of me, could I tell quickly which object was a shadowlands object, and which was a skinlands object?<br /> <br /> Can I tell the difference between an object made out of plasm, or whether it is a relic, artifact, or something else by looking at it?<br /> <br /> I hate to ask, but how does the Stygian economy work? What are they paying all these legionnaires to make them do what they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS!<br /> <br /> Actually A lot of these questions I was asking in a sense in a new thread I started, but I posted it before I saw this post of yours froggy.<br /> <br /> As for those last few questions though, Plasm tends to scream a little and the economy is fueled by people soul forged into coin. Who also scream a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T08:13:04-08:00","id":35581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=35503#post35503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the thing that I find challenging is understanding the nature of the shadowlands. For all intents and purposes, the shadowlands is an alien world which shares some of its living space with our own.<br /> <br /> If I were a wraith walking around your typical necropolis, what would I see?<br /> <br /> Do wraiths often move among the quick, or do they tend to avoid them?<br /> <br /> Would I see a lot of shadowlands buildings crammed in between skinlands ones?<br /> <br /> What happens when one of the quick takes a stroll through an area where a wraith has built a building? Does the quick just pass through the building, or does he crash through the wall?<br /> <br /> If I saw two objects in front of me, could I tell quickly which object was a shadowlands object, and which was a skinlands object?<br /> <br /> Can I tell the difference between an object made out of plasm, or whether it is a relic, artifact, or something else by looking at it?<br /> <br /> I hate to ask, but how does the Stygian economy work? What are they paying all these legionnaires to make them do what they do?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=35461#post35461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A general question for you:<br /> <br /> How do you view Orpheus as you're working on Wr20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah these questions I'd like to hear answers for as well. Especially Orpheus to be honest. I love Orpheus as just about as much as WtO and I've been trying to get a game of it started for years, partly because it's a little less intimidating than WtO and I know if I can get them interesting in Orpheus I can get them into WtO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T08:57:50-08:00","id":35608,"title":"","content":"No questions, just very, <b>very</b>, <i><b>VERY </b></i>happy to see Rich Dansky back for Wraith. In my opinion, there is no Warith without him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T10:08:40-08:00","id":35645,"title":"","content":"Yay, Wraith!<br /> <br /> <br /> While I think Wraith <i>should</i> be depressing and the setting should be grim, it needs to be more accessible. I'm pretty new to Wraith; I only grabbed the corebook a few weeks ago and that was mostly because I'm trying to write a fanbook for VtM Necromancy. It's a great book, and I <i>love</i> the art! But the setting is hard to get involved in.<br /> <br /> Why? Well, there are no splats, for one, and that's something that gives every other game an immediate organizational plan. Wraith hasn't got that. It has Legions, which apparently all Wraiths are in but not all of them care about? So how do you differentiate between &quot;real&quot; Legionnaires and everyone else that's just busy doing their thing? The Guilds don't exist anymore, except they totally do, but only some of them and only kinda? How is that possibly something you can sell people on?<br /> <br /> The basic idea is cool. You're a wraith, and that's it. There's no possibility of new people &quot;Oh, I wanna be a Gangrel!&quot; and stopping there. They have to make a full-fledged person, because there's no splat to take over the concept. Cool! Except.. there's also no splat to provide any guidance. There's these two things, Legions and Guilds, that could work, but don't. The setting is fighting itself. I'd like to see the Hierarchy be primarily a plot device. Legion membership optional for PCs, and have it <i>mean something</i>. It means they have jobs, duties and responsibilities. They joined the army, after all. But there needs to be civilian jobs and careers: the Guilds. The game already treats the Guilds as its splats. There are Guildbooks, after all, but not Legionbooks. Just GO with that!<br /> <br /> Please, please make the changes that Wraith needs to be accessible, easy to play and still keep its original themes and moods. Don't stick with the WW baggage of &quot;NEVER RETCON ANYTHING EVER&quot;. Don't say that the Guilds reformed in 2001 or whatever. Just CHANGE the setting so that the Guilds EXIST. Or CHANGE the setting so that whatever other awesome idea you have works. Don't try to avoid retcons <i>when they make your game better</i>. WW did that for years. Rather than dump something stupid, like the Thulsa-Doom-Setites, they tried to come up with a way to incorporate Thulsa Doom into actual Egyptian mythology. Instead of saying &quot;Maybe a Clan that's eeeeevil for eeeeeevil is a bad idea&quot; they tried to transition &quot;eeeeevil&quot; into a form of anarchy.<br /> <br /> Argh. It was such a mess! Please don't make those mistakes. If there is something that doesn't work about Wraith, then <i>just change it</i>. Don't try to explain in character how the new, working solution <i>evolved</i> from the old, non-working problem. That's dumb. Just FIX the problem, and either pretend the old way never existed or flat out <i>say it never was that way</i>. Your real-world decision to change Broken Mechanic 3 does not need an in-character justification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T10:49:29-08:00","id":35665,"title":"","content":"Telgar: There is a Legion book. It's called Book of Legions. Maybe you mean it needs a bigger book? Other than that I agree with everything else you've said. Especially about Retconning. Since Wraith didn't get the Revised treatment, I don't think it had the chance to evolve the way the other previous systems did, for better or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:18:47-08:00","id":35971,"title":"","content":"A comment of the way things are: Wraith is a spectacular game, and is uniquely designed to tell fascinatingly powerful stories of the PCs personal struggles. The constant turmoil with the Shadow, the fixation on Passions and Fetters, and the general sense of unfinished business let characters shine. However, WtO has the bulk of its text dedicated to Shadowlands society; the structure and conflict of the Hierarchy, various Renegades and Heretics, and the forces of Oblivion. You get this funny contrast where the star of the game is personal stories and the things people have left behind in the Skinlands, but the bulk of the written material (and with it, many games) is instead focused on this sort of large-scale other world that Wraiths inhabit.<br /> <br /> I adore Wraith's setting, but more love given to those small, painful, personal stories would be great. I want less &quot;stoic Doomslayers throwing themselves at hordes of Spectres&quot; and &quot;Stygian politics&quot; and more direction given towards how a recently-dead (the average PC) Wraith deals with the people and places they've left behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:33:55-08:00","id":36015,"title":"","content":"Mr. Dansky, I write as a long-time Wraith fan.<br /> <br /> 1. Where is the Wr20 project in terms of decisions? Have important decisions already been made about things like the 6th Maelstrom, Charon, etc.?<br /> <br /> 2. Please speak to the differences between Wr20 and the Wraith 2nd edition book.<br /> <br /> 3. Can wraiths and specters twerk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:35:57-08:00","id":36017,"title":"","content":"Some quick hits before I get dragged back into the word mines (longer answers soon, I promise)<br /> <br /> 1-I love me some Orpheus. Lucien Soulban and I go way, way back, and I really enjoy his work. It was a pleasure and an honor to contribute to the first Orpheus book, and I think there's a lot that's really great in the game. I'm certainly not going to ignore it when it comes time to have the rubber hit the road on Wraith 20; that being said, the focus of Wraith is going to be - big shock reveal here - Wraith. <br /> <br /> 2-Favorite Guild that didn't get a book? Probably Solicitors, because I had all sorts of deeply wicked stuff planned for them back in the day that never saw the light of day. <br /> <br /> 3-General work philosophy: Folks, I love Wraith. I am thrilled beyond words to be getting the chance to engage with it - and with you - again, and to take on the challenge of some of my own artistic Fetters. And I want Wraith to be the best game it can possibly be, which means fixing mistakes and potentially making changes to make the game a cleaner play experience. That doesn't mean the game is going to suddenly become more pastel than My Little Pony, and it doesn't mean that wholesale sweeping changes are coming for change's sake. It means exactly what I said, which is that I want Wraith to be the best game it can be - and not for it to be turned into something else that ain't Wraith. If that means rethinking Shadowguiding rules /and/ storytelling guidance to make sure players get more enjoyment out of that aspect of the game - and don't immediately start trying to flush each others' characters down the nearest nihil - that's the sort of positive change that improves the game without changing its essence. That's what I'm looking to do, and as I told Rich T., I've spent 14 years thinking about this. I know that not everyone is going to be absolutely ecstatic with absolutely every tweak that's made, and not every concern is going to get addressed, because that's the nature of the beast (and The Beast, for all of you Wraith-l folk still out there). But please trust me when I say that every change and decision is going to be carefully thought through, and that the only intention is make Wraith 20th magnificent.<br /> <br /> 4-Twerking is a tool of Oblivion. <br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:59:56-08:00","id":36119,"title":"","content":"First off, I cannot express the joy I felt the moment I first read that Wraith 20th is a happening thing... And then have to exceed that joy the moment I read that The Deadguy was gonna be involved in it once more. Here are my thoughts for this latest project...<br /> <br /> 1) Present all the Guildbooks as mini-Guildbooks and attempt to cram as much detail on the individual Guilds as possible. Cuz, who knows if/when the opportunity will arise to fill these out?<br /> <br /> 2) One big critique about Wraith I remember is in mixed parties that exist primarily in the Skinlands, the Wraith PCs tend to be the ones with the biggest disadvantages. Maybe make those Arcanoi that deal the heaviest with the Skinlands somehow the most accessible to use.<br /> <br /> 3) Clarify the layers of Underworld existence (ie., Tempest, Shadowlands, Stygia, Far SHores, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1738-charon","name":"Charon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:34:50-08:00","id":36153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=35370#post35370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon Cat:<br /> Have you been listening in on the phone calls I've been having with Rich Thomas? Just curious :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I clearly have no idea what you are talking about, am in no way affiliated with the NSA <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:42:17-08:00","id":36158,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms: I believe you've asked this question of Rich before in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:43:19-08:00","id":36159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=35503#post35503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the thing that I find challenging is understanding the nature of the shadowlands. For all intents and purposes, the shadowlands is an alien world which shares some of its living space with our own.<br /> <br /> If I were a wraith walking around your typical necropolis, what would I see?<br /> <br /> Do wraiths often move among the quick, or do they tend to avoid them?<br /> <br /> Would I see a lot of shadowlands buildings crammed in between skinlands ones?<br /> <br /> What happens when one of the quick takes a stroll through an area where a wraith has built a building? Does the quick just pass through the building, or does he crash through the wall?</div> </div> </div> </div> Let's see if I can help...<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands overlays (underlays?) the Skinlands - the physical world. Each necropolis is different, like each mortal city is different. <i>Ends of Empire</i> has a good example with London(?) and of course <i>Necropolis: Atlanta</i> has... Atlanta. As for moving among the Quick, well, depends on how heavily populated by the living the area is. Structures in the Shadowlands are a reflection of the Skinlands, and act... strangely. A derelict warehouse where addicts used drugs and overdosed that was demolished to make room for a new skyscraper might look like that dilapidated warehouse for the first few floors, then be modern steel and glass after that. Wraithly structures are often built away from high traffic, as the concentration of ghostly energy usually lowers the Shroud in the area - giving it the rumor of being &quot;haunted.&quot; Most living that pass through a building in the Shadowlands feel the same kind of chill that they do when passing through a &quot;haunted&quot; spot.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I saw two objects in front of me, could I tell quickly which object was a shadowlands object, and which was a skinlands object?<br /> <br /> Can I tell the difference between an object made out of plasm, or whether it is a relic, artifact, or something else by looking at it?<br /> <br /> I hate to ask, but how does the Stygian economy work? What are they paying all these legionnaires to make them do what they do? </div> </div> </div> Are you a wraith? Wraiths can tell the difference between Skinlands and Shadowlands objects - things in the Shadowlands appear slightly more &quot;real&quot; while Skinlands objects usually have a bit of fuzz or haze around them. As for detailing the means of an object's creation... Soulsteel looks and feels different than most things. Divining whether it is an Artifact, Relic, or something else (I believe) requires Arcanos. And as for what they are paying the Legionnaires, well... coin. Soulsteel coin, <i>oboli</i>, along with weapons, armor, and lodgings.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:44:27-08:00","id":36160,"title":"","content":"i think it would be easier if the W20 had a map or an exemplification of a map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:57:31-08:00","id":36169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36160#post36160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think it would be easier if the W20 had a map or an exemplification of a map.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though hopefully Much better than the Umbra Map. &gt;.&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T23:17:10-08:00","id":36176,"title":"","content":"theres an umbra map? Link :P<br /> <br /> i keep imagining the Underworld/shadowlands like layers uppon layers, Similar to the Hell acording to Dante but not directly intertwined<br /> <br /> (pardon my bad english, not my first language)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T00:01:37-08:00","id":36205,"title":"","content":"As far as I know things...<br /> <br /> Skinlands<br /> Shroud<br /> Shadowlands<br /> Tempest (with Stygia and the Far Shores floating about in bubbles of calm)<br /> Labyrinth<br /> Oblivion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T00:08:52-08:00","id":36208,"title":"","content":"You're right, Crowley - it's layered. The Skinlands and the Shadowlands inhabit almost the same &quot;space&quot; - layered over each other. Byways connect the Shadowlands to Stygia. Stygia and the other Dark Kingdoms (and Far Shores) sit upon an ocean. That ocean is the Tempest. Below that is the Labyrinth, and below <i>that</i> is Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Imagine you're in a city - any city, your city. Then you die. Now you're in the Shadowlands - a dark, gloomy reflection of your city. From there you take a highway out of town, a highway you've never seen before, even though you've lived in the city your entire life. This highway takes you to strange and confusing places, all kinds of weirdness, until you arrive at Stygia. You've just traveled a byway (and made it safely - lucky you!). From there you take a ship made from the fingernails of hanged men, and sail across the ocean. But you're hit by a sudden storm of kitchen utensils, tears of widows, and cat skulls! Your ship capsizes and you tumble into the ocean! Rather than drown, you pass through a summer's day as a little girl buries her beloved dog, which morphs into the scene of a boy packing a teddy bear into a bag as he runs away from home. Then, cold, sharp, and inky black fingers grab you and pull you further down - the memories fade and the edges of your vision constrict. Around you a frenzied, cackling monsters. You're in the Labyrinth, the Spectres have you. They haul you through twisting, dark chambers, corridors that weep blood and refuse to even admit the laws of physics exist. Finally, everything goes cold - no, not cold. <i>Numb</i>. You can't feel anything. And you can't bring yourself to care that you can't, because in front of you is not <i>blackness</i> - no, blackness would mean that there's something there. In front of you is <i>nothing</i>, the absence of anything. You brain breaks, and you giggle to yourself. <i>Ultrablack</i>, you think. <i>The color you see right before you're unmade. </i>And faintly, you can sense something coming out of that hole, a single desire. Hunger. Unending, all-consuming <i>hunger</i>.<br /> <br /> And then the mortwrights throw you in.<br /> <br /> That's Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:02:01-08:00","id":36226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36159#post36159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let's see if I can help...<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands overlays (underlays?) the Skinlands - the physical world. Each necropolis is different, like each mortal city is different. <i>Ends of Empire</i> has a good example with London(?) and of course <i>Necropolis: Atlanta</i> has... Atlanta. As for moving among the Quick, well, depends on how heavily populated by the living the area is. Structures in the Shadowlands are a reflection of the Skinlands, and act... strangely. A derelict warehouse where addicts used drugs and overdosed that was demolished to make room for a new skyscraper might look like that dilapidated warehouse for the first few floors, then be modern steel and glass after that. Wraithly structures are often built away from high traffic, as the concentration of ghostly energy usually lowers the Shroud in the area - giving it the rumor of being &quot;haunted.&quot; Most living that pass through a building in the Shadowlands feel the same kind of chill that they do when passing through a &quot;haunted&quot; spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually just picked up the Necropolis: Atlanta book today while it was on sale and I am working through it. Hopefully I have some new insights when I finish. (also Midnight Express because: trains.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36159#post36159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you a wraith? Wraiths can tell the difference between Skinlands and Shadowlands objects - things in the Shadowlands appear slightly more &quot;real&quot; while Skinlands objects usually have a bit of fuzz or haze around them. As for detailing the means of an object's creation... Soulsteel looks and feels different than most things. Divining whether it is an Artifact, Relic, or something else (I believe) requires Arcanos. And as for what they are paying the Legionnaires, well... coin. Soulsteel coin, <i>oboli</i>, along with weapons, armor, and lodgings.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>My question here is mostly for being a storyteller. If I describe something, I need to be able to convey easily what kind of thing it is with a minimum of confusion or fuss... Saying shadowlands objects are more &quot;real&quot; isn't that helpful, and judging from some Wraith artwork (I am thinking specifically of the comic in the 2nd edition core book) I am thinking describing them as fuzzy or hazy isn't quite right? I mean, that house they entered looked pretty solid to me. Maybe in Wr20 this could be helped with some full color art rather than being strictly monochromatic, and some special consideration toward describing the environment. Oddly enough I have less of a problem with the Tempest and the Labyrinth than I do with the Shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T08:07:00-08:00","id":36376,"title":"","content":"Anything new with the Sixth Maelstrom?<br /> Will Wraith The Great War get an update if the Kickstarter succeeds?<br /> One thing I never got with the Arcanoi (then again I might be reading it wrong. How come the 1 dot abilities for moving around in the Skinlands are better than the 4-5 dot abilities for dicking around with stuff in the Skinlands?<br /> If your a real dead guy, when did you die?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":". 12-24-2013, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:04:47-08:00","id":36462,"title":"","content":"Hello RealDeadguy,<br /> <br /> 1. Myself and my group love the Wraith setting. You did an amazing job with 2nd ed and it is hands down my fav WOD setting. We played a bit back when it was originally released and I have been running a game for the past few months. Amazing experience and awesome setting (I converted it to the NWOD from the 2nd ed and our party is in Paris during the Great War era). I think one of the most interesting dynamics of a longer wraith campaign is the development of the shadow over time. Its easy enough to route its experience to non-offensive areas during the first few games, but once the xp begins to stack up, the shadow begins to become a force to be reckoned with (which is not a bad thing). Did you experience this same phenomena during your campaign(s)?<br /> <br /> 2. Will we see more on the Dark Kingdom of Ivory? I think Jade is pretty well covered and the rest are pretty workable with the material from the players guide.<br /> <br /> 3. Only real mechanical request would be consolidation of some of the rules for things like how wraiths heal and maybe additional guidance on things like the relative power levels of relics to artifacts in relation to the backgrounds needed to buy them. Minor nips and tucks really. Consolidating the relics/artifacts from 1st ed and the book of buried secrets into W20 would be great to.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the amazing world. Its been a lot of fun this far with plenty more to come.<br /> <br /> Regards,<br /> <br /> Aeoris","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:05:21-08:00","id":36463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36226#post36226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question here is mostly for being a storyteller. If I describe something, I need to be able to convey easily what kind of thing it is with a minimum of confusion or fuss... Saying shadowlands objects are more &quot;real&quot; isn't that helpful, and judging from some Wraith artwork (I am thinking specifically of the comic in the 2nd edition core book) I am thinking describing them as fuzzy or hazy isn't quite right? I mean, that house they entered looked pretty solid to me. Maybe in Wr20 this could be helped with some full color art rather than being strictly monochromatic, and some special consideration toward describing the environment. Oddly enough I have less of a problem with the Tempest and the Labyrinth than I do with the Shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it like this: There's a piece of super-fine, dark grey gauze. For wraiths, objects in the Shadowlands are in front of the gauze, while objects in the Skinlands are behind it. Or if you're a tech guy, Shadowlands objects are in 1080p, while Skinlands objects are upscaled to 720p (and everything's native format is 480p). Shadowlands items are more &quot;real&quot; because they're more solidly anchored in the wraiths' plane of existence, where Skinlands items are almost holographicly layered over it. The wraith's Lifesight and Deathsight affect everything and allow them to intuitively know the difference (I believe that the -sights do not work on Shadowlands objects, if I'm remembering the book correctly). Deathsight especially, as it touches all Skinlands objects with a bit of decay.<br /> <br /> Huh. It just hit me. Shadowlands objects don't decay. Skinland ones do, and are always decaying due to a wraiths' Deathsight. There's your descriptor. (My games always take place in decaying, run-down cities. Maybe that's why I forgot that tidbit.)<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T12:25:10-08:00","id":36502,"title":"","content":"Greetings Mr. Dansky,<br /> <br /> questions, questions...ah...questions!<br /> <br /> 1.) Can we get a commemorative Samuel Haight ashtray of our favorite Marty Stu as he exists in The Shadowlands? Failing that, maybe a piece of nice artwork showing Mr. Now-Soul-Forged as an ashtray and maybe a quick writeup of how the encounter went down (I know, I know...we know he got the crap kicked out of him, but the devil's in the details!)<br /> <br /> 2.) Can we get an update on The Lady of Fate/Eve and how she has handled things since her son, apparently, has not resolved his issues with his descendants? How about her perspectives on the Fallen and their relation to Grandma (of <i>Orpheus</i>) and The Well of the Void? How about her perspectives on her husband's first wife, Lilith? Or maybe her opinions on Lucifer? How about the original Charon, the Halaku, whom the wraith was named for and what became of his people (were they, in fact, the basis for The Never-born Malfeans)?<br /> <br /> 3.) What about our favorite leg breaker and <i>Shadow Guide/Hunter: The Reckoning/Mummy: the Resurrection</i> risen spectre Maxwell Carpenter? Any perspectives on him still running around the Skinlands, doing whatever evil stuff he could do?<br /> <br /> 4.) Any more goodies to share with us from the never-published side of <i>Wraith</i>? More guild information? New <i>Risen</i> stuff? Any <i>Wraith: The Great War</i> stuff lying about (which, btw, was my favorite of the historical settings. I studied US Military History in college and even managed to take an upper level history course specifically on The Great War).<br /> <br /> Now, to a few observations.<br /> <br /> 1.) The Shadow Guide mechanic needs to be rethought. From a personal perspective, I believe that was the single hardest aspect of the game for players to overcome. Maybe an alternate system can be put in place for it to be handled by The Storyteller? While it puts more strain on an ST, it would be more fair, generally speaking, than having a player do it.<br /> <br /> 2.) Some thoughts on how to have Wraith players interact with regular Skinlands types more easily than resorting to Risen status? I say this because I'm among those that actually played in real honest-to-Zod crossover games. I would have loved to play a Wraith...but it was too much of a pain in the keister to do so.<br /> <br /> I think that'll do for now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T14:12:33-08:00","id":36549,"title":"","content":"ok, silly question (as i read the manual)<br /> So..all the rivers and seas are in the middle of a storm, this one being the tempest, and if a character falls into its waters he is dragged onto the laberyth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T16:28:03-08:00","id":36618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craftmason Bob's Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36502#post36502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings Mr. Dansky,<br /> <br /> questions, questions...ah...questions!<br /> <br /> 1.) Can we get a commemorative Samuel Haight ashtray of our favorite Marty Stu as he exists in The Shadowlands? Failing that, maybe a piece of nice artwork showing Mr. Now-Soul-Forged as an ashtray and maybe a quick writeup of how the encounter went down (I know, I know...we know he got the crap kicked out of him, but the devil's in the details!)<br /> <br /> 2.) Can we get an update on The Lady of Fate/Eve and how she has handled things since her son, apparently, has not resolved his issues with his descendants? How about her perspectives on the Fallen and their relation to Grandma (of <i>Orpheus</i>) and The Well of the Void? How about her perspectives on her husband's first wife, Lilith? Or maybe her opinions on Lucifer? How about the original Charon, the Halaku, whom the wraith was named for and what became of his people (were they, in fact, the basis for The Never-born Malfeans)?<br /> <br /> 3.) What about our favorite leg breaker and <i>Shadow Guide/Hunter: The Reckoning/Mummy: the Resurrection</i> risen spectre Maxwell Carpenter? Any perspectives on him still running around the Skinlands, doing whatever evil stuff he could do?<br /> <br /> 4.) Any more goodies to share with us from the never-published side of <i>Wraith</i>? More guild information? New <i>Risen</i> stuff? Any <i>Wraith: The Great War</i> stuff lying about (which, btw, was my favorite of the historical settings. I studied US Military History in college and even managed to take an upper level history course specifically on The Great War).<br /> <br /> Now, to a few observations.<br /> <br /> 1.) The Shadow Guide mechanic needs to be rethought. From a personal perspective, I believe that was the single hardest aspect of the game for players to overcome. Maybe an alternate system can be put in place for it to be handled by The Storyteller? While it puts more strain on an ST, it would be more fair, generally speaking, than having a player do it.<br /> <br /> 2.) Some thoughts on how to have Wraith players interact with regular Skinlands types more easily than resorting to Risen status? I say this because I'm among those that actually played in real honest-to-Zod crossover games. I would have loved to play a Wraith...but it was too much of a pain in the keister to do so.<br /> <br /> I think that'll do for now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Getting rid of the Shadowguide will ruin it. Might as well not be Wraith, then.<br /> <br /> <br /> Question of my own: Will rules for the Risen be in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1800-randaconda","name":"Randaconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T20:45:15-08:00","id":36725,"title":"","content":"ok, quick and very blunt question.<br /> <br /> Acording to you Deadguy, i know you wont give us a straight answer but i would like an explanation perhaps or your perspective..<br /> A ) How does te Grandmother affects on Wraith<br /> B ) is She, God?<br /> C ) How do you think God would fit on the entire plot of Wraith, is She dead and a ghost? Is she a villian or just a force that felt into the Oblivion ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T21:58:01-08:00","id":36771,"title":"","content":"Random answers while I wait for Santa (and, coincidentally, turn up the heat in the fireplace...)<br /> <br /> 1-We're still early days on a lot of continuity issues, including critters like Grandmother. I'm fairly certain she's not God; for all that Wraith skirts the edges of multiple creation myths, having an all-powerful being lurking in the background who isn't Rich Thomas potentially mucks with player agency in ways I'm not sure I like. On the other hand, you can look at the covenant Adonai made with Noah, think about the Great Maelstroms, and draw some interesting conclusions, if you're so inclined. <br /> Regardless, I'll keep you posted. <br /> 2-Never say never when it comes to Carpenter. About anything. <br /> 3-Rest assured, there will be nods to old favorites like Sam and Sock Girl. You just may have to look carefully in some cases...<br /> 4-I will be cracking open the door on Ye Olde Tales Of Wraithe 2nde Development as things progress, and that includes a few notes on things that never made it to the printed page. There are not, I'm afraid, vast piles of unpublished Official Manuscripts, but there were plans for some titles that never happened, and I'll be happy to share those stories and intentions.<br /> 5-Aeoris, the Shadow getting more powerful as things went along was pretty much exactly what I was going for with the design there. It seemed to make more thematic sense - and provided a more interesting balancing issue - if the Shadow grew in proportion with the rest of a wraith. They are, after all, parts of the same whole.<br /> 6-No promises, but I have always loved the other Dark Kingdoms material, and I would like to do more with it. Now, if folks would just give The Sea That Knows No Sun some love, I'd be all kinds of happy :-)<br /> 7-PaladinDemo - Haven't actually died, though I did stick my hands in a vat of liquid nitrogen once. Does that count?<br /> 8-Please keep the notes on what you liked/didn't like coming. That's tremendously helpful, and I very much appreciate it.<br /> 9-If you go under in the Tempest, you're going down. Most wraiths, for the record, are not so good with the swimming thing.<br /> <br /> Wishing a Merry Christmas and a happy Yule to those who celebrate such. May the ghosts of Christmas past, present and future go bother that Scrooge guy tonight, and leave you in peace with your loved ones.<br /> <br /> \u200bDeadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T02:28:51-08:00","id":36842,"title":"","content":"Here's a real question: how the hell did you guys make the Player's Guide to the Shadow<i> so damn good?</i> It goes in my 'top 3 RPG books of all time,' and that's not an easy spot to get into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T03:13:24-08:00","id":36852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36771#post36771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wishing a Merry Christmas and a happy Yule to those who celebrate such. May the ghosts of Christmas past, present and future go bother that Scrooge guy tonight, and leave you in peace with your loved ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relevant video:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T13:22:29-08:00","id":37979,"title":"","content":"The Shadowplayer's Guide was the result of a lot of hard work from a great and focused writing team, a wonderful layout job, roughly 300 cans of DIet Coke, some 48 hour long development jags, some fantastic art from a group of freelancers who took the time to really get the material, a bottle of Tomatin 12 year single malt scotch, one incident where I nearly set my office desk on fire, and a lengthy debate over the color the Shadow dialog text on the back cover should be. Among other things. Deadguy out (in the fields of Missouri)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T13:51:45-08:00","id":37995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=37979#post37979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadowplayer's Guide was the result of a lot of hard work from a great and focused writing team, a wonderful layout job, roughly 300 cans of DIet Coke, some 48 hour long development jags, some fantastic art from a group of freelancers who took the time to really get the material, a bottle of Tomatin 12 year single malt scotch, one incident where I nearly set my office desk on fire, and a lengthy debate over the color the Shadow dialog text on the back cover should be. Among other things. Deadguy out (in the fields of Missouri)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you wretched tease! That will do for now. Thank you so much for answering!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T13:55:10-08:00","id":37996,"title":"","content":"Hello Rich,<br /> <br /> Long time Wraith fan. I started in 1996. Helped me work through a lot of personal issues about my own emotional issues during being a teenager. So simply, thank you for that. The game will always be vastly important to me and is why I own a physical copy of nearly every Wraith book printed (a couple city books and Quick and the Dead slipped my grasp). <br /> <br /> My favorite book, was Midnight Express (next to Shoah...cause...whoa man. I just don't count black dog books with the main lines). I loved how it showed how to do a cinematic style of game which is what lead me to the bag of ideas I've lugged around for 17 years for games of a more ethereal quality. <br /> <br /> I love anything about the Tempest and the Labyrinth as wild teeming lands. I added that in some areas they bleed into The Dreaming or the various Umbral layers, etc. This allowed for me to tell stories which brought multiple supernaturals into contact, forcing them to come to terms with co-existence.<br /> <br /> My least Favorite bit was how mature shadow guiding needs people to be. Eventually, the few times I convinced people to let me run, I ended up running all shadows. It was hard at first but eventually I got a hang for it.<br /> <br /> I am most fascinated by how Wraith relates to other settings (Euthantos, Giovanni, etc) and how the wraith setting could continue forward post Time of Judgement. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now that I have fawned over you and Wraith, time for a few questions:<br /> 1) What is your favorite Ghost Story?<br /> 2) When developing the Shadow Players Guide (if I remember correctly) how hard was it with the Creole Arcanoi to avoid the topics of Zombism so much? <br /> 3) Would you consider in Wraith20 including Zombism and/or Risen in the core book (ala W20 having Changing Breeds) or even expanding to wraiths of the various kingdoms or even spectres?<br /> 4) Is there going to be a KS reward that would possibly include the backer getting involved with some of the design or is the plan to have the book largely written by the KS? (planning on throwing stupid money at this so always good to plan ahead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> 5) Monitors seemed like perhaps they might have been the biggest bad of the Guilds due to Lifeweb. Were they intended this way from early on?<br /> 6) In your mind, how much interaction would a standard vanilla wraith game have with the Skinlands? I know there is variation but I like to know what was default during conception.<br /> 7) How did you feel when Wraith was ended? Was is conflicted? Did you agree but regret? etc. I don't mean to open old wounds but it seemed so sudden to me (I was young and not as forward thinking at the time so there were likely signs) that I am curious if it was a surprise. I remember the forward to End of Empires feeling like it was trying to be put into words. Thank you for trying to do as much as was done with that book. It did make me feel that even thought my favorite was being put down, that I was not thought less of by the team working on it for liking it.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:57:39-08:00","id":38111,"title":"","content":"two things<br /> One, please. i beg you , check your private messages<br /> Second: i know this is stupid but...after a couple of beers with some friends, Would Pirates of The Caribean (The First one) be a good example of a risen trying to resolve a fatter or conduit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T20:12:18-08:00","id":38140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=38111#post38111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">two things<br /> One, please. i beg you , check your private messages<br /> Second: i know this is stupid but...after a couple of beers with some friends, Would Pirates of The Caribbean (The First one) be a good example of a risen trying to resolve a fetter or conduit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed.<br /> <br /> Also what's a conduit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T20:18:45-08:00","id":38144,"title":"","content":"i belive its like the fetter but for risen's only","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T21:49:36-08:00","id":38159,"title":"","content":"Basically a conduit is a special fetter created during the creation of a Risen. It is usually one of the wraith's already existing fetters and during the Risen creation process the wraith's Shadow enters the fetter, though it is possible for Psyche to forced in the conduit instead giving the Shadow the Risen's body*. The conduit serves a connection between the worlds of the living and the dead and the Risen needs to come in physical contact with on a regular basis or else its body will start rotting away. If it's destroyed will guarantee the end of that Risen and that will not return but not right away as their body will rot away over the course of hours before finally ceasing to function. But if the Risen's body is destroyed without the destruction of the conduit, the item retains its power and are desired by necromancers and others with similar powers/connections to the restless dead.<br /> <br /> *Though as much as the Shadow would like to destroy the Conduit and Psyche with it while it's in the body it cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T08:38:40-08:00","id":38297,"title":"","content":"More minions Rich?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T11:02:26-08:00","id":38347,"title":"","content":"Hello RealDeadguy,<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> 1. How much influence do you envision Stygia having over Africa (Egypt in particular)? I assumed that Alexandria would be a kind of Stygian outpost similar to the way New Orleans is to the Ivory Kingdom (solely because Stygia has the Library of Alexandria). How much (if any) of Africa is controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Iron?<br /> <br /> 2. How do you represent the power of the mightier servants of oblivion in game? In the fluff of the ancients (Sea of Shadows i believe), it implied that some of the mightier servants of oblivion would be akin to a Methuselah from vampire. Did you have a way of scaling/representing their power? I understand that a true malfean is basically beyond the ability of any group to destroy without some epic gaming, but what about some of their more potent nephwracks (sp)?<br /> <br /> My game is set in the NWOD so i've basically been using a combo of the blood potency system from Vampire the Requiem and synergy from Geist to represent the power of gaunts and other ancient wraiths.<br /> <br /> 3. Are there any special rules for dark steel weapons and armor? We see a little color on them in Orpheus, and I assumed that they would basically follow the same rules for which weapon breaks the other as true jade v soul jade. Will we see dark steel given additional rules or will it basically be an aggravated damage version of a standard weapon?<br /> <br /> Things to add to the game:<br /> 1. Rule consolodation: It would be great to see some of the rules consolidated for things like healing (aggravated damage in particular), travel in the tempest (Wraith the Great War, Sea of Shadows, etc..), lists of arcanoi will all of their ancient/modern arts in one place. <br /> <br /> 2. More sample specters/specter powers to pick from.<br /> <br /> 3. Ceremonies/rituals to augment the wraithly arsenal of powers.<br /> <br /> 4. More color on the symbols of the hierarchy and its ranks of office...mmmmm....bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> 5. A starter adventure/sample setting in the main book.<br /> <br /> 6. More information on prominent necropoli around the world (ex...the Great War). <br /> <br /> Regards and thanks for the wonderful game. We are actually going to play a game this evening.<br /> <br /> Aeoris<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T08:24:39-08:00","id":38743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=37979#post37979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among other things. Deadguy out (in the fields of Missouri)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you think December was a good month to drop Missouri's Fog rating? Seriously, there was many a Willpower roll.<br /> Also, something I asked during one of those Foggy nights. What is the Skinland weaknesses for Wraiths? Stygian steel and Soulfire is used in the Shadowlands, one wonders what we use against Wraiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T01:58:56-08:00","id":39251,"title":"","content":"Is there a universal language of the dead? Wraith: The Great War mentions it, but I don't see this anywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T04:29:35-08:00","id":39308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=38743#post38743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What is the Skinland weaknesses for Wraiths? Stygian steel and Soulfire is used in the Shadowlands, one wonders what we use against Wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div> Historically and culturally a combination of salt and/or holy water with some sort of prayer is supposed to do the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T08:02:06-08:00","id":39388,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=39251#post39251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a universal language of the dead? Wraith: The Great War mentions it, but I don't see this anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buried Secrets, 27<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe language of death is universal. All of the wraiths from a particular paradigm can converse, while their Linguistics ratings determines how well they can understand the languages of the Skinlands.\u201d</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:01:08-08:00","id":39923,"title":"","content":"Hey folks - sorry for the radio silence of late. I'm out at my wife's family farm for the holidays, which has me mildly distracted :-) i'll be a little more active once we get back home. Here's wishing all of you a very happy New Year! Deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T19:16:26-08:00","id":42634,"title":"","content":"hey deadguy, i been looking for some inspiration as for stygia and other things (like the harrowing) and i got in a discussion (SPOILERS AHEAD) could the entire movie of &quot;Jacob's Ladder&quot; be concidered a Harrowing<br /> <br /> and what pieces of fiction, movies/comics/novels/tv shows could you recomend for a newcommer in wraith and what was your inspiration for stygia and the underworld","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T06:04:59-08:00","id":44108,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to drop by and say it's great to see you on board Mr Dansky.<br /> I was wondering if we will see alternate Arcanoi powers present in Wr20? Such as those featured in the Great War, or would such abilities have fallen out of use in the modern era?<br /> <br /> Also, guys, you heard it from the horses mouth:<br /> <br /> Grandmother = Rich Thomas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Years of speculation are over!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T15:40:23-08:00","id":44486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=42634#post42634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey deadguy, i been looking for some inspiration as for stygia and other things (like the harrowing) and i got in a discussion (SPOILERS AHEAD) could the entire movie of &quot;Jacob's Ladder&quot; be concidered a Harrowing<br /> <br /> and what pieces of fiction, movies/comics/novels/tv shows could you recomend for a newcommer in wraith and what was your inspiration for stygia and the underworld</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich D answered that last one in another thread of mine titled &quot;What says Wraith to you?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T23:35:56-08:00","id":44731,"title":"","content":"OK, am back in Cackalacky, where it is only cold relative to where I used to live (and where Rich T lives now)<br /> <br /> Answer time: <br /> <br /> Alternate Arcanoi - I'd definitely like to do that, apace permitting. <br /> <br /> Inspirational stuff - thank you, D_R for the pointer on that one. I expect I'm going to do a much fuller unloading of All The Things That Say Wraith In My Office at some point - I've been building a collection of classic horror novels and whatnot since college, so as you might expect, the house is pretty durn Wraithy. The fact that my wife's My Little Pony collection lives in our guest room with all of the ponies arranged so that they are staring right at the pillow of the guest bed, well, that's a whole other issue.<br /> <br /> But. <br /> <br /> Let's start with a few good inspirations for Harrowings.<br /> <br /> Music-wise, I recommend things that are unsettling. My personal taste runs to film soundtracks and the weirder edges of prog and post-prog, so your mileage may vary on these, but here goes nothing:<br /> Van Der Graaf Generator - <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y6V0iFiicuY\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y6V0iFiicuY</a> for a good example of how messed up those guys can get you. I saw this particular show from the 4th row and it was...emotionally disturbing. <br /> Gosta Berlings Saga - <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hTxWTorC5Tg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hTxWTorC5Tg</a><br /> Anglagard - <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NnzxCI9dQkA\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NnzxCI9dQkA</a><br /> Soundtrack - <i>The Serpent and the Rainbow</i> - <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cza26wA59gI\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cza26wA59gI</a><br /> And, oddly enough, &quot;Don't Come Around Here No More&quot;, by Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers, though largely for the video. It's goofy as hell, but it has the nightmare logic of a Harrowing down pat - <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h0JvF9vpqx8\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h0JvF9vpqx8</a><br /> <br /> Televison:<br /> <i>Millennium</i>, still IMHO the greatest creep-fest mindscrew on network television in the last 20 years. The Halloween and &quot;A Room With No View&quot; episodes in particular work well<br /> <i>Twilight Zone</i> and <i>Ray Bradbury Theater</i> episodes, if you can find them - they're all puzzle boxes<br /> <i>American Horror Story: Asylum</i> is probably the best I've seen on TV recently, with some truly striking imagery. (The current season's more fun, but less flat-out freaky)<br /> <i>\u200b</i>Oh, and go back and check out any of the Moffat episodes of <i>Dr. Who </i>he wrote but didn't show-run. <br /> <br /> Movies:<br /> <i>Jacob's Ladder</i> and <i>Altered States</i> are the touchstones here. There are some great sequences in the early <i>Hellraiser</i> films, and <i>Event Horizon</i> (just don't watch the ending. For the love of God, don't watch the ending). Also, if you can find an old British horror film called <i>Paperhouse</i>, which is a kids' film, it has a nice creep/surreality factor to it. <br /> <br /> Fiction:<br /> Start with Ambrose Bierce's short story &quot;Occurrence at Owl Creek Bridge&quot;. Follow that with <i>The Haunting of Hill House</i> and Ligotti's &quot;The Frolic&quot;. Then we'll talk next steps :-)<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out<br /> Because it's 3 in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:34:35-08:00","id":45129,"title":"","content":"As long as there is no My Little Oblivion: Pathos is Magic, I'm good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:55:46-08:00","id":45149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=45129#post45129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as there is no My Little Oblivion: Pathos is Magic, I'm good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely it would be <i>My Little Psyche</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T15:42:51-08:00","id":45192,"title":"","content":"Aren't there horses along the banks of the River of Death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T16:26:36-08:00","id":45210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=45192#post45192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't there horses along the banks of the River of Death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes there are.<br /> <br /> But even they don't have the dead, staring eyes of a classic My Little Pony.<br /> <br /> There are some places even I won't go.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T17:14:06-08:00","id":45234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=45129#post45129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as there is no My Little Oblivion: Pathos is Magic, I'm good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there may not be My Little Oblivion there is <a href=\"http://rhanite.deviantart.com/art/My-Little-Masquerade-Wallpaper-266442136\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T20:59:02-08:00","id":45358,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thank you so much for or your beautiful work on Wraith and for being here and answering posters' questions and taking notes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I thought I would put my two oboli in as well for things that I would like to see in the upcoming W20 and have a few questions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think Aeoris' post contained a lot of what I what I would want too and I have some of the same questions so I'll just second his post.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">What I also would like to see is:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1) The &quot;Official Office of Maelstrom Preparedness Handbook&quot; (simply because it would be fun and very cool)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2) The symbol of Stygia that is mentioned, but we don't know what it looks like. (Even a very cool stylized) &quot;S&quot; would be nice. Also would love symbols for the ranks and various orders in the different legions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3) The inclusion of a version of idea of the &quot;ghost bride/groom&quot; from Chinese belief. I really recommend &quot;The Ghost Bride&quot; by Yangzse Choo for a good ghost read. The majority of the book takes place in the Chinese underworld. Her writing is a bit like Neil Gaiman and is has adventure, intrigue, Chinese mythology, and a slight touch of romance. Her idea for the book was from reading a Malaysian article of the recent decline of Chinese ghost marriages, which she went on to research.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A few thoughts on things others brought up...I know people were asking about the Grandmother and God...I like the fact that Wraith doesn't try to force a particular &quot;spiritual viewpoint&quot; as being absolute, but let's the players work that out for themselves so if someone wants to have a Jewish, Christian, Catholic, Buddhist, Agnostic, Atheist, etc. underworld take, it's up to them, whether it has to do with the existence of Wraiths to the idea of Transcendence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Since Wraith never received the full treatment that had been planned for it, I hope that it will be primarily more Wraith than focused on crossovers with other WOD worlds. It is such a fascinating place, a dark Wonderland, as I mentioned in my post on Why I Love Wraith, so of course, I want more of it! </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Relating to things like Geist or Orpheus. Orpheus itself is a closed storyline so other than that projectors or the Orpheus Group would be around in the past, I see it as touching Wraith but separate from it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As far as \u201cEnds of Empires\u201d gave options for the players to determine how and if things truly end and I know while the \u201cend\u201d was mandated, I am happy that it did give options rather than saying surely the whole underworld was completely destroyed (which of course it would have to have been for the story in Orpheus). Since other Maelstroms\u2019 were survived and rebuilt in the past, I think it much more interesting to think it would be the same. (So don\u2019t want to lose the underworld)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I know I will think of more things.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once again, thank you for being here and for your work!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Happy New Year, Anno Stygia Post Sextium 2014!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Khaleesi</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","user":"Khaleesi","date":". 01-09-2014, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:48:05-08:00","id":45383,"title":"","content":"All I ask is that we get a quote from the wraith of Rich Glumsky.<br /> <br /> (And historical settings as Stretch Goals, but that's a slightly larger demand.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T07:39:17-08:00","id":46247,"title":"","content":"Khaleesi - I would like to think that Stygia is plastered with various public safety warnings and announcements from various cities that have been sacked, bombed, or abandoned over the centuries. &quot;Keep Calm And Stay Dead&quot;, as it were. And thank you for the recommendation!<br /> <br /> Atamajakki - He has no idea that he's dead, which makes that problematic. Of course, Justin and I now work in the same building once again, so there may be an update in Mr. Glumsky's employment status in order.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T08:18:09-08:00","id":46268,"title":"","content":"was watching sci fi channel and something popped into my mind...How do organizations/tv shows like &quot;Ghost Hunters.&quot; and &quot;Haunted Collector.&quot; would affect to the wraiths ?<br /> <br /> Second: Do Wraith have primal urges like the need for food (do they eat?), bathroom, etc... i guess if two wraiths have sex they cant create a new (Never?)born.<br /> Third: i recently saw a movie and i wanted your opinion as for &quot;Watch this movie, its the closest thing to Stygia.<i>&quot; </i>Theres a movie called &quot;What Dreams May Come.&quot; and the entire sequence in which robin william character finds someone who can help him find his wife in hell (from the library to hell) i think it would give a fair description of stygia. What do you think about this depiction? <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HwrmILnrzbk\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HwrmILnrzbk</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3w6FSfMx3bE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3w6FSfMx3bE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3w6FSfMx3bE\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3w6FSfMx3bE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":".  another question 01-10-2014, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T21:11:20-08:00","id":46731,"title":"","content":"Deadguy: mention is made of Redemption for Spectres, but the specifics are very ill-defined and some think it isn't possible at all. <i>Orpheus</i> gives us Orphan-Grinders, who are rather explicitly Redeemed Spectres. What's your stance on the chance for a Spectre to claw his way free from the clutches of Oblivion, and what they become if they pull it off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:34:42-08:00","id":46966,"title":"","content":"The original wraith setting had examples of redeemed specters. The Great War alludes to &quot;mutiles&quot; (sp?) who turned back to the light side (ever earning the mistrust of their fellow specters). p74 of the Doomslayers book also mentions that the Martyr Knights managed to redeem 9. Its not exactly common, but its possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:57:06-08:00","id":46972,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Deadguy,<br /> <br /> Some of the Arcanoi have well-defined markings; inky fingers, odd eye coloration, noticeable patterns on the skin, etc. Others, however, really didn\u2019t have \u201cmarkings\u201d per se, just habits and slight peculiarities. A Harbinger has black eyes, but a Chanteur carries a lute (or whatever) and Spooks look buff. <br /> <br /> Will Wr20 address the mechanics of Arcanoi markings? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:54:34-08:00","id":47700,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy Questions 1. How much influence do you envision Stygia having over Africa (Egypt in particular)? I assumed that Alexandria would be a kind of Stygian outpost similar to the way New Orleans is to the Ivory Kingdom (solely because Stygia has the Library of Alexandria). How much (if any) of Africa is controlled by the Dark Kingdom of Iron? 2. How do you represent the power of the mightier servants of oblivion in game? In the fluff of the ancients (Sea of Shadows i believe), it implied that some of the mightier servants of oblivion would be akin to a Methuselah from vampire. Did you have a way of scaling/representing their power? I understand that a true malfean is basically beyond the ability of any group to destroy without some epic gaming, but what about some of their more potent nephwracks (sp)?My game is set in the NWOD so i've basically been using a combo of the blood potency system from Vampire the Requiem and synergy from Geist to represent the power of gaunts and other ancient wraiths. 3. Are there any special rules for dark steel weapons and armor? We see a little color on them in Orpheus, and I assumed that they would basically follow the same rules for which weapon breaks the other as true jade v soul jade. Will we see dark steel given additional rules or will it basically be an aggravated damage version of a standard weapon? Aeoris","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:03:54-08:00","id":47764,"title":"","content":"Ah, here's a question I'd forgotten to ask: what do the Shadowlands of the Middle East look like? Technically it all fits into the Dark Kingdom of Iron, but is there any particular history of the region? I doubt Persian (and later, Islamic) lands happily gave themselves over to rule by a Roman-European power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:12:02-08:00","id":47768,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> Just a quick question: Can wraiths cry tears since they have no physical body? Would they cry plasm tears?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Best wishes,<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:12:49-08:00","id":47833,"title":"","content":"quick update as for harrowings, (waiting for realdeadman confirmation) would the show Life on mars be an example of a more subtil but contemporany harrowing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:43:31-08:00","id":47860,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeoris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=47700#post47700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026 but what about some of their more potent nephwracks (sp)?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>End of Empires</i> details Coldheart\u2019s stats. Since he\u2019s kinda like the General Kael of the Labyrinth, that might give you a fair idea as to what the stats of a powerful Nephwrack might look like.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:53:44-08:00","id":47867,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khaleesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=47768#post47768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Would they cry plasm tears?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>There is some in-story precedent for Wraiths crying. From some of the subsplat fiction in Doomslayers: <br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI reached the top of the steps with my body aching and tears of plasm streaming from my eyes\u2026\u201c</i> (Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth, 87).</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T22:21:10-08:00","id":47928,"title":"","content":"Will the explosion of paranormal investigator TV shows (<i>Ghost Hunters</i>, <i>Ghost Adventures</i>, <i>Destination Truth</i>, <i>Fact or Faked</i>, and any number of others about psychic mediums) in the past decade be addressed in Wr20? The idea of clueless mortals mucking about inside your Haunt and trying to drive them out without generating more interest is too amusing to pass up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T23:17:19-08:00","id":47964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=47928#post47928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the explosion of paranormal investigator TV shows (<i>Ghost Hunters</i>, <i>Ghost Adventures</i>, <i>Destination Truth</i>, <i>Fact or Faked</i>, and any number of others about psychic mediums) in the past decade be addressed in Wr20? The idea of clueless mortals mucking about inside your Haunt and trying to drive them out without generating more interest is too amusing to pass up.</div> </div> </div> </div>hey that was my question xD<br /> <br /> was thinking about it actually, theres a show called The Haunted Collector. its about a guy who goes to haunted houses, finds out Objects tied down to a ghost and take these items to a &quot;Secure Location in which they wont harm anyone.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T23:43:33-08:00","id":47976,"title":"","content":"I wonder how the average wraith feels when their Fetter ends up on eBay as 'REAL HAUNTED DOLL: very haunted by GHOSTS porcelain 1976 house fire CHEAP&quot; and gets sold to some idiot on the other side of the country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:59:21-08:00","id":48271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=47976#post47976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how the average wraith feels when their Fetter ends up on eBay as 'REAL HAUNTED DOLL: very haunted by GHOSTS porcelain 1976 house fire CHEAP&quot; and gets sold to some idiot on the other side of the country.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres an answer for that one, look for Joe Hill &quot;Heart Shaped Box.&quot; novel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T20:11:02-08:00","id":48673,"title":"","content":"Hello from the aftermath of IllogiCon, here in Cary, NC. Lots of good Wraithy stuff there, especially the late night ghost panel with Gail Z. Martin and Michael G. Williams.<br /> <br /> So, on to questions:<br /> <br /> Wraith and reality TV ghost hunters - There are Haunters who specialize in &quot;dealing&quot; with these folks, some of whom honestly consider Beetlejuice to be an instruction manual. Also, just because they're dead doesn't mean they don't have a sense of humor. Sending the equivalent of the Ghost Facers running in FLIR-lit circles can be all kinds of fun. <br /> <br /> Life on Mars would be a great example of a Harrowing. Good call. (Note: Life on Mars was also inspiration for Driver: San Francisco, which had some, shall we say, dark moments)<br /> <br /> Tears - Yes, they cry plasm tears. A few wraiths weep perpetually, the poor devils. Unless their tears are collected, the plasm is reabsorbed...<br /> <br /> Shadowlands of the Middle East - Can't answer this one here because, well, spoilers.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T09:10:06-08:00","id":49019,"title":"","content":"This talk about tears brings to mind several old discussions I've had. I think it'd be neat to get an official opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> A wraith's clothes are plasm and basically part of her body correct? She pops out of her caul fully dressed in whatever outfit is appropriate. How closely are said clothes to being part of her body? If the hem of her skirt gets stuck in a door, does it hurt? Can she unbotton her shirt or remove her clothes entirely? Can they be removed or altered without her concious awareness or willingness? If they can be removed, what happens to them afterward?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for doing this thread btw, It's a really great opportunity for discussion. I'm really psyched Wraith is coming back, and can I just say quickly, it'd be really great if it afforded the opportunity to finish the guildbook series (or at least Proctor and Chaunter. ;p)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/79-alexisvalarr","name":"alexisvalarr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar79_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:19:43-08:00","id":49544,"title":"","content":"Florence; an ancient city, conquered by Spectres dyring the Great War. The Grim Legion attempted to take it back and suffered heavily for it. Were the Spectres ever driven out, and if so, how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:55:54-08:00","id":49560,"title":"","content":"what if a human collects a fetter?, remember the Haunted Collector show? <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_vrYwS1E_Bw\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_vrYwS1E_Bw</a><br /> <br /> Also, how do wraiths actually loose permanent corpus points and can they recover it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T22:36:17-08:00","id":49574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=49560#post49560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, how do wraiths actually loose permanent corpus points and can they recover it?</div> </div> </div> </div>A wraith who loses all temporary Corpus plunges into a Harrowing with himself as the target. If they fail the Harrowing, they pop back out at a Fetter with one less point of permanent Corpus. This sucks because 