},{"date":"2014-01-16T01:00:01-08:00","id":50514,"title":"","content":"Not sure how much work you did on the Dark Kingdom of Jade material, but was there ever any canon information on Kowloon? The walled city was a notorious den of sin and crime, largely ran by the Triads until its demolition by Chinese authorities in the 90s. I imagine large portions would manifest in the Shadowlands intact and their desperate, criminal inhabitants would likely be resistant to joining Yu Huang's oppressive empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:46:57-08:00","id":53270,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I was wondering, if it was snowing in the world of the Quick, would there also be a type of plasm snow in the Shadowlands, such as you could ride a sled with, etc.?<br /> <br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:45:34-08:00","id":53298,"title":"","content":"ok...If a wraith goes to the skinlands, does he has an umbral reflection? and what happends when this umbral reflection gets attacked? does it recives damage or not?.<br /> <br /> Second: Any chances that in the manual, when you add the Antagonist you can create or add a Ghostfacers group for more Lighthearted or Dark Humour campaings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T12:19:25-08:00","id":53376,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Deadguy,<br /> <br /> Can Wraiths &quot;turn off&quot; Lifesight?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:51:04-08:00","id":54030,"title":"","content":"Reposting questions as they may have gotten buried/overlooked due to December/January.<br /> <br /> Now that I have fawned over you (see page 4 for me fawning) and Wraith, time for a few questions:<br /> 1) What is your favorite Ghost Story?<br /> 2) When developing the Shadow Players Guide (if I remember correctly) how hard was it with the Creole Arcanoi to avoid the topics of Zombism so much?<br /> 3) Would you consider in Wraith20 including Zombism and/or Risen in the core book (ala W20 having Changing Breeds) or even expanding to wraiths of the various kingdoms or even spectres?<br /> 4) Is there going to be a KS reward that would possibly include the backer getting involved with some of the design or is the plan to have the book largely written by the KS? (planning on throwing stupid money at this so always good to plan ahead <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> )<br /> 5) Monitors seemed like perhaps they might have been the biggest bad of the Guilds due to Lifeweb. Were they intended this way from early on?<br /> 6) In your mind, how much interaction would a standard vanilla wraith game have with the Skinlands? I know there is variation but I like to know what was default during conception.<br /> <br /> This last one I assume probably cannot be answered (professionalism, etc) but incase it can be (seeing some of the things Rich has discussed makes me think it might be possible).<br /> 7) How did you feel when Wraith was ended? Was is conflicted? Did you agree but regret? etc. I don't mean to open old wounds but it seemed so sudden to me (I was young and not as forward thinking at the time so there were likely signs) that I am curious if it was a surprise. I remember the forward to End of Empires feeling like it was trying to be put into words. Thank you for trying to do as much as was done with that book. It did make me feel that even thought my favorite was being put down, that I was not thought less of by the team working on it for liking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:26:16-08:00","id":54448,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Soulsteel: does it take one soul to make \u2013 say \u2013 a sword? Or can a few items be made from the same piece of Corpus [a single wraith]? <br /> <br /> If a few items can be made from the same Wraith, could a Soulforger amputate an arm (from someone else), forge it into something, then let said bit of Corpus grow back?<br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:27:42-08:00","id":54747,"title":"","content":"@Deadguy<br /> Question: What is the official symbol of Stygia?<br /> <br /> Comments:<br /> 1. Paris is awesome necropolis material. As it happens our weekly wraith game is set there<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. Highly recommend &quot;Ghost Bride.&quot; Its basically color text for a Dark Kingdom of Jade campaign.<br /> <br /> 3. Inspiration for harrowing...what could be better than Lady Gaga's ad for her perfume line...its just wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:18:09-08:00","id":55087,"title":"","content":"Random answer time, as the snow comes down in Carolina...<br /> <br /> [Bear in mind - all answers given relate to as things are /now/. There may be some changes coming. You have been warned.]<br /> <br /> As things stand now, it's one Corpus, one item. Industrialized wraith-farming is a little more Robin Cook than I was willing to go. This, incidentally, is why <br /> <br /> The official symbol of Stygia - The Key and the Mask are the two symbols that commonly stood in for Stygia. Groups on the outside looking in might have had...less flattering suggestions.<br /> <br /> A wraith cannot turn off LIfesight - at least, nobody's ever admitted to being able to do so. *cough cough*<br /> <br /> Ghostfacers are awesome. And some of the best ghost stories of all time have had humorous elements - I never want Wraith to be exclusively grim (or Grim). If you go back and look through the books, you'll see all sorts of sneaky jokes; horror and humor go hand in hand. So, to make a long answer even longer, yes, there will be some light-hearted elements. And I love the picture from Book of Legions of the guy underneath the soda machine.<br /> <br /> Just as there is no crying in baseball, there is no sledding in the Shadowlands, unless the snow is native to the core identity of the place. You can get snow from Maelstroms, but I wouldn't recommend sledding in it. <br /> <br /> Dark Kingdom of Jade was actually the second book I developed for WW, and I have great fondness for the Dark Kingdoms material. Kowloon was never specifically addressed, IIRC, but as far as I am concerned it's a lone, defiant outpost and a constant thorn in the Empire's side. Or it was, at least, before Xerxes made his left turn at Albuquerque.<br /> <br /> No umbral reflections. When you go to the Shadowlands, you go all the way. I've got no patience for souls that won't commit :-)<br /> <br /> Favorite ghost story - that's tough one, but I think the list starts with &quot;O Whistle And I'll Come To You, My Lad&quot; by M.R. James. My bookshelves are full of James, Oliver Onions, Robert Aickman, T.M. Wright and more. And yes, my first non-WW novel was in fact a ghost story, called Firefly Rain :-)<br /> <br /> Avoiding Zombiism - With anything, you need to draw a line about what fits and what doesn't, and then you have to be ruthless in excising the material that's across that line. Enforcing it can be hard, but the alternative is what we in the video game biz call &quot;feature creep&quot;, and that's a Cthulhoid horror that you really don't want to deal with.<br /> <br /> Broad-spectrum answer: I intend to get as much into the book as possible, and I have no idea as to any of the logistics vis-a-vis KS or whatever. Right now, my main antagonist is the book outline, and until I get that done I have blinders on to anything else.<br /> <br /> I don't know what was intended for Monitors before I got there, but I always regretted not having the chance to make people realize exactly how scary they could be. Not necessarily /bad/, but scary. That being said, imagine a few of those folks going into business with the late Mr. Artemus Vanderwal....<br /> <br /> Speak not the Gaga's name, lest ye summon it. <br /> <br /> And as for Wraith's ending...well, I meant what I wrote in the afterword to Ends of Empire, and I think those words still say it best. I wish we'd had more time to tell the story, but I was very lucky that I got as much time as I did, and I appreciate you all coming along for the ride. And, I got the chance to close the door and turn out the lights in a way that very few creatives in any medium ever get to do. If Wraith had stayed dead, I would have been creatively satisfied with the sendoff that we - Bruce, Geoff, Ed and the rest of the crew - gave it. It is and always will be one of the creative achievements I am proudest of.<br /> <br /> That being said, right now it just means I've got a helluva starting point. <br /> <br /> \u200bDeadguy out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:25:32-08:00","id":55091,"title":"","content":"hey deadguy, any chances to have a Map of the Underworld on the next book? <br /> im a bit confused, the way i described the underworld to my players was pretty much this &quot;Imagine a map of the world, a giant island between america and europe, and a big ass storm in the middle.&quot;<br /> I odnt know if that would be a more accurate potrayal of it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":