my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:42:20-08:00","id":55751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=55741#post55741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, in theory every object that has been destroyed is now an artifact (or relic), What happend to the nuclear bombs that were used on WW2 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>One was used to destroy Enoch. The Smiling Lord kept the other in reserve to use against Yu Haung. As for you question about babies.. I would assume they don't exist long enough to make any real attachments, so they either immediately fall to Oblivion or Transcend.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:48:20-08:00","id":56907,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your time Rich. I am super excited for Wr20 and told my wife to expect me to give in to my weakness and devote many many USD to it....many indeed.... /beard stroke","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T17:22:13-08:00","id":57091,"title":"","content":"hey deadguy, thanks for all your help with wraith and for being so direct when it comes to answers and with the information.<br /> i wanted to ask you something, if its not much to ask. I recently meet a lovecraftian fan who makes soundtracks and scores, i asked him if he could work music FOR Wraith. i was wondering if theres any even little chance for him to get a shout out on the 20Years of Wraith, for the Reference section,thats some of his work <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/grail-nights\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/grail-nights</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T11:30:50-08:00","id":57540,"title":"","content":"You have questions. I have about five minutes at the keyboard before I need to go deal with the terrible thing happening on the stove in my kitchen.<br /> <br /> Erik - That was all me, and thank you for the kind words. The original Erik story in WPG was inspired by an executive outplacement firm I was working for at the time, which had a lovely office just off Newbury Street in Boston. One of the key office features was a giant map with huge stickpins marking where our various offices were, and that's what inspired the original story.<br /> <br /> Maps - One of my main stated goals for W20 is to make it more accessible. So, yes, I fully intend for there to be a map. Hopefully, someone with better small motor skills than mine will draw it.<br /> <br /> Wraith Sexytime - Think Passions, not....err, never mind. Going to leave that figure of speech right where I found it and back away slowly.<br /> <br /> General note - Not every dead person becomes a wraith. Not every item that's destroyed becomes a relic. Extrapolate as you will to all applicable instances :-)<br /> <br /> And that's the smell of terrible things happening to some unfortunate root vegetables and pork belly what never did no harm to nobody, so Deadguy Out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T12:26:57-08:00","id":57568,"title":"","content":"Can you be able to convert a Passion into a Fetter? (Since Asylum was used, I'll reference a scene from Coven) In Coven, the butler collects baby dolls (don't ask), his collection is one of his Passions (or his Fetter, not sure which). He cons the blood bather to getting a rare doll for his collection. He is gets the doll. Would said doll be his Passion (seeking the doll for his collection) or his Fetter (when he obtains it)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T12:53:48-08:00","id":57581,"title":"","content":"quick question Deadguy, How do Dreamcatchers and Ouija boards affect wraiths?. i imagined the Ouija like a sort of Magnet which captures any close creature from the underworld (such as wraiths, shades etc..) and tortures him while forcing him to answer questions..the catch being that the Ouija board bounds the wraith to the board itself..But it cant turn into a fetter.<br /> <br /> Also, the W20 years edition will Impliment the websites and &quot;Creepy Pastas.&quot; ? i mean wraiths trying to flee to the skinlands by creating myths or by creating eerie websites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-25-2014, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:03:11-08:00","id":58975,"title":"","content":"I cannot help but think of Slenderman as a Wraith.<br /> <br /> How much re-writing do you think might go on of the guilds? The Artificers I assume may have a stronger grasp into the skinlands now due to the Internet and inhabiting websites like /r/creepy and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T18:40:45-08:00","id":61228,"title":"","content":"Not so much a question as a suggestion: Resolving Passions/Fetters needs more weight to it; a point of Eidolon, at least. As it stands, all the process does is free you from travel restrictions. Hardly a fitting reward for the largest step on the road to Transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T00:10:14-08:00","id":63326,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> A bit of a different question. I was wondering about wraiths getting married to each other in the underworld. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I would imagine some would, wouldn't they? Would they have civil services from the Hierarchy and spiritual ones by the Heretics perhaps, depending on their personal affiliations, beliefs, etc.?<br /> <br /> Thank you and best wishes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T19:18:32-08:00","id":63688,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> I forgot to ask this question too: Do Vulpines count as Specters for Brendan's Lay and like Arcanos that repel Specters?<br /> <br /> Looking forward to your answers for both my questions.<br /> <br /> Sincerest thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","user":"Khaleesi","date":". 02-02-2014, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:31:24-08:00","id":64112,"title":"","content":"Tying in the Kitsune?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T22:02:06-08:00","id":67722,"title":"","content":"Hi PaladinDemo, No, not Kitsune. I mean vulpines, as in the Specter version of barghast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T15:11:33-08:00","id":68664,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy,<br /> <br /> 1. Is there a way to buy off a shadows thorns?<br /> <br /> 2. My Wraith campaign has been going on for some time now and the players shadows are becoming fairly powerful. What do you think would be a good avenue for shadow experience?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> Aeoris","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":1391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","user":"Aeoris","date":". 02-10-2014, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:24:24-08:00","id":70734,"title":"","content":"Greetings from Greece!<br /> <br /> Long time fan of Wraith, both of the official and the unofficial material (that has surfaced some time ago in Scribd and elsewhere).<br /> One of the most impactive, albeit short-lived experience of Role Play I have ever enjoyed, was with Wraith. I don't think many ways of typing &quot;thank you&quot; are left in this forum, so I will proceed to some questions. Kind of.<br /> <br /> All of the (three) times I have initiated a Wraith campaign as ST, I gathered an even amount of people; half would play the Psyches and the other half would play the according Shadows. Psyche players created characters in Psyche/Shadow pairs, background and all. Afterwards the Shadowguides would gather and create their own characters in secret of the Psyche players. This style of character creation would make Shadows privy to every and all details of the Psyches, thus providing them with intimate details further augmenting their role play and the experience, in general. What is, in your opinion, the kind of Shadowguiding that would better reflect the mood of Wr20? Something like the former or each player being the Shadowguide of the player next to him?<br /> <br /> Will there be an Angst-equivalent rating of Shadowguide RP voice volume (eg 1-2 whispering, 3-6 normal voice, etc)? Do you think this was an unpopular &quot;instruction&quot; of the previous edition?<br /> <br /> Would you consider producing any &quot;Black Dog&quot; material for Wr20? If yes, what would it be? (And yes I know, that the imprint doesn't exist (for the time being) Political Correct-ness be damned)<br /> <br /> Do you think after Gehenna, Vampires would continue their Jyhad in Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>kill your god, kill your tv","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2261-urbanfractal","name":"urbanfractal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:27:55-08:00","id":80386,"title":"","content":"Hi Mr. Deadguy!<br /> <br /> Thanks for being here! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was wondering about two things:<br /> <br /> 1) I want to second Khaleesi's question about marriages in the Shadowlands. I would also think they existed, probably for both nostalgic reasons, romantic ones and for alliances as well, much as they did in Medieval times, for political purposes, etc. Looking forward to your thoughts on this!<br /> <br /> 2) Would a wraith be able to get new merits and thorns (oops, I meant flaws!)? It seems overtime and their experiences this should be possible. If so, how would it work? Could they be bought with experience?<br /> <br /> Had some more questions, but will wait!<br /> <br /> Thanks so much!<br /> <br /> Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","user":"Katrina","date":". 03-01-2014, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T00:22:37-08:00","id":81984,"title":"","content":"Let me see if I can help, since I'm re-reading all the <i>Wraith</i> material right now...<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE</b>: I don't work for Onyx Path, and I am not involved in any of the Wr20 stuff. Source material/Deadguy (the ultimate source) trumps anything I might be wrong about, of course. This is just musings from another fan.<br /> <br /> PaladinDemo - both, if I understand your question correctly. Using your example, collecting the dolls is the Passion, and the dolls themselves are the Fetter. Fetters are the physical objects, while Passions are the emotions regarding them.<br /> <br /> Crowley - I recall something from <i>Mediums</i> about Ouija boards and the like, you might want to check that out. I haven't hit that one in my (re-read) list yet.<br /> <br /> cryocube - Spectre or some sort of Unseelie Fae, definitely. The last episode of Supernatural had Slenderman as a thing (I haven't seen it yet. Have you? It sounded pretty awesome.). As to the rest of your statement, I don't work for OP, so I don't know.<br /> <br /> atamajakki - I agree, but there's systematic problems with it. As a background, Eidolon is optional (though you'd be crazy <i>not</i> to take it). Perhaps a more detailed explanation (and process) of Transcendence is in order?<br /> <br /> Khaleesi - Vulpines are basically made in the same manner as barghasts, so I would assume so (being Moliated Spectres and all). As to marriage... I'm sure some of the Far Shores practice it, but I can't imagine Stygia endorsing such a thing. At least, not with Charon gone.<br /> <br /> Aeoris - I can't think of a way to &quot;buy off&quot; Thorns, but there are ways to (permanently) reduce a Shadow's Angst, which would affect how often they could use them.<br /> <br /> urbanfractal - I can't speak as to the bulk of your post, but if any vampires made it to the Underworld, yes, I would expect them to continue the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Katrina - Thorns can be purchased with experience, though Merits are usually Storyteller fiat, springing out of plot.<br /> <br /> Again, this is my opinion. Do not take anything I say as written in stone, I'm just trying to help people out.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T07:12:59-08:00","id":82093,"title":"","content":"Ideally, we'd get a book that covered Heretics, Transcendence, and the Far Shores. All three are pretty big deals in Wraith, yet there's not much ink on any of the subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:39:26-08:00","id":82787,"title":"","content":"Whoops.<br /> <br /> Big apologies for the long absence, folks. Part of that was due to a very bad week spent wrestling with norovirus - lots of Harrowing inspiration coming from that one, believe me - and part of that was me desperately trying to pick up pieces of everything that fell behind due to norovirus.<br /> <br /> But, I'm back, and will be digging into the question backlog forthwith. I thank you for your patience, and hopefully this won't happen again.<br /> <br /> Marriage - Avoiding the obvious Peter Cook/Princess Bride jokes, I firmly believe in the concept of marriage for wraiths. Leaving aside questions of consummation, the grounds certainly exist for emotional attachment between two dead folks, and people - alive or dead - often formalize behaviors with rituals. So I can certainly see wraiths falling in love and wanting to share their existence, and I can see them wanting to formalize their arrangement and celebrate doing so. Whether wraiths could develop Passions related to their spouse, well, that's an area for exploration. And I can certainly imagine Shadows making a normal domestic squabble worse...<br /> <br /> That being said, I regard most episodes of &quot;Say Yes To The Dress&quot; as my own personal Harrowing, so I'm making an executive decision and banning that sort of thing from the Underworld forthwith.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shadow stuff - this is a little bit of a spoiler, but here goes. We will not be making huge changes to basic Shadowplay in 20th edition. We are, however, going to be exploring and providing alternate methods of play for folks, and we're looking to deepen the RPing experience of Shadowguiding. Shadowguiding is one of my favorite aspects of Wraith and I don't want to do anything to take away from it; at the same time, it's also potentially difficult to find a good &quot;level&quot; for it within a group, it demands a certain level of trust between players that can be hard to come by, and you want to stay away from trigger-y badness. So there will be more on playing Shadows, and some rules variants to make sure the experience is as accessible and enjoyable as possible.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T17:36:15-08:00","id":82860,"title":"","content":"so,no chances on adding the manifestations of the Oblivion and spectres within the internet? (creepy pastas and urban myths?)<br /> which actors/musicians etc... are official wraiths on your book? would Molly ringwood's career be a wraith or spectre?<br /> <br /> What determinates Who becomes a servant of Oblivion , i mean is there an Evil-O-Meter to pick servants of the Oblivion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":".  more questions 03-02-2014, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T21:23:02-08:00","id":82944,"title":"","content":"Playing with a ouija board in Wraith is a lot like walking into a biker bar humming &quot;Call Me Maybe&quot; with your overstuffed wallet in one hand and a poorly folded map in the other. You might be just fine, but you're pretty much asking someone to mess with you.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T21:29:17-08:00","id":82948,"title":"","content":"Reposting an old query: any chance of mechanically beefing up resolving Passions/Fetters? The only mechanical benefit is easier travel throughout the Underworld when I think something more meaty might help lure players to Transcendence/resolutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T21:41:15-08:00","id":82960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=82948#post82948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reposting an old query: any chance of mechanically beefing up resolving Passions/Fetters? The only mechanical benefit is easier travel throughout the Underworld when I think something more meaty might help lure players to Transcendence/resolutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely on the radar.<br /> <br /> Important things should be important.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:48:17-08:00","id":83212,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy!<br /> <br /> Is there a way to get rid off, resolve or negate a Thorn? I would imagine any such process would be challenging.<br /> <br /> And can more Merits and Flaws be bought later, rather than just at the start of the game, as events happen and your new experience might suggest adding to these?<br /> <br /> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T21:31:56-08:00","id":85829,"title":"","content":"Hi there<br /> <br /> Katrina - Bearing in mind that everything is on the table for Wraith 20th, the Shadow is a spiky thing. Trying to detach one of its Thorns - one of its primary ways of interacting with the universe - would be a very, very big deal, and very difficult to do. But that doesn't mean I'm not thinking about it.<br /> As for more Merits and Flaws, that's a Storyteller decision. If the experience is there, and the player and ST agree that a new Merit and/or Flaw is /appropriate/ based on character experience, there's no reason not to adjust things accordingly. What that sort of thing shouldn't be used as, however, is a sort of Cayman Islands account for character creation points, where new Merits and Flaws miraculously pop up to float things around without any character or story justification.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T10:32:20-08:00","id":86108,"title":"","content":"will you work on the relations between the wraiths and others beings of the world of darkness?, i ask this because i run demon the fallen. and in the demons eyes the wraiths should HATE them. but what about the wraith relation towards the fallen ones?<br /> <br /> also, correct me but, a wraith cant speak with the living unless the living wishes to hear them? how does the comunicating mechanic works? (i mean, Hunters/Imbued seem to always be able to comunicate with them, but wraiths have a hard time trying to reach their loved ones)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T01:37:11-08:00","id":86592,"title":"","content":"Hey I just noticed this thread! Great work on a great game that has affected the whole company, Exalted draws a lot from Wraith, and even Scion stole a lot of ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> So Things I most want are:<br /> <br /> More info on the Dark Kingdoms, we could use a whole damn book on it! It was probably the best part of the Shadows Players Guide. And I would love to know how for instance the Dark Kingdom of Sand holds out since they have access to divine miracles and ancient Effigies. Mummies even have the power to do things like easily convert real world items to relics, anything from a warehouse of stationary to a Cruiseliner. That and the fact that say Mages, and Demons can also have a huge impact on the Underworld. As mentioned you have a lot more to cover like Arabian Dark Kingdoms and the fallout say of ancient dark Kingdoms from say Persia, Sumeria, Australia.<br /> <br /> I really think it would be beneficial to talk about raising traits past 5, for instance Ghosts should have some access to Abilities and Attributes past five, and I would really love some discussion on Arcanoi past five, at the very least it would be cool to use them for things like Malfeans, and hoary old Plasmids.<br /> <br /> I would love some more Arcanoi, I've mentioned before it would be nice to say have say an Arcanoi to represent Demonic Wraiths/beings, one for Angelic Wraiths, and an Arcanoi for building your Own Far Shore like realm (Swar and the Dark Kingdom of Jade for instance got unique powers to build their realms, a general one would be nice). I love the bits on Angelics/Demonics and Djinn, I really love it when you encounter mysterious non Ghost entities in the Underworld. I really loved Nudhri, and the Nudhriel option, and I like the secret that the Black Spiral is connected to Labyrinth, and some Malfeans are also Maeljin Incarna. With that Said I would love talk of say Apep in Wraith since it seems like he would be recognized as a Malfean plaguing the world. Phantasmagoria really needs cleaning up. And I would really like it if there was discussion on say Rituals/Ceremony magic, you could use it to represent the already existent power of things like the Ferrymen Ritual, but it could be used for all sorts of things missing from the gameline, like creating Artifacts and any weird misc thing.<br /> <br /> I love Risen, it was my first Wraith Book and it is great, I would love that in the Core! And discussion of the interaction between Risen and those revenant walking dead that resulted from the Maelstrom. Its kind of a big deal that the Walking Dead issue went from a rare instance to a common occurrence after the Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also was it true that you were thinking of having Anubis turn out to be Abel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T06:36:18-08:00","id":86717,"title":"","content":"Wraith 20th is happening for sure? take my money, NOW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T06:40:56-08:00","id":86719,"title":"","content":"I have a lot of questions On wraith, some already mentioned... The Main concerns being Orpheus and Demon, and how you are going to incorporate (or not incorporate) those to &quot;species&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> (upon reading the forum I got basically what i wanted answer wise, I was just to hyped to wait).<br /> <br /> Another Question though...Do you think that Risen are going to be &quot;nerfed&quot; because it seemed that they could easily be abused if the ST was not really careful. I really hope risen will be included and hopefully added upon in the release, as well as the spectres. so much evil to be used in those books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","user":"Iris","date":". 03-08-2014, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T07:33:48-08:00","id":86745,"title":"","content":"Quick general statement on Risen:<br /> <br /> 1-I love those guys.<br /> 2-Nobody ever believes me when I say that the inspiration for them was Ray Bradbury's short story &quot;Pillar of Fire&quot; and not The Crow, but there you go.<br /> 3-Yes, there's going to be room for them in Wraith 20. How much is still TBD.<br /> 4-No, they're not going to be nerfed. They're tremendously powerful, yes, but they also have tremendous vulnerabilities. The trick is making sure it's an appropriate balance.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T07:40:38-08:00","id":86750,"title":"","content":"It makes me happy that it actually was not &quot;The Crow&quot; but ill admit, I assumed haha!. I agree they are very vulnerable, thats why wraith is tied for my favorite classic WoD game (with Changeling). I feel Wraith is the game for experienced RPers. There is so much amazing stuff in it, thank you so much for doing it, you will be getting alot of money from me to fund!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T22:01:24-07:00","id":89259,"title":"","content":"General positioning statement on Dark Kingdoms and Other Critters:<br /> <br /> I have always been a big fan of expanding the Dark Kingdoms. The Sea That Knows No Sun was my baby in the original Wraith PG, and I have always been a big fan of expanding the world. So, yes, I am working on including Dark Kingdoms material.<br /> <br /> Other Critters: My main interest is in wraiths. Which means that yes, there will be some exploration of how they interact with and feel about other critters, but it's always going to be a Wraith-centric view. And if there's a choice between &quot;content that makes for a better core Wraith experience&quot; and &quot;nailing down every last bit of inter-critter sectionality&quot;, then wraiths win every time. I unfortunately have only so many words to play with, and the Arcanoi chapter alone is threatening to grow larger than my first novel.<br /> <br /> So: On the radar, yes. Can't promise everything, but my ambition is boundless.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T03:22:01-07:00","id":89373,"title":"","content":"Bwhahahaahaaaa Arcanoi!<br /> <br /> On a side note, I'm reading Dark Kingdom of Jade right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T09:35:14-07:00","id":89538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=89373#post89373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bwhahahaahaaaa Arcanoi!<br /> <br /> On a side note, I'm reading Dark Kingdom of Jade right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Witness the origin of Martial Arts for some reason needing to be different from Brawl! (^VVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T10:10:35-07:00","id":89553,"title":"","content":"Year of the Lotus before it was cool... man its an insanely readable book breezing right through it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nother Wraith 20 Question, will we finally get some info on rural and wilderness Goodness? That was something I always felt was missing after reading the core, Buried Secrets and the Players Guide, we never get much on Wilderness from a Wraith's Perspective, the closest thing we get is the Bush of Ghosts has Ghost Animals. But what about haunted forests, Mountains or even farms? There is an insane amount of stuff that can go in here, even if it was an ominous paragraph that would of been better then nothing.<br /> <br /> And with basic material being constantly in Demand what about trips to Islands in the Tempest for materials to build with? I mean Stygia mines the Veinous Stairs, and the Labyrinthe, seems like even sand, dirt and rocks would be worth the trip, not to mention having odd Islands with misc materials like ghost metals, goo, and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T13:14:01-07:00","id":89662,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> I wanted to know:<br /> <br /> 1) If there would be more information on the <i>Equitaes?</i> How many? How armed? Would love to see the emblems for them too and any other info.<br /> <br /> 2) Any more information on the Order of the Sacred Band? Other orders?<br /> <br /> 3) Is the Order of the Avenging Flame still around from the Hierarchy book?<br /> <br /> Wish I had a large Patho coffee cup! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I sent in a submission; wish me luck!<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for your responses! I am so excited to be able to look forward to exploring more of the underworld! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T03:26:49-07:00","id":90080,"title":"","content":"which new concepts or ideas would you include in the book? you mentioned that middle east would be a &quot;Spoiler.&quot; but any other hints?<br /> second question: how ya been?<br /> Third Question: you been incredibly helpfull for all of us, resolving our questions very directly. taking care of the Players and ST by taking time in responding our questions and replying to us. I belive i speak for all on the forums to say that we appreciate that a dev takes his time to be so transparent and so willing to be in touch with the fans of his work...so the question being. After W20 Years is Released, Will you still be around to help us with our question or &quot;My job is done, my dimension needs me.&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 03-16-2014, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T19:05:18-07:00","id":92568,"title":"","content":"So, off to GDC this week. Communication may be light. There will be more on the day to day functioning of Stygia and its state institutions. Especially the cool ones. And fwiw, it means a lot to me that you folks still enjoy and care about the game. Wraith will always be very important to me. And the same goes for its fans. One way or another, I'll always be around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T19:40:08-07:00","id":92580,"title":"","content":"We love you bunches, Dansky.<br /> <br /> Can we expect any detail on specific Far Shores or Heretic cults? It's always felt like there's a hole in the <i>Wraith</i> book list for a book specifically on those two, which go ever so nicely hand in hand. The Far Shores are fascinating and tragically under-explored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T03:20:43-07:00","id":92717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=92568#post92568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, off to GDC this week. Communication may be light. There will be more on the day to day functioning of Stygia and its state institutions. Especially the cool ones. And fwiw, it means a lot to me that you folks still enjoy and care about the game. Wraith will always be very important to me. And the same goes for its fans. One way or another, I'll always be around.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, whenever a fan has a question , whenever a DM is confused. we can hope that we will see you around going &quot;Luke, You Will Go to Stygia, there you will learn about wraith..&quot;<br /> <br /> Im currently running a MtA game, i dont know how much you know about the game..but since is your juridistiction....<br /> <br /> some of my mages might..be on ermm...Stygia, trying to pass as Wraiths....yeah, thats getting a bit complicated.<br /> Thing is, Would paradox apply as if they were on the Fleshlands or since theres ghosts, and oblivion, and spectres and what not. there woudnt be any dangers of gaining paradox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 03-23-2014, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T22:23:53-07:00","id":98956,"title":"","content":"Right. Back for GDC, and all its attendant wonders and horror. (Note: the zombie plague is going to start at t hat show one of these years. Just wait. You'll see)<br /> <br /> In any case:<br /> <br /> Far Shores and particular Heretic cups? Almost certainly there will be more material on them. There will probably be some adjustment of the power dynamic in the three-cornered Heretic/Hierarchy/Renegade triangle, as I think we can make things a little more interesting by unbalancing things a bit. I'll keep you posted :-)<br /> <br /> As for the mages in Stygia, hooboy. This is always a bad idea, especially for the mages. My understanding for something like this would be that normal Paradox rules would go by the by, but if they did stuff that was counter to the consensual reality of the Underworld - which, you must admit, gives a hell of a lot of latitude - then they run the risk of generating Paradox that way.<br /> <br /> Now, back to the outline.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T06:56:15-07:00","id":99129,"title":"","content":"Great to hear about the Heretics and the Far Shores! They need more stuff kind of badly.<br /> <br /> Any chance at more info on the Guilds? Specificly the ones that never got books<br /> <br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> *hides Proctor cheerleader uniform*<br /> On the subject of Proctors, btw, I'm curious for your take on a disagreement I had a while back. Can an Embodied wraith see and hear back accross the shroud into the Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> Lastly, I was wondering if we can expect new/updated information on the Ferrymen and Pasiphae?<br /> <br /> Thanks Rich!<br /> Keep being awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/79-alexisvalarr","name":"alexisvalarr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar79_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T07:07:15-07:00","id":99135,"title":"","content":"got a little question about the writting process and some others.<br /> How do you and other writters work on the plot when it involves other games, for example (major spoiler) did you talk to the other guys saying &quot;Hey, i think the true black hand its a bit too OP, mind you if i go all Doctor Strangelove on them?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> kind of a touchy subject here, Will you include or will you avoid subjects such as school massacres within the wraith universe as possible origins for spectres or even new oblivion soldiers and LT.?<br /> <br /> <br /> Is Kurt (THe Ferryman) A lead singer of a grunge band who may or may not had comitted suicide?<br /> <br /> <br /> On the core book its stated on the idea that wraiths can act on the Skinlands through belief per say, if more people belive that a place is haunted, they can act more freely, right?. how does youtube and the mass media willaffect the wriaths as for now?<br /> <br /> any chances to see famous people as wraiths and as part of the cannon ?<br /> <br /> my mage players are currently stuck on stygia and i wanted to know, they bought weapons from the skinlands, do they affect other wraiths or they need weapons From the Underworld to actually inflict damage to wraiths and spectres.<br /> <br /> another touchy subject: theres a couple of astronauts that actually died and we have the Discovery and Columbia incident, any chances to mention wraiths trying to go to the outerspace within the umbra? (yeah..spaceghosts.....i think hanna barbera will try to sue me now)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T22:13:26-07:00","id":99758,"title":"","content":"I am very interested in Wraith Astronauts. We know Relic space tech must exist, as well as various accidents, not just from NASA we know the Soviets have had a lot of censored casualties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:26:57-07:00","id":99994,"title":"","content":"It seems to me like Oboli were mentioned less and less after a certain point. Did they stop being a concept in later books or was it just something that ended up being overlooked? Also, any info on the spending power of an Obolus might be nice.<br /> <br /> Also not so much a question as a nag, but please remember to include how to recover Pathos this time. I keep having nightmares about it getting left out again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:34:04-07:00","id":100002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=99994#post99994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me like Oboli were mentioned less and less after a certain point. Did they stop being a concept in later books or was it just something that ended up being overlooked? Also, any info on the spending power of an Obolus might be nice.<br /> <br /> Also not so much a question as a nag, but please remember to include how to recover Pathos this time. I keep having nightmares about it getting left out again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I attribute it to the writers seemingingly confused about Oboli. Half seemed to not realize they represented a whole soul's worth of material. Its kind of like how they seemed to forget that Wraiths speak the Language of the Dead for each Paradigm, so my guess for each Dark Kingdom or so. They luckily remembered it in the Great War Fiction.<br /> <br /> It would be nice if they talked about the Economy taking both Pathos and Oboli into account.<br /> <br /> And Yeah seriously that was a HUGE dent in the system missing the Pathos Harvesting in the Core rules. It would be nice to also clarify it, so that for instance there is a limit to how often you can harvest. My rule is once per scene, but its hard to tell how generous or strict that is without getting actual play opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:06:20-07:00","id":100179,"title":"","content":"I promise not to leave one of the main rules out this time. Scout's honor.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:51:01-07:00","id":100266,"title":"","content":"Would it be safe to say that Jason Vorhees is a bad ass risen? Because that always my go to description for a really pissed risen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:53:52-07:00","id":100267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=100266#post100266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be safe to say that Jason Vorhees is a bad ass risen? Because that always my go to description for a really pissed risen.</div> </div> </div> </div>im pretty sure that he is Either<br /> A ) a risen with equal parts spectre<br /> B ) a gorehound (pentex/fomori)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T00:25:51-07:00","id":100633,"title":"","content":"Are the Guilds back in operation officially or will it still be guilt by association?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:59:59-07:00","id":101960,"title":"","content":"I love Wraith. I think it's one of the best world buildings I have ever seen - the setting is incredible, so ripe with potential that it's almost overwhelming (in a good way).<br /> <br /> The only thing that annoyed me a bit was the shadow play. Wraith is something hard to find players for, so all my Wraith games were on online forums; and at the site we used at the time (Ex Libris Nocturnis, anyone?), the usual was for the player who was controlling the character to also control the shadow. The issue with this was how it massively derailed games - any given turn would be 90% about characters interacting with their own shadows, and 10% about characters interacting with each other and the world.<br /> <br /> How much is the shadow really supposed to represent? A constant voice that is always there and replies to every single thing that happens in the world? A little devil on the shoulder that only speaks or acts when there's an opportunity to do extreme mischief, staying hidden otherwise? Or something in between?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2518-erasculio","name":"Erasculio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2518_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T15:46:22-07:00","id":102220,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> Welcome back! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had a question on children wraiths. What happens to child wraiths as they age. Do they develop mentally and emotionally, as normal children do? Since they will not go through the biological and hormonal changes the living go through, would they maintain their childlike presence? Would the type of Passion they have tie into this too. For example, if their Passion was to protect their doll, if they did grow in maturity, then wouldn't the doll lose the intensity of connection? Or would staying at a childlike emotional level, would they maintain those bounds?<br /> <br /> Thank you so much!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T15:51:27-07:00","id":102223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khaleesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=102220#post102220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> Welcome back! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had a question on children wraiths. What happens to child wraiths as they age. Do they develop mentally and emotionally, as normal children do? Since they will not go through the biological and hormonal changes the living go through, would they maintain their childlike presence? Would the type of Passion they have tie into this too. For example, if their Passion was to protect their doll, if they did grow in maturity, then wouldn't the doll lose the intensity of connection? Or would staying at a childlike emotional level, would they maintain those bounds?<br /> <br /> Thank you so much!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impression they were in a state of Emotional retardation, but they could possibly grow beyond this as many of the dead can transform throughout the ages potentially. It begs the question if a ten year old wraith is moliated into something akin to a hulking demon, or a crone after millennia of existence are they emotionally still a child? After all Moliation can make mean into beasts, and many Wraiths who would liken themselves to Gods or Demons seem to be reinforced by new moliated images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T16:46:16-07:00","id":102246,"title":"","content":"A handful of questions:<br /> <br /> Has there any thought been put in towards giving Shadowguiding a little bit more mechanical guidance? Not like extra Thorns or further Angst rules, but rather defining how active the Shadow should be and how much each player needs to do it. Someone posted a Whisper Points mechanic a while back - the Shadow can talk/act a number of times per scene equal to the character's permanent Angst, or something like that - and a similar, official mechanic would be welcome.<br /> <br /> What's the state of Necropolis Florence in the modern day? Spectres sacked and occupied it for a fair deal of The Great War, and while I assume they had to flee once the Great Maelstrom subsided, such a place has to be tainted still.<br /> <br /> Can we expect Dark Kingdom of Jade (and other non-Western) Wraith material in Wraith20? I'm tallking equal parts fluff and their funky Arcanoi. (As a sub-question; could we please get information on Aokigahara, the &quot;suicide forest&quot; of Japan?)<br /> <br /> Will there be example Heretic cults in Wraith20? They never got the love they deserved during the original run and I can't honestly remember anyone beyond the Riders on the Wheel (from <i>Haunts</i>, I believe; the gambler guys?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:10:15-07:00","id":102838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=102246#post102246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone posted a Whisper Points mechanic a while back - the Shadow can talk/act a number of times per scene equal to the character's permanent Angst...).</div> </div> </div> </div>...........<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:45:25-07:00","id":102867,"title":"","content":"Guild by association...OK, not touching that one...yet :-)<br /> <br /> Shadowplay: Optimum shadowplay should max out at 25-30% of the time. Where it's really useful, of course, is if the party splits and Shadowguiding allows all the players to stay involved, but really, if a Shadow becomes constant chatter its blandishments become white noise - easily ignored because they're just a constant buzz. Pick your spots and don't overuse it for maximum effectiveness. That being said, the rules and advice on Shadowguiding will be expanded.<br /> <br /> Dark Kingdoms stuff - Hoping to have some nice meaty material on them. The question of how much is largely one of word count.<br /> <br /> Child Wraiths - Some of them may mature as they age - it depends on experience and will to change. Others, not so much. And I can think of few things more frightening than an angry, resentful 6 year old in a Moliated body with all kinds of spiky bits.<br /> <br /> I'd stay out of Florence if I were you. <br /> <br /> Heretic Cults - well, the Riders were one of mine originally, so I'd be kind of a jerk to myself if I got rid of them :-) More seriously, yes, I want there to be more definition and more usable material for the Heretics. <br /> <br /> Deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T14:23:00-07:00","id":102930,"title":"","content":"One minor thing; could we finally see Phantasm get polished up a bit? It's always seemed like a funny fit for Wraith and doesn't often come up (to say nothing of &quot;rip out someone's soul&quot; as the final power with no further explanation!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T18:53:25-07:00","id":103057,"title":"","content":"necronauts D:?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:16:20-07:00","id":104239,"title":"","content":"There will be polishing of Phantasm. I know just the guy to do it, too...<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T15:14:46-07:00","id":104370,"title":"","content":"I'd like to go ahead and make a request if I may, since now seems the best time. I would like in the Arcanoi/Guild write-ups for the Guild Marks to be called out specifically in their own section, like so:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Argos is the art of blah blah blah the Harbingers are blah blah blah<br /> <b>Guildmark: </b>The mark of Argos users is solid black eyes. Harbingers debate whether adding sunglasses makes them look cool or is simply redundant. </div> </div> </div>That way they are easy to pick out, and I can readily look up what they are for NPCs ('Yeah, Marcus has had Argos all this time!&quot; &quot;Then why didn't he have black eyes?&quot; &quot;Uh....&quot;). <br /> <br /> I think it would be a nice addition for the Lost/Dark Arcanoi too. So if you could, I'd appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T09:59:51-07:00","id":105638,"title":"","content":"Shadowguiding has always been one of my favourite parts of Wraith and while I do have the utmost trust for the man who has created the single most amazing RPG of all time I still do hope that you aren't gonna bog it down with extra rules.<br /> <br /> This is the project I have been waiting for since they announced V20 so it's a real dream come through for me. All Wraith needs is a slight polishing of the system to the Revised era and a little more fluff about the Heretics and the Guilds that never got their own books and naturally the Arcanoi of said Guilds being expanded. Of the Guilds I really have missed that the Monitors and the Solicitors the most followed closely by the Harbingers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T21:34:03-07:00","id":106032,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mr. D,<br /> <br /> In the real world, the Zombie Apocalypse-shtick is going full-throttle, with different organizations (including the CDC a few years ago) using the threat of zombies as a pretext for survivalist practices and products. When these \u201czombie preppers\u201d die, are they impacting Wraith Society? Would the Legions find themselves with raw recruits ready to take on the hordes of Shadow-eaten? Are the Walking Dead (as an element of pop-culture, not actual zombies) having an effect on the culture of the Restless Dead?<br /> <br /> [To be clear, I\u2019m not suggesting that zombies be included in Wraith. I\u2019m just curious what effect, if any, the RL zombie craze is having on the other side of the Shroud.] </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T11:20:09-07:00","id":107563,"title":"","content":"Zombie Wannabees and Doomsday Preppers in the Underworld - The thing you have to understand is that Doomsday preppers are going to be really, really disappointed that the world didn't end before they did, which potentially makes for some interesting Passions. (And of course, the basement bunker makes a heck of a Haunt...). My off the top of the head feeling on this is that these guys really wouldn't make good Legion recruits - they're not really &quot;joiners&quot;. I can, however, see a few Heretic cults that would be very appealing...<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T15:06:04-07:00","id":107730,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> I was curious to know about Castigation works when traveling to the Far Shores. Do they have their own Pardoners or an equivalent there to get rid of Angst? How do some Far Shores, which seem to incorporate elements that would seem to increase Angst deal with it without becoming Shadow-eaten? <br /> <br /> Thank you so much!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T15:19:34-07:00","id":107735,"title":"","content":"I am curious as to Pre-Charon Stygia, or Ancient Underworld in General. There was a lot of goodies in the Haunter book, and among them was the notion that they were originally Pandoran mystery cultists of a sort.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in more legends about Death Gods from the Ghosts Perspectives. We got so very little, like Hades talked about as a powerful wraith in Risen, and Wang Luo as possibly the first Ghost in Dark Kingdom of Jade.<br /> <br /> <br /> More on Swar! So twisted that they present the Underworld of India as one of their Heavens, cast in a dark light. We only got a taste of Swar, so I want to know more about the Indian Underworld! Moaaar I say!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T20:21:41-07:00","id":107925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=98956#post98956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the mages in Stygia, hooboy. This is always a bad idea, especially for the mages. My understanding for something like this would be that normal Paradox rules would go by the by, but if they did stuff that was counter to the consensual reality of the Underworld - which, you must admit, gives a hell of a lot of latitude - then they run the risk of generating Paradox that way.<br /> <br /> Now, back to the outline.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So what about the Euthanatoi and their Agama rituals that are meant to specifically place the Mage's soul (and Avatar?) into the Shadowlands for their spiritual enlightenment?<br /> <br /> I can't say what M20 will hold covering this topic (if it does at all) but the specifics of the Agama spell can be found in the revised Euthie trad book Pg. 68 for anyone interested. My question is what is the Wraith's perspective on this event? It barely mentions that it's possible for Wraith's to sense the Mage as not like all the other ghosts. (and I imagine that would make them very interested in finding out why or very annoyed if they do.) This arises many more questions.<br /> <br /> Do Euthies in the Agama appear with a Caul like other newly dead? If so is it always or just the Magi's first 'visit'? Also if so can they be Reaped by another Wraith or does the Avatar protect them? That section mentions them using their powers but only certain spheres. If the Mage is a ghost do they still get Paradox? (Harrowings are covered nicely and clearly, but nothing else about the situation) And something much more relevant to an upcoming game I'm running. When a Mage undergoes the Agama where do they end up in the Shadowlands? Is it random or does it correspond with there they lived or died in the physical world? I've seen these run in many different ways. I have two characters who come from different backgrounds. One is a Chakravant and expects to wind up in India when they die returning to their homeland, even if they die on an entirely different continent. I can't find any information on this. He is embarking on an Agama-te with this other character who's homeland is in America but is an initiate. Which controls where they end up? I might just have to tell them to shut up and deal with where I put them, but it does make me wonder.<br /> <br /> Another player I used to know told me their Euthanatos' Avatar was a Ferryman. I assumed despite their insistence that the Avatar merely had the image and abilities that resembled those of Wraith Ferrymen, yet wasn't an actual Ferrymen, but that was before I picked up the Wraith system myself. In a crossover scenario is that possible or just makes for someone's wishful thinking?<br /> <br /> Crowley mentioned also Necronauts.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure to which he was referring, but there was a so very brief mention of them in the Euthanatos Revised book as Magi who enact the Agama-re and explore the Shadowlands Professionally. However not much more was written on them besides a little info and a character template. This could have been an interesting bit of crossover to explore, but never got the chance since Wraith didn't make it to the Revised phase. Will there be any expansion on this? or will it be dropped?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T23:16:02-07:00","id":108000,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy!<br /> <br /> Will there be any rituals like there are in Geist and Vampire? In the Ebon Mask books series, based on Wraith, there was a ritual done by the Death Lords for a new one to use the mask of his predecessor. It seems like rituals of some sort would be a great edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T03:24:00-07:00","id":108070,"title":"","content":"can soulforged materials be destroyed? my players turned Carpenter into a bullet, and they are afraid that if they shoot it to someone, carpenter will take over","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:33:57-07:00","id":108863,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Mr. D,</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Any plans on expanding Haunt rules/benefits?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Speaking of Haunts\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">From the corebook, page 234,</span><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">\u201d A wraith may resist damage\u2026by seeking shelter within a Haunt.\u201d </span><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> If a Wraith has a Haunt, for example, that is the crossroads where he died (or another similarly open environment), would that protect against Maelstrom winds? Or would it have to be a structure that the Restless could retreat into? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T14:53:35-07:00","id":114342,"title":"","content":"Some quick hits:<br /> <br /> A mage can tell you their Avatar is a Ferryman. I also told a lot of people in high school that I had a girlfriend who lived in Canada, which is why they'd never met her. YMMV.<br /> Any Haunt will protect a bit; it's just a question of the effect being metaphorically appropriate. So the winds that howl around a building may just sweep past a crossroads. <br /> Destroying soulforged materials is doable but very, very difficult. And I don't blame them for being afraid of Carpenter. That vicious son of a bitch managed to jump game lines when no one was looking.<br /> Rituals of the dead - they exist, but they are very few and far between. Let's just say they get saved for momentous occasions.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T17:55:12-07:00","id":114439,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the devil...Will we see Carpenter on the anniversary book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T23:26:48-07:00","id":114577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=114342#post114342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some quick hits:<br /> <br /> A mage can tell you their Avatar is a Ferryman. I also told a lot of people in high school that I had a girlfriend who lived in Canada, which is why they'd never met her. YMMV.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured as much. Now about the other questions.....? Any hints? An upcoming game kinda depends on it.<br /> <br /> If anyone else on here wants to throw out their thoughts on those questions, I'm all for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","