of fun. After fifteen years (or more) or wanting to run a Wraith game based on Sartre's No Exit, I finally got my chance this summer. <br /> <br /> My question is simple,maybe I'm a dumbass, but I still can't piece together the story of Nhundri. Can you piece it together here or promise an answer in WtO20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2763-nunboi","name":"nunboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2763_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T11:50:38-07:00","id":115431,"title":"","content":"Forgive if this has been asked before, but will there be wordcount put towards playing in the aftermath of the Sixth Great Maelstrom and exploring the world once the Stormwall goes up? The depiction of a blasted Stygia was one of my favorite parts of Orpheus, and seeing that shattered underworld as a play option would be lovely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T16:53:59-07:00","id":115601,"title":"","content":"And that one wraith in the tower when the fragment comes through the wall... what was she going to say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T14:33:35-07:00","id":117650,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mr. D,<br /> <br /> Some Arcanoi, like Argos and Castigate, have well-defined Markings. Others, like Keening and Pandemonium don\u2019t do anything except give a Wraith a wardrobe-disposition. Any plans on re-working Arcanoi Markings? </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T20:23:48-07:00","id":117817,"title":"","content":"Will you update or add more info on other necropolis around the world? im chilean and it would be interesting to see how Santiago is a necropolis (since the military took over, tortured and killed people. i imagine chile having a large ammount of wraiths due to that)<br /> <br /> And, what happends when someone falls into coma? does he sort of enters Stygia and the underworld? or thats another's game jurisdistiction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 04-23-2014, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T09:15:40-07:00","id":118458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=117650#post117650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mr. D,<br /> <br /> Some Arcanoi, like Argos and Castigate, have well-defined Markings. Others, like Keening and Pandemonium don\u2019t do anything except give a Wraith a wardrobe-disposition. Any plans on re-working Arcanoi Markings? </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Pandemonium actually causes insanity and often tends to mold your very corpus according to that insanity. So it actually should be fairly well covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:45:48-07:00","id":118498,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=118458#post118458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pandemonium actually causes insanity and often tends to mold your very corpus according to that insanity. So it actually should be fairly well covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cHaunters are recognizably quirky, adopting all manner of peculiar mannerisms. Many have adopted billowing black cloaks as a sort of badge of honor or theatrical device,\u201d (<i>Wraith: the Oblivion</i>, 1996, p. 154).<br /> <br /> Unless it was in the Haunter Guildbook, I\u2019m not sure where the corpus-molding comes into play. Assuming, for the moment, that this corpus-molding is from the Guildbook (which I don\u2019t own), it still doesn\u2019t make it a \u2018well-defined\u2019 Marking. In addition to the aforementioned wardrobe-disposition, doesn\u2019t that mean that the Haunter\u2019s Marking is, essentially, Moliate? <br /> <br /> My thought with Arcanoi Markings is that they\u2019re like the classic \u2018devil\u2019s mark\u2019; little, unobvious tells that that don\u2019t stand out. However, if a Wraith knows what to look for, he can figure out what kind of Arcanoi another Wraith has a predilection for. <br /> <br /> Imagine a waiting room just outside an Anacreon\u2019s office. A Wraith is bringing in another soul, freshly-reaped from her caul, and showing her around. While the Reaper is showing her around, he gestures to a few of the waiting Wraiths, pointing out some of these tells. \u201cSee that lady with the black eyes? If you need directions, she\u2019d be a good person to talk to. I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve noticed that unpleasant voice stirring in the back of your head; see the guy with blackened fingertips? You might want to have a chat with him if that voice starts getting uncomfortably loud.\u201d<br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T11:05:07-07:00","id":118505,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy<br /> Whats the airspeed velocity of an undead stygian Swallow ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T01:56:00-07:00","id":119642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=118498#post118498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it was in the Haunter Guildbook, I\u2019m not sure where the corpus-molding comes into play. Assuming, for the moment, that this corpus-molding is from the Guildbook (which I don\u2019t own), it still doesn\u2019t make it a \u2018well-defined\u2019 Marking. In addition to the aforementioned wardrobe-disposition, doesn\u2019t that mean that the Haunter\u2019s Marking is, essentially, Moliate?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in the Haunters Guildbook, all the Guildbooks are simply excellent by the way so I highly recommend them. And no it's not Moliate, like said it's more of a mental quirk that can manifest in their Corpus, if taking the Aggravated Quirk flaw, and when it does manifest it tends to be in ways that Moliate really doesn't do. The book introduces three main quirks that are Spacial warping, Temporal anomality and Hallucinations (paraphrasing from memory). If the Haunter suffers from spatial warping he tends to experience space as somewhat fluid which may cause problems as he sometimes may miscalculate distances and generally seem a bit at odds with the environment, if he has aggravated quirk this can manifest for example as items worn, clothes, masks etc., seemingly warping to be inside their corpus wholly or partially. Temporal anomality means that they have problems with their perception of time and as aggravated there is one famous haunter who has aftershadows each younger than the last following it as it moves. Hallucinations clearly need little explanation but as aggravated they can manifest as stormclouds gathering and lighting flashing within his corpus to something whole lot odder.<br /> <br /> None of the Aggravated Quirks can really be molieted away since they manifest from within.<br /> <br /> So a bit like with Puppeteers the Haunters Arcanoi markings tend to be psychological instead of physical. Puppeteers can be noticed from the quirks they take with them from their multiple hosts and Haunters can be spotted by the quirks the Wylding, aka Pandemonium to those outside the Guild, causes in them. And atleast in my opinion it's fine that not all Arcanoi markings are physical ala Argos etc.<br /> <br /> Also there is a difference between Arcanoi markings and Guild markings... But that's mostly the problem with Artificers since their Arcanoi leaves them with Markings of the Machines they possess, in the modern day computer circuits and in the past oil stains, while their profession as Soulforgers leaves them with burn marks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:28:44-07:00","id":120403,"title":"","content":"Just found this thread and I just want to say I am a HUGE fan of Wraith. My best friend hasn't been too involved with the kickstarters, but the moment he heard Wr20 was coming out he requested I let him know when that kickstarter was going to start so he could help pledge money to it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, a major gripe my friend and I have had is actually with how limited the interaction between the land of the living and the land of the dead is. I'm not talking about wraiths popping into a coffee shop and saying hi to people or anything, but we felt more interaction with human proxies in the land of the living and more discussion about feeding of pathos off of humans would be nice. Just something to help remind us that Wraith's have something to do with the land of the living as we felt the two worlds were so segregated that the land of the dead almost started to feel like a fantasy realm where you would find dungeons and dragons.<br /> <br /> Also, so glad to hear you will be touching on shadowguiding, it has been something I've seen as a hindrance in the past but I loved it and knew it should stick around in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Finally, why has no one commented that Deadguy answered questions with post #42. I feel this was gross negligence on everyones part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> PS: For the Ultra Deluxe edition I would like to recommend more glow in the dark chains and ghosts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:44:04-07:00","id":120430,"title":"","content":"Will we be seeing Mediums in the Wr20 core? Speakers With The Dead was one of my favorite supplements from the original run (he says, as though he disliked any of them) and they add a lovely bit of spice to any chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:29:18-07:00","id":120978,"title":"","content":"Oh, and if you have the ability to decide where you can unveil it I would like to recommend the Winchester Mystery House in San Jose, California. They are opening it up for overnight stays and it is considered one of the most haunted places in America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T14:18:03-07:00","id":122662,"title":"","content":"Right. Speaking of death, the universe and everything...<br /> <br /> Had a lovely week last week running the narrative track at East Coast Game Conference, which included visits from the estimable Will Hindmarch and Jesse Scoble. For some reason they let me run the narrative track at the conference, so wacky hijinks abound. <br /> <br /> Wraiths' appearance is often based on self-image. With Pandemonium, self-image gets a little...funky. <br /> <br /> More Necropoli: Yes. Though obviously there's going to be a lot of pick-and-choose going on.<br /> <br /> Interaction between the living and the dead - the goal is to streamline that a bit, though within limits - we don't want every wraith to be &quot;Kitty Pryde with more superpowers but dead&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mediums will be touched on, but they're furthest out on the chopping block, I'm afraid. We'll see how much word count permits...<br /> <br /> There is no such thing as an undead Stygian swallow, nor is there air in the Underworld. YOUR QUESTION IS INVALID.<br /> <br /> Whew :-)<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:00:23-07:00","id":123011,"title":"","content":"Hi, RealDeadGuy, enough word count for specters and risen? I'm talking specifically about material from the Dark Reflections and The Risen books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:38:57-07:00","id":123227,"title":"","content":"xD! ok, being serious here. Do animals go to the underworld once they are dead? (yeah, i want my hachiko ghost finding his master in the underworld so he can trascend).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T11:01:27-07:00","id":123287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=123227#post123227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">xD! ok, being serious here. Do animals go to the underworld once they are dead? (yeah, i want my hachiko ghost finding his master in the underworld so he can trascend).</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. Only animals in the underworld, and animals is used rather loosely here, are the horses found on the banks of River Styx.<br /> <br /> Only dogs in the underworld are Barghest and they have nothing to do with animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T12:22:21-07:00","id":123348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=123287#post123287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they don't. Only animals in the underworld, and animals is used rather loosely here, are the horses found on the banks of River Styx.<br /> <br /> Only dogs in the underworld are Barghest and they have nothing to do with animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're in the Bush of Ghosts, where animal ghosts are a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T23:33:43-07:00","id":123625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=123348#post123348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you're in the Bush of Ghosts, where animal ghosts are a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> Thanks for pointing that out, I just tend to assume either Kingdom of Iron or Jade as the setting most play in and so tend to forget to mention exception happening elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T00:38:26-07:00","id":124322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=123348#post123348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you're in the Bush of Ghosts, where animal ghosts are a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saving me from making an &quot;All Dogs Go To Heaven&quot; joke. Y'all are probably too young for that, anyway.<br /> <br /> Just put the final touches on the outline of the Spectres chapter. So, yes, that's a thing. Risen I'm still futzing with. As opposed to the Riesen, which are the ghosts of chocolate caramel candies, which will appear in a later supplement.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy Out<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T01:39:19-07:00","id":124348,"title":"","content":"Hello Deadguy,<br /> <br /> So... about those Necroonauts... Any info? Or like Sorcerers they are out there for the chop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:36:27-07:00","id":124377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=124322#post124322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for saving me from making an &quot;All Dogs Go To Heaven&quot; joke. Y'all are probably too young for that, anyway.<br /> <br /> Just put the final touches on the outline of the Spectres chapter. So, yes, that's a thing. Risen I'm still futzing with. As opposed to the Riesen, which are the ghosts of chocolate caramel candies, which will appear in a later supplement.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy Out<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>ooo! I <i>loved</i> All Dogs. More kids' movies should be that good. And dark. Fairy dust is awesome, but sometimes sewers are too.<br /> <br /> Will there be a quicker-starter or simple intro adventure for the newest iteration of Wraith? I'm as much looking forward to introducing friends to Wraith as I am to seeing the new book. A ready to play intro would be super handy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:53:43-07:00","id":124645,"title":"","content":"why did i had a vision of Wraith Animals and Wraith dinosaurs being rided WW2 ghosts to fight the spectres......Someone do a metal albumcover with that!!<br /> <br /> Now being a bit more serious, How an spectre is born.. What i mean is, i know humans have great and terryfing ideas...but, do humans create the spectres, giving them shape and apparience, or does the oblivion creates them directly on looks and apparience?<br /> <br /> What i ask is, i seen some ghost stories involving demon like creatures and horryfing ghosts...so i wanted to know, how much of human input its on their creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T06:21:54-07:00","id":125757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=124645#post124645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now being a bit more serious, How an spectre is born.. What i mean is, i know humans have great and terryfing ideas...but, do humans create the spectres, giving them shape and apparience, or does the oblivion creates them directly on looks and apparience?</div> </div> </div> </div>What now? This is an odd question.. Well Spectres are &quot;born&quot; either when a truly wicked person dies and leaves an equally wicked Ghost, that ghost is the Spectre, or a normal human suffers an especially painful and horrific death and leaves a ghost behind. The third way is that a person dies and becomes a Wraith and in time his shadow slowly gains power and ends up usurping the shared Corpus permanently pushing the Psyche to be little whispering voice in the back of his head.<br /> <br /> So I guess yes humans create Spectres just as they create Wraiths, after all the main difference between the two ghosts is who is in control and who is just on for the ride Shadow or Psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:17:39-07:00","id":126098,"title":"","content":"what i mean was, can a place with heavy bad energy (like a torture chamber) feed of this bad mojo and create its own spectres based on those bad experiences. or can a persons trauma take form and become an spectre?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/