would Risen/Human work.<br /> <br /> and i mean on sensations, ectoplasm and all the gooey fanfic worth details","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T23:03:45-07:00","id":126477,"title":"","content":"Wraith sex? I would say it works badly. Meaning, either a Wraith doesn't have the natural desire for sex at all, or it desires degrading, painful or depraved sex as part of its reason for continued existence as a Wraith. I'd say some Spectres feed off the negative reactions others get from its sexual deviance, and act as really bad sexual predators. Most Wraiths won't have any such motivations at all - they do not have hormones, so any sex drive should be linked to the reason for a Wraith's unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T23:54:46-07:00","id":126500,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My two oboli on wraith loven\u2019:<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s the carnal act that offers gratification, but more the emotion behind the faux coupling. A Mortwight of the Alex DeLarge school of philosophy would have a very\u2026interesting\u2026idea of what constitutes \u2018intimacy.\u2019 On the other hand, a husband and wife who crossed over at the same time (perhaps both dying in an automobile accident or some such) might find just as much gratification in snuggling their ectoplasmic bodies together in the comfort of their Haunt. Or they might try to be ol\u2019 fashioned, Skinlands style, but I think the overall effect (insofar as the characters\u2019 emotional state) would be the same. Think of the Passions that drive the characters; I think that\u2019s how their ideas of intimacy \u2013 in regards to the sort of coital gratification that meatbags get \u2013 would manifest.<br /> <br /> Again, just throwing my opinion out there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T06:02:12-07:00","id":128896,"title":"","content":"re: Wraith Sex<br /> <br /> Passions, Passions, Passions. If you've got a Passion that involves your ectoplasmic snugglebunny, and they have one for you, well, you'll do just fine. <br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T06:03:35-07:00","id":128897,"title":"","content":"In other news....<br /> <br /> The first workable draft of the outline for Wraith 20 has been turned in to Onyx Path. I expect we'll go through some revisions, as right now the book is A)rather large and B)still manages to not include absolutely everything I wanted (it's been 15 years since I estimated word counts. I may be rusty). But, my friends, we are on our way.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T08:53:14-07:00","id":128999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=114439#post114439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the devil...Will we see Carpenter on the anniversary book?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=114712#post114712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends if Charlie Bates is nice to me in the next few months. Carpenter was actually his PC in the in-house Wraith 2nd playtest campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich made the mistake of telling me about this forum, so hello!<br /> <br /> For the record: I've always been nothing but a gentleman toward Deadguy, and anyone who says otherwise is a liar and a scoundrel. Carpenter survived a hack-y fiction trilogy* AND being stuck in fetish gear in two different video games; he deserves an encore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bates<br /> <br /> <i>*Yes, I wrote it\u2014that's how I know it was hack-y! Although, now that you mention it \u2026is it too early to start lobbying for a stretch goal of a Carpenter fiction series?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:11:11-07:00","id":129505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bates</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=128999#post128999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record: I've always been nothing but a gentleman toward Deadguy, and anyone who says otherwise is a liar and a scoundrel. Carpenter survived a hack-y fiction trilogy* AND being stuck in fetish gear in two different video games; he deserves an encore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say, sir, we are all liars and scoundrels here, and anyone who claims otherwise is... wait. I had something good for this.<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:21:47-07:00","id":129515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bates</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=128999#post128999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rich made the mistake of telling me about this forum, so hello!<br /> <br /> For the record: I've always been nothing but a gentleman toward Deadguy, and anyone who says otherwise is a liar and a scoundrel. Carpenter survived a hack-y fiction trilogy* AND being stuck in fetish gear in two different video games; he deserves an encore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bates<br /> <br /> <i>*Yes, I wrote it\u2014that's how I know it was hack-y! Although, now that you mention it \u2026is it too early to start lobbying for a stretch goal of a Carpenter fiction series?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mr Bates....its my honour to say that my players officially hate Carpenter, they Know they cant get rid of him, he is their walking nightmare who now wishes nothing else but power and retribution.....Thank you, any messages for my players?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T02:01:19-07:00","id":129725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=129515#post129515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr Bates....its my honour to say that my players officially hate Carpenter, they Know they cant get rid of him, he is their walking nightmare who now wishes nothing else but power and retribution.....Thank you, any messages for my players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey; just Bates is fine (Mr Bates is that dude from <i>Downton Abbey</i>\u2026). <br /> <br /> For your players; let's see\u2026<ul><li>Good news? Carpenter is far from omnipotent\u2014there's plenty of dudes more powerful than he.</li> <li>Bad news? He's a mean bastard who's elevated cunning to an art form.</li> </ul>(I've mentioned this before, but in the original <i>Wraith</i> playtest, I built him using standard starting points for a Spectre, and he almost took down the entire group of PCs single-handedly in one session.* He's learned a bit since then.)<br /> <br /> Carpenter was out for retribution, sure, and he's not above being petty and vengeful. But his <i>raison d'etre</i> is survival and control. Power is simply a means to an end.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nice(?) to hear that he's taken on a life (ha!) of his own in peoples' games.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bates<br /> <br /> <i>*I'm more proud of that than I should be.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T13:01:26-07:00","id":130093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bates</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=129725#post129725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey; just Bates is fine (Mr Bates is that dude from <i>Downton Abbey</i>\u2026).<br /> <br /> For your players; let's see\u2026<ul><li>Good news? Carpenter is far from omnipotent\u2014there's plenty of dudes more powerful than he.</li> <li>Bad news? He's a mean bastard who's elevated cunning to an art form.</li> </ul><br /> (I've mentioned this before, but in the original <i>Wraith</i> playtest, I built him using standard starting points for a Spectre, and he almost took down the entire group of PCs single-handedly in one session.* He's learned a bit since then.)<br /> <br /> Carpenter was out for retribution, sure, and he's not above being petty and vengeful. But his <i>raison d'etre</i> is survival and control. Power is simply a means to an end.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nice(?) to hear that he's taken on a life (ha!) of his own in peoples' games.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bates<br /> <br /> <i>*I'm more proud of that than I should be.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Any chances to elaborate on What happend on that game, how did it played out?. Also, did you based Carpenter off any existing character? as for his mannerism, way to talk or such? how do you picture him. who could play him on a movie or which character from comics, books, tv or movies could be a good carpenter a like ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:18:51-07:00","id":132285,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to have a Haunt that is still in the living world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T10:55:56-07:00","id":134048,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> What wonderful news that you've submitted the draft for Wraith 20! I hope that if your word count is too high, as you mentioned, the extra stuff gets released as stretch goals or supplements! They can always make the pictures smaller to give space for more text! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you so much for being here with us and answering our questions. Since I am a huge Wraith fan, I am probably more focused on what was missing, meaning from the full treatment since Wraith ended early, than others who are using it more as a crossover to supplement their love of other games, which I would think is limited only to the creativity and imagination of the storyteller. I do hope that we get to see many new details in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> One day I wish there could be a Dark Ages Wraith, the way there was for the other lines! Please! Please! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Quick seem to glow to a wraith, but how does a wraith using embody look to them?<br /> <br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T12:20:28-07:00","id":134186,"title":"","content":"Pitching in my hopes for Dark Ages Wraith (or better yet, a setting set before the Third Great Maelstrom!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T10:54:31-07:00","id":135527,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy!<br /> <br /> I third the hopes for a Dark Ages Wraith, and I also second Khaleesi in the wish for the focus of WtO20 to be on what is missing versus anything else. (And for me the underworld versus the world of the Quick.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is awesome news! Will we get our own forum soon?<br /> <br /> Gratzie!<br /> <br /> Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T19:55:26-07:00","id":136133,"title":"","content":"I dont know or dont remember if any book tackles it..but what about insanity?<br /> i mean, what happend when someone with mental derangements dies? whats up with his shadow and such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T21:35:19-07:00","id":136180,"title":"","content":"@Crowley<br /> <br /> It's in the Core Rulebook. The Hierarchy even has the Penitent Legion which are victims of Madness. If you are not a member of the Hierarchy it's business as usual for the insane in whether Heretic, Renegade or Free Wraith. This might be good for another thread since it's things that are already available to us in the books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","user":"Khaleesi","date":". 05-14-2014, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:46:12-07:00","id":136292,"title":"","content":"Death via depression, however, falls under the Silent Legion, the victims of despair. Yes, there are clashes between Penitent and Silent over the Silent's existence; the Penitent want to claim the Silent as theirs, which the Silent don't want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T22:50:01-07:00","id":138980,"title":"","content":"I was doing some research and i found out that Himmer is in fact a Vampire and he is still kicking around (sort of)...Woudnt that like..make riots on stygia in order for someone to get him and finish him?<br /> <br /> Do the wraith archives got this sort of information?.<br /> <br /> Also, Are any laws involving Wraiths and The Living? for example: Wraiths are not allowed to commit acts of vengeance against a mortal or stuff like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T23:39:39-07:00","id":139045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=138980#post138980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Are any laws involving Wraiths and The Living? for example: Wraiths are not allowed to commit acts of vengeance against a mortal or stuff like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Charon's dictum mortuum prohibits interaction between the living and the dead, save for the Deathlords and those they authorise (in large part because of the capacity for wraithly abuse of the living).<br /> <br /> As you might guess, that doesn't sit well with a lot of wraiths. (Hell, even parts of the Hierarchy turn a blind eye to breaches in the right circumstances.)<br /> <br /> ...Crowley, have you read any of the Wraith books? Because the dictum mortuum is a major part of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T04:41:12-07:00","id":139194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=139045#post139045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charon's dictum mortuum prohibits interaction between the living and the dead, save for the Deathlords and those they authorise (in large part because of the capacity for wraithly abuse of the living).<br /> <br /> As you might guess, that doesn't sit well with a lot of wraiths. (Hell, even parts of the Hierarchy turn a blind eye to breaches in the right circumstances.)<br /> <br /> ...Crowley, have you read any of the Wraith books? Because the dictum mortuum is a major part of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>i did, i cant remember it fully though, must re read it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:53:09-07:00","id":139265,"title":"","content":"The Dictum Mortuum seems like a lot of the Masquerade or most HR Departments... It exists as a way to punish people when authority wants to exercise its muscles. There's pretty much no way to have NO interaction with the living/mortals unless you hie off to Stygia or similar parts. There are whole Arcanoi that do nothing but affect the living. There are more that have some affect if used on mortals. Wraiths need to get Pathos, which means hanging around a Userer or, much less costly, hang around the living. If the wraith does anything to prompt the emotion he's jonesing for, BAM! violation. If the Hierarch of the Iron Legion wants that nifty bauble, she could just look at it longingly or she could coerce some living stooge to have strong feelings about it (Keening a la Pavlov) then use Outrage to smash it. (Do it right and you'll get a good jolt of Pathos off the destruction... time it just right so she thinks SHE destroyed it. Violation? I doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T11:08:51-07:00","id":139562,"title":"","content":"Himmler being a vampire is exclusive to the <b>Vampire</b> setting; officially, there is no mention of it in the <b>Wraith</b> canon. Unlike nWoD, the cWoD lines were (are) their own separate, discrete worlds.<br /> <br /> Check out <i>Charnel Houses of Europe: Ths Shoah</i> for more information (and because it's one of the best role-playing books ever written, for any game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T11:35:51-07:00","id":139603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=139562#post139562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Himmler being a vampire is exclusive to the <b>Vampire</b> setting; officially, there is no mention of it in the <b>Wraith</b> canon. Unlike nWoD, the cWoD lines were (are) their own separate, discrete worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... at some points. The cWOD went all over the place on the question of whether they shared the same setting or not.<br /> <br /> Himmler, meanwhile, was quietly ignored as Vampire went on, as was a fair bit of stuff from the early years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:24:44-07:00","id":140264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=139562#post139562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unlike nWoD, the cWoD lines were (are) their own separate, discrete worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say I disagree completely. For easy reference see Tremere/Order of Hermes, Giovanni/Wraiths, Setites/Silent Striders, Fianna/Changelings, Sluagh/Wraiths and even more so the Keremet/Wraith etc there are countless examples. Also the old adds for Wraith found in CtD books explicitly mention the possibility of Changeling murdered with Cold Iron to become a Wraith and continue the tale that way. Oh and there was this Vampire city within the Tempest until it was nuked by the Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> They all exists in the same world or there is no internal consistency to speak of. The difference between nWoD and cWoD in this regard is that nWoD has easier crossovers mechanically as all lines share certain mechanical facts and if you look into nWoD forums there are similar disagreements on whether or not the lines share the same world. In the end nothing has changes in this regard. And considering how often these debates pop up it's likely nothing will ever change in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T00:10:58-07:00","id":140306,"title":"","content":"Can we... not re-litigate the &quot;cWOD, one world or many&quot; thing? Because the answer both. The original intent was separate worlds, but that got scrapped fairly early as something exclusive, but it was never scrapped entirely. So some books kept going with that base assumption, others treated the cWOD as one massive convoluted world, and others tried to do both.<br /> <br /> Lets get back to waiting for answers to questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T01:36:34-07:00","id":141370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=130093#post130093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chances to elaborate on What happend on that game, how did it played out?. Also, did you based Carpenter off any existing character? as for his mannerism, way to talk or such? how do you picture him. who could play him on a movie or which character from comics, books, tv or movies could be a good carpenter a like ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy. I'll keep it brief, as I don't want to hijack the thread \u2014 or go down a whole &quot;tell me about your character&quot; rabbit hole.<br /> <br /> It was a long time ago so I forget exact events, but I do recall that neither the other players nor characters knew that Carpenter was a Spectre. Anyway, the session involved him leading them someplace that was ostensibly important to their mission. Really, he was calling in a mess o' Spectres while he kept them distracted. Much of this was regular ol' roleplaying, supported by judicious use of Intimation and Mnemosynis. It was going surprisingly well (for Carpenter) \u2014 even the other players weren't quite aware for quite a while what he was doing, till someone finally used some power (Lifesight?) to scan Carpenter and realize what he was. After a very ugly 4-on-1 fight, Carpenter was finally forced to flee since the other Spectres hadn't arrived yet. <br /> <br /> Carpenter was based off one of my old D&amp;D characters from years earlier. His genesis came from a whole thing with how the game was set up and how all the characters were introduced in-game. The gist is that I was burned out on the genre and had literally no idea what to play, so his personality emerged full-blown directly from my subconscious.*<br /> <br /> Some other Carpenter-like characters you can use as a guide? Let's see\u2026 guys like John Constantine, Keyser S\u00f6ze, and Petyr Baelish come from a similar mold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>*Bit of gamer trivia: That D&amp;D character? &quot;Carpenter&quot; was simply an alias. Likewise with &quot;Dennis Maxwell&quot; in the World of Darkness. His real name? No idea, to this day. Yes, the character that I made up, I do not know his real name. I expect a psychologist would have fun digging into that\u2026</i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:08:37-07:00","id":144168,"title":"","content":"Right. First, the news: I've started assigning sections to specific authors. I think you'll be pleased with some of the familiar faces who are coming back to the fold for this, and there are some very talented new writers climbing on board the Midnight Express as well. So, all kinds of happy about that.<br /> <br /> Second: Charlie is perhaps understating how perfectly flummoxed he had the rest of that Circle. And he maintained a perfect poker face while doing it. Never play cards with Charlie Bates.<br /> <br /> Third: Officially, CHoE superseded Berlin by Night in the greater WoD continuity. My stance in doing CHoE was, and is, that it was disingenuous of us to talk about how we were making games for mature minds without tackling the consequences of that head on, as there was a big hole in certain parts of WoD continuity that pretty much coincided with WW2. So I proposed filling that gap, and I made it clear that we weren't going to be blaming the Holocaust on vampires or werewolves or anyone else - that there was plenty of evil perpetrated by human beings to go around, even in the WoD. So vampire Himmler is, IMHO, hors d'continuity, and should stay that way. <br /> <br /> Fourth: What's an obolus worth? There will be a slight overhaul in the Stygian economy coming down the pike. In the intervening years between Wraith 2nd and now, I had the good fortune to marry someone who's professionally trained in economics and statistics. I will be asking her a lot of questions.<br /> <br /> Fifth: Nobody's riding a wraith dinosaur but me, you hear?<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:23:25-07:00","id":144216,"title":"","content":"Always a pleasure to hear from you, Dansky. Two questions; what's your forum icon (that Stygian key thing), and do you have any say in who will be doing art for Wraith20? Wraith had a potent visual aesthetic that I'd hate to not see make a proper return; Guy Davis' work in particular did a lot for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:06:30-07:00","id":144574,"title":"","content":"on my game of wraith, its very important for the players and for the wraiths in general to remind themselves how was to be alive (by eating rotten food and such). i wanted to know, hows the entertaiment in stygia?, do we have wraiths doing plays on famous movies? do we have movies at all? (Yes, i want my wraith James Dean playing as the Joker in a Wraith Rendition of the Dark Knight xD). How important are Shrinks in a world where everyone is dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:11:35-07:00","id":144583,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Deadguy Dansky,<br /> <br /> Thank you for the terrific update!<br /> <br /> 1) Will you be contacting everyone who turned in a writing submission for Wraith? Even if its a sad little rejection?<br /> 2) I'll at my query regarding who are the artists for Wraith20? One my favorite artists, who would be great for Wraith, though I don't think in the opting are Amano Yoshitaka and Ayami Kojima<br /> <br /> Khaleesi<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. I don't know about wraith dinosaurs, but how about dragons? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> j/k","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:33:18-07:00","id":144595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=144574#post144574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on my game of wraith, its very important for the players and for the wraiths in general to remind themselves how was to be alive (by eating rotten food and such). i wanted to know, hows the entertaiment in stygia?, do we have wraiths doing plays on famous movies? do we have movies at all? (Yes, i want my wraith James Dean playing as the Joker in a Wraith Rendition of the Dark Knight xD). How important are Shrinks in a world where everyone is dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there're the Chanteurs and the Sandmen - which is to say, music and dreams. Notably, the Sandmen have the power to enter dreams, shape dreams, and bring other wraiths along. If they want to turn a dream into a movie reenactment, it's within their capabilities.<br /> <br /> As for how important shrinks are... well, pretty much _every_ wraith needs help with their dark sides, their Shadows, and the Pardoners' Guild offers a variety of ways to deal with it - psychoanalysis, confession, physical punishment...<br /> <br /> (Wraiths from the Yellow Springs prefer confronting their Shadows themselves, with the Way of the Soul Arcanos.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:03:48-07:00","id":145110,"title":"","content":"Hey, folks - just dropping in quickly. Got a double fistful of editing to do tonight on Lillian Cohen-Moore's excellent novel Guidebook to the Village By the Sea, which IMHO is pretty darn Wraithy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on to the questions:<br /> <br /> 1-Artists - I don't have any say on the artists in the book, though I can bat my eyes at Rich Thomas winsomely and make requests. Honestly, we haven't even started discussions on that yet.<br /> However, if you want to see who a couple of my favorite Wraith artists are, there's a profile that Polygon ran of me a few months back that featured a few pictures of my home office, and you might recognize some of the pieces hanging on the walls...<br /> <br /> 2-The icon is the Great Key of Stygia. I happen to have a physical copy of it hanging from my office ceiling. True story - the last time I took a picture of it, I got orbs like crazy, and weird streaks of light in the shot. Now, I don't believe orbs are ghosts and I don't think my office is haunted, but....Wraith curse, anyone?<br /> <br /> 3-Entertainment is Stygia is, in a word, awe-inspiring. Imagine Shakespeare performed by the ghosts of the actors who were in Shakespeare's original theatrical company. Imagine a concert where The Lizard King, Mama Cass, Elvis and Freddie Mercury performed together. (Not Cobain, though. He had an unfortunate Castigation incident a while back.) Of course, that's if you're in the sort of social circles where that kind of stuff is available...<br /> <br /> 4-Writing staff - we are a long way from final on this. Right now I'm matching up certain specific writers from Ye Olde Days with sections I had them in mind for when this process started, but we ain't close to done yet.<br /> <br /> 5-Recommended reading for Wraithy folks: Steve Rasnic Tem's Deadfall Hotel. 'Cause it's creepy and very well written, and Steve is a mensch who owns the coolest author signing pen I've ever seen. If folks are interested, I'll be posting more of my favorite ghost stories on occasion. Some of these are Wraith inspiration, some are just things that I found worthwhile to read. Feel free to ignore or not as desired. <br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T20:12:24-07:00","id":145193,"title":"","content":"Ok...you been mentioning cobain here and there....Whats going on there? or, do we have to wait for the book?<br /> <br /> P.S: was checking tvtropes on Wraith the oblivion. found this one among others<br /> <br /> &quot;<ul><li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FanNickname\" target=\"_blank\">Fan Nickname</a>: &quot;The Big Grey Book of Depressing&quot;, because of its less than cheery subject matter, and White Wolf's decision to print the books in grey ink on grey paper.&quot;</li> </ul><br /> Any thoughts on that?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/WraithTheOblivion\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...ithTheOblivion</a> (if you havent checked the link)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 05-22-2014, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T07:27:00-07:00","id":145645,"title":"","content":"It cracks me up. Though on the W:tO mailing list, we always called it &quot;The Beast&quot;<br /> <br /> And it's better than the informal nickname the first printing of Wraith 1st ed had: &quot;Noseroids&quot;.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:10:50-07:00","id":146372,"title":"","content":"How was Wraith born? i mean, how did it came to be. how was it made<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_TPFgRP0JIY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_TPFgRP0JIY</a> How i meet your Wraith.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T13:50:09-07:00","id":147135,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in here to say I'm glad you're back and that Wr20 is going ahead. It was always my favorite CWoD line. I can't wait to go along for this ride and see what you've got in store for us. I still have my entire Wraith book collection and those books have provided me with some of the best reading (and re-reading) and gaming experiences I've ever had. So thanks, for everything past and for what is to come!<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> An old fan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3098-theblockknight","name":"TheBlockKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T14:46:50-07:00","id":150815,"title":"","content":"I loved the rules for relic ships between Wraith the Great War and Blood Dimmed Tides. Any chance a streamlined version of those making it into the 20th anniversary edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T09:12:42-07:00","id":151345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://f