"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T15:18:03-07:00","id":168297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=168033#post168033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mr. D:<br /> <br /> It seems most of the Dark Kingdoms have their seats of power on islands nestled in the Tempest: Is the Dark Kingdom of Wire the only Kingdom that exists solely in the Shadowlands?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dark Kingdom of Wire isn't a proper Dark Kingdom. It's technically an independent little bit within Stygian territory with a cruel name attached to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T15:30:09-07:00","id":168309,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=168297#post168297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Kingdom of Wire isn't a proper Dark Kingdom. It's technically an independent little bit within Stygian territory with a cruel name attached to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more curious if other Dark Kingdoms exist without a Tempest-centric \u2018capital.\u2019 Basically, do you need a tree-house before you can start a club? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T16:31:44-07:00","id":168367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=168155#post168155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i meant more thant that, i mean festivals and such whitin stygia</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, then probably about the same way the Nazis &quot;celebrated&quot; Passover. With ruthless jackbooted oppression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T08:09:25-07:00","id":169784,"title":"","content":"Super excited for Wraith20. Looks like great things in the works. I was excited when Onyx Path launched the T-shirt store, and saw on a wiki that there was a Wraith T-shirt made at one point, but can't find an image of it. Do you have one? or know what the art on that thing looked like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2732-darprime","name":"DarPrime","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:46:22-07:00","id":169960,"title":"","content":"Will there anything on playing as a Legionnaire in Wraith 20th or will it be in the Great War 2.0?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:20:51-07:00","id":170844,"title":"","content":"@DarPrime (Is that a bit like Zor Prime?) There are two t-shirts for Wraith.<br /> <br /> A black T-shirt with a rectangular image in portrait. The border is the same as from the character sheets. It has two lines of text below the top border saying &quot;Wraith The Oblivion&quot;. Below is an Image of what looks like a specter on one side and to the right of the image text that reads: &quot;Death is a rite of passage marking the end of one journey and the beginning of another the cycle of fear isn't over when you die. It simply begins again. Death is the revelation of Oblivion.&quot; The text is white.<br /> <br /> The white T-Shirt has on the back &quot;Wraith the Oblivion&quot; With &quot;Wraith&quot; in Gold text and &quot;The Oblivion in black.&quot; Underneath is the key. On front side: 3/4 Image from the mini-poster of winged person holding a book with arms crossed over it, face is smudged out. Text below reads &quot;There is a storm that's always screaming under the skin of the world, sometimes it comes looking for you...&quot; The key image is beneath<br /> <br /> Hope this helps! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:24:29-07:00","id":170861,"title":"","content":"Dear Real DeadGuy,<br /> <br /> A quick question please. Would something like jumping over a small wall and using enshroud count as one or two actions? Can you enshroud while jumping over the wall?<br /> <br /> Thanks so much!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T10:10:32-07:00","id":171742,"title":"","content":"Grim Fandango is brilliant, and it was one of my main creative inspirations when I got into working in videogames. <br /> <br /> Festivals for the dead, among other things, offer an awful lot of emotional energy directed towards the dead. There just might be some rituals developed around that...<br /> <br /> I'd do a dicepool split for the jump/enshroud, but the jump should be ridiculously low difficulty. <br /> <br /> The Dark Kingdoms are built on a combination of dominant cultural paradigm, ability to find &amp; hold territory in the Underworld, and occasional bits of plain luck. The major powers have secured major real estate; that's not to say there aren't outposts of wraiths who came out of a different culture who interact with the afterlife in their own way, trying to carve out their own territory here and there. Of course, that sort of existence isn't likely to make them friendly to outsiders. As for the Dark Kingdom of Wire, that name is bitterly ironic, and the entity it describes exists within Stygia's borders.<br /> <br /> I still have one of the old white Wraith t-shirts. At one point we were talking about doing a black long-sleeve, but it never happened. I think there was a black short-sleeve shirt that had John Cobb art on it back in the early days of the game, but that's ancient history and my brain is fluffy.<br /> <br /> And on a completely unrelated note: Over the past year, I've had people send me pictures of themselves doing terrible things to my latest novel, VAPORWARE. You can find the greatest hits at <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WnbOSGSarYg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WnbOSGSarYg</a>. Be afraid. Be very afraid.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T14:07:51-07:00","id":172007,"title":"","content":"i was wondering, what are the limits of soulforging. i mean, i imagine you CANT BUILD A MOTHERFUCKING TANK OUT OF ONE SOUL. but can you make a whole book out of one wraith or would you have to make each page separately? and why do i have this creepy idea of legos made of soulforge.... The lego movie will never be the same<br /> <br /> P.S Will you ever writte a campaing about Not findind Bigfoot in the underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 06-17-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T21:22:00-07:00","id":172352,"title":"","content":"I'm keeping my cryptozoology and my Wraith obsessions separate :-)<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:15:33-07:00","id":173414,"title":"","content":"Hi RealDeadguy! I have a question about using Muse. It affects the Quick and the Restless, but can you use it through the Shroud? Is it an area effect? It says difficulty is the highest WP but how many can it effect? Looking forward to all your updates! Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","user":"Katrina","date":". 06-19-2014, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T08:47:34-07:00","id":175271,"title":"","content":"Hey Deadguy!<br /> <br /> I have some questions that were born out of old arguements with Troupemates I was hoping you could resolve:<br /> <br /> 1) Are the clothes a Wraith originally appears in the shadowlands in part of her corpus (and thus, theoretically, unremovable without Moliate) or are they relics?<br /> <br /> B) What degree of awareness, if any, does an Embodied or Risen Wraith retain of the underwold while in the Skinlands? Can they see/ hear back accross the shroud?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> Looking forward to the new book! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/79-alexisvalarr","name":"alexisvalarr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar79_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:31:45-07:00","id":176286,"title":"","content":"This may have been already asked: what's the likelihood of Jade and Dark Arcanoi getting markings like the standard ones? We always used the ones the unofficial ones that Grabowski and Harviainen came up with, but it'd be neat if there were official ones! Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T16:06:24-07:00","id":176495,"title":"","content":"I was wondering...well...more of a suggestion.<br /> I talked to many of my friends who play and DM and i was wondering if is possible to have a &quot;The Quick&quot; or &quot;The Flesh.&quot; character sheet, a sheet meant for a prelude, with stats like Hopes: Goals and Favorite Things but mainly for the Alive character","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T17:33:49-07:00","id":176586,"title":"","content":"Concerning all the Dark Kingdoms, I've noticed that all of them are defined in relation to Stygia. Each has their own version of the nature of the soul with certain Arcanoi that manifest because of that worldview. It seems they all have their own thing PLUS Stygia. Jade has their own five arcanoi, the Ivory has Behest, and Swar has its own. The Ivory wraith also manifest with four parts to their soul, and the Creole wraith have the potential to have 10 dot fetters. What metaphysical eccentricities does the Stygian wraith have because of the fundamental nature of the soul for the Dark Kingdom of Iron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T18:47:58-07:00","id":176629,"title":"","content":"@Crowley - It's already addressed in &quot;The Great War&quot;. See page 102. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:01:56-07:00","id":176652,"title":"","content":"@Old Rusty Pipe: Yeah that would be interesting to see the Dark Kingdom of Iron to get some unique traits of their own though I have no idea what that could possibly be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T09:54:03-07:00","id":178038,"title":"","content":"I have interviewed Richard for Twisted Tales. Although it is possibly redundant to those in this thread, as you can ask him your own questions directly, some of you may find it interesting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://twistedtalesevents.blogspot.co.uk/2014/06/richard-dansky-interviewed-by-david.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://twistedtalesevents.blogspot.co.uk/2014/06/richard-dansky-interviewed-by-david.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://twistedtalesevents.blogspot.co.uk/2014/06/richard-dansky-interviewed-by-david.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://twistedtalesevents.blogspot.co.uk/2014/06/richard-dansky-interviewed-by-david.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>Wraith: The Oblivion</i> 20th Anniversary Edition is the World of Darkness project I am most looking forward to from Onyx Path, so I hope that this will help raise awareness in advance of the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3048-aaron-boone","name":"Aaron Boone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T06:19:00-07:00","id":181850,"title":"","content":"Been re-reading my WtO and I've been wondering something Deadguy, a couple things actually.<br /> <br /> 1) Out of all the WtO material you've worked on, what's the material you're most proud of?<br /> <br /> 2) And is there any material that looking back on it you think could have been done better and you're not so proud of?<br /> <br /> 3) Finally is there Wraith material that you wished you had gotten a chance to do and explore but never got to because the line ended early?<br /> <br /> Also while I love Carpenter there is one Wraith character I would love to see more in Wr20, Erik. Out of all the signature characters in the OWoD he's easily been my favorite and I loved that the last scene of WtO is him finally meeting the girl he's been chasing after all this time. So I would love to see another bit of Wraith fiction about him in Wr20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T13:22:31-07:00","id":182181,"title":"","content":"Dear RealDeadguy,<br /> <br /> I was wondering if Dreamcloak can be placed on someone else, either when it is constructed or can it be taken off and placed over someone else? Can you weave it around yourself and someone you are holding/touching? <br /> <br /> Looking forward to your response! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:49:43-07:00","id":184053,"title":"","content":"So today, I'm formally recruiting authors for Wraith 20 and assigning them chapters.<br /> <br /> It feels good.<br /> <br /> The Beast, it is back.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T17:42:12-07:00","id":184237,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=184053#post184053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So today, I'm formally recruiting authors for Wraith 20 and assigning them chapters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if only I had a decent portfolio\u2026<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T20:25:08-07:00","id":184354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=184053#post184053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So today, I'm formally recruiting authors for Wraith 20 and assigning them chapters.<br /> <br /> It feels good.<br /> <br /> The Beast, it is back.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy out</div> </div> </div> </div>The demon bunny from Monty Python?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:41:46-07:00","id":184514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=184237#post184237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Oh, if only I had a decent portfolio\u2026<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>if only i could writte in english...propely<br /> <br /> <br /> Now being serious. Any thoughts on Zdzis\u0142aw Beksi\u0144ski and how much did his art influenced the look of the Underworld, any other artists you recomend as a vision of &quot;Wraith&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 07-01-2014, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T22:53:19-07:00","id":186842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=184354#post184354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The demon bunny from Monty Python?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, no silly knees-bent running about advancing behaviors here.<br /> <br /> Back in the good old days of Wraith-L, the nickname for 2nd Edition was The Beast. It got this name because A)it was significantly longer in terms of word count than first edition and B)I spent an awful lot of time wrestling with it, and there were times when it wasn't sure which of us was going to come out on top.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me - I will cheerfully spill anecdotes from The Good Old Days, including behind the scenes looks at various books, etc. if people are curious. Just let me know.<br /> <br /> But back to business: The author roster is filling up and once folks are officially under contract, I'll start naming names. There will be some old friends, some fresh victims, and some interesting collaborations happening between various folks whose skills I think will complement each other wonderfully.<br /> <br /> So, strap in. Things are about to get intense.<br /> <br /> Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{