igh Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:40:02-07:00","id":193555,"title":"","content":"Will the new character sheet come with a death certificate as a option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:55:43-07:00","id":193738,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Possessed on that one, IMHO. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:21:43-07:00","id":194979,"title":"","content":"Question: why are international wraiths (i.e. those not from Stygian territory) 'built' differently, in terms of having makeups other than Psyche+Shadow? It's always bothered me a little that Europe and America has a fantastic invention with no basis in reality other than perhaps Jungian psychology, but then everyone else has different souls for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:52:36-07:00","id":195072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=193555#post193555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the new character sheet come with a death certificate as a option?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always download the one I have. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T23:53:58-07:00","id":195305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=194979#post194979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: why are international wraiths (i.e. those not from Stygian territory) 'built' differently, in terms of having makeups other than Psyche+Shadow? It's always bothered me a little that Europe and America has a fantastic invention with no basis in reality other than perhaps Jungian psychology, but then everyone else has different souls for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>In large part, it's cultural - Great War notes that wraiths from other Dark Kingdoms can only remain so long in Stygia before they come to identify with the Psyche/Shadow paradigm.<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking of it in terms of paradigms might be useful here: _that_ there's a division in a wraith is a given - a cosmological constant. What form that division takes is shaped by the dominant cultural paradigm of a Dark Kingdom. A wraith starts off in the paradigm of their culture of origin, but the longer they spend as part of another culture's paradigm, the more likely it is that they'll identify with that culture's paradigm.<br /> <br /> Why the writers decided to do it like that, I couldn't tell you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T23:46:20-07:00","id":196067,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy, When a wraith bleeds, what color is the plasm? Is the color different for Spectres? Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T14:43:29-07:00","id":197177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=184053#post184053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So today, I'm formally recruiting authors for Wraith 20 and assigning them chapters.<br /> <br /> It feels good.<br /> <br /> The Beast, it is back.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy out</div> </div> </div> </div>If only I were a skilled writer lol. These days its mostly technical though. I went ahead and I submitted for the open call a few months back and did an 'alternate reality' piece talked about most 6th Great Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> I would also love hearing stories about the creation of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T10:56:47-07:00","id":198052,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy!<br /> <br /> When a wraith uses Embody, Corpse or Slip the Lethan Bonds, can they still see into the world of the Restless and affect it? I was rereading this thread and and am curious about too about a question that was asked earlier, being is how does a wraith using embody look to other wraiths. The Quick glow, but an Embodied wraith would look...?<br /> <br /> Thanks so much! And another thing that would be cool would be symbols for the Spectre Arcanos! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T20:19:25-07:00","id":200675,"title":"","content":"Will this make up for our hearts being broken by Wraith being cancelled in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T20:27:47-07:00","id":200676,"title":"","content":"Deadguy, do you have a personal favorite Legion? (Nobody cares, but mine is the Silent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:06:46-07:00","id":200695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=200676#post200676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Nobody cares, but mine is the Silent).</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I care.<br /> I care deeply about anyone who cares about Stygia.<br /> You might say I have a\u2026Passion\u2026for Stygia.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:45:03-07:00","id":200730,"title":"","content":"I'm a Penitent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I have a thing for the Grim. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T22:43:41-07:00","id":201820,"title":"","content":"hey rich, i know youre a busy guy. but i was hoping you could check the thread &quot;Dark Corners of the Earth: Location Location Location.&quot; i showed the guys the historial background of my country and the Ghosts of the 73, maybe you could use that someday. if you dont mind.<br /> <br /> Also , your thoughts con The Devils Backbone (el espinazo del diablo). And what story and movie do you feel that represents Wraith and its Feel or that you can say &quot;yup, thats pretty much the game&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 07-22-2014, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T22:22:08-07:00","id":210874,"title":"","content":"You should get Wraith 20 because it is the one game that, taken away from the Stygian politics and the Great Maelstroms and all that, still forces you to develop those mundane relationships and roleplay with them. \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1738-charon","name":"Charon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T01:49:54-07:00","id":213284,"title":"","content":"Someone who knows a bit of (latin?)<br /> <br /> Is Dictum Mortuum pronounced (Dick-Tum More-Toom) or (Dick-Tum Mort-you-um)?<br /> <br /> In enforcing the Dictum, how much does the Hierarchy care about things like...<br /> <br /> -A wraith has used Keening to make a Quick happy. While a violation of the Dictum, there is no way for the quick to know that the emotion was foreign, unless it is particularly jarring. Even then, there is no reason to suspect a ghost is involved. Is a Hierarchy enforcer going to care?<br /> <br /> -What if a wraith more blatantly breaks the Dictum, but the Fog covers the wraith's tracks...<br /> <br /> -What if a wraith is caught on camera (say using Embody) but offers to destroy the evidence? Can the transgression be forgiven?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 07-30-2014, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T07:34:35-07:00","id":213555,"title":"","content":"All 3 cases are clear Dictum Mortuum violations and would be punished accordingly though in the first case the offender is a lot more likely to avoid the Forges than in the latter two. And naturally a lot is dependent upon the Hieararchs who caught him, how strictly do they interpret the law and could they use the violation as blackmail material against the Wraith in question, then again the Forges are always hungry for more....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T11:38:10-07:00","id":213787,"title":"","content":"Classical Latin or Church Latin? Which would they be using in Stygia?<br /> <br /> For Classical Latin (my bet), you can only make a reasonable stab. Using poetry is the way most historical linguists I know of go...<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> Dictum - DIHK tuhm (possibly dihk TOOM) <br /> Mortuum - MOAR too uhm or MOAR tyoo uhm (either/or)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T04:49:36-07:00","id":214548,"title":"","content":"What would it be in Church Latin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T08:22:17-07:00","id":214691,"title":"","content":"Hmmm..... let me backpedal a bit..... since the Empire lasted a long time....<br /> <br /> (And I've bothered to pull a few books on it, since it's been, dear Gods, over two decades since I was working towards a Classical Archaeology degree....)<br /> <br /> How about Church Latin = DIHK tuhm MOAR tyoo uhm<br /> Old Latin = deek TOOM MOAR too uhm<br /> <br /> Though the inflections on the later could change a bit, at least poetically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-31-2014, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T21:51:45-07:00","id":215542,"title":"","content":"Ah, much appreciated. I suspected that they both ended in an -um sound","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T22:36:04-07:00","id":217185,"title":"","content":"i was wondering, are there any drugs on the underworld? how do drug addicts wraith cope?, if a person dies while drunk or on drugs, is his wraith permanently high?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T23:14:03-07:00","id":217203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=217185#post217185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do drug addicts wraith cope?</div> </div> </div> </div>By learning Puppetry and Possessing drug users, or just normal people whom you subjugate to drugs but that's kinda dick move and much more costly than simply skinriding someone experiencing a high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T23:58:27-07:00","id":217244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=217185#post217185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i was wondering, are there any drugs on the underworld? how do drug addicts wraith cope?, if a person dies while drunk or on drugs, is his wraith permanently high?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The is also one rather well known wraith in Atlanta that often barters information for relic liquor. <br /> <br /> One way of acquiring said relic liquor is by using the Claim art of the Inhabit arcanos, and finding some means of destroying the liquor while the wraith is inhabiting the object. Like, for instance, having a friend with outrage knock it off a shelf in a liquor store.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T03:52:43-07:00","id":217321,"title":"","content":"There are totally too many Guilds (one each for each Arcanoi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so maybe they should be placed together in one big book along with lacking ones?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Dictum Mortuum pronounced (Dick-Tum More-Toom) or (Dick-Tum Mort-you-um)? </div> </div> </div>As a foreigner I am nearly sure it is Dick-Tum More-Toom cause my language (polish) is pronounciated in very similar way to latin and derives many words from it.<br /> Double &quot;u&quot; can be even said: Dick-Tum More-Too-Um. But no single &quot;y&quot; out there..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-03-2014, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T10:01:48-07:00","id":217481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=217321#post217321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are totally too many Guilds (one each for each Arcanoi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so maybe they should be placed together in one big book along with lacking ones?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As a foreigner I am nearly sure it is Dick-Tum More-Toom cause my language (polish) is pronounciated in very similar way to latin and derives many words from it.<br /> Double &quot;u&quot; can be even said: Dick-Tum More-Too-Um. But no single &quot;y&quot; out there..</div> </div> </div> </div>Just going off what was taught in higher level Latin classes designed for classicists and several classes in historical linguistics. <br /> <br /> In any case, it's just guesswork. Albeit good guesswork. The fact Romans wrote poems where the meter and certain rules(like elision) affected pronunciation helps a lot. Particularly of vowels. But vowel pronunciation is very slippery over a very short period of time. Particularly when you don't have TV or radio or recording media to slow such things down. (In any case, go listen to recordings of people talking from a recently as the start of the 20th Century and there are definite differences that are not due to persistent accents, idiom, grammar or vocabulary. If you want to see how fast sounds can diverge, spend some time places like Rhode Island or eastern Mass. Even today, literally every separate town has it's own pronunciation of words, particularly vowels.) <br /> <br /> Using modern Polish pronunciation as a guide to Ancient Roman pronunciation is probably not the most accurate way to go. Much like using modern English spelling for word pronunciation. It's been a long time since anyone said &quot;knife&quot; as &quot;kehnee FAY&quot;, knight as &quot;kehnigh it&quot; (with that &quot;gh&quot; actually sounding more like &quot;ch&quot; in the Scottish &quot;loch&quot;) or &quot;through&quot; as<br /> &quot;throwgh&quot; (same &quot;gh&quot; sound) instead of &quot;thru&quot;. Hells bells, we can't even tell a thorn from a &quot;y&quot;, hence all the &quot;Ye old inn&quot; etc. Which is really just &quot;The old inn&quot; using a letter that's no longer in the alphabet we learn in school that looks a lot like a &quot;y&quot;. <br /> <br /> Long and short of it, say Dictum Mortuum the way you want to. One pronunciation is going to be pretty common across a Necropolis, whether it's from the populace at large just reading the words and coming up with it, having it come down from Hierarchs who had to learn Latin in school the &quot;Weni, Widi, Wici&quot; way or some folks that learned the &quot;Vei, Vidi, Vichi&quot; of Church Latin, or a temporary visitor from Stygia who actually spoke Roman Latin....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T10:58:05-07:00","id":217526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=217321#post217321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are totally too many Guilds (one each for each Arcanoi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so maybe they should be placed together in one big book along with lacking ones?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As a foreigner I am nearly sure it is Dick-Tum More-Toom cause my language (polish) is pronounciated in very similar way to latin and derives many words from it.<br /> Double &quot;u&quot; can be even said: Dick-Tum More-Too-Um. But no single &quot;y&quot; out there..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where I live, people sometimes say the word &quot;mortuary&quot; as &quot;mort-you-airy&quot; or even &quot;more-choo-airy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T22:40:13-07:00","id":220762,"title":"","content":"When the rulebooks mention wraiths travelling, they usually suggest that a wraith would need to skinride a target for an extended period of time. Any reason why that would be necessary? Why not just... board a plane or stow away on a boat? Why skinride a target?<br /> <br /> Also, what is the difference between the Embody 4 art &quot;Life-in-Death&quot; and the Embody 5 art &quot;Materialize&quot;? Materialize seems to be pretty limited in scope. While, yes, it allows you to &quot;live again&quot; for a short while, its duration is extremely brief. (The span of 1 breath/Success, unless you are hanging out with a consort, then it lasts 1 hour/success. An odd amount of time, since usually storyteller games measure time in scenes, rather than hours.) Meanwhile Life-in-Death allows you to remain solid for a scene or more, presumably able to move, albeit with cold flesh and a distracted look on the wraith's face. It almost sounds like Embody 4 is more useful than Embody 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T11:04:52-07:00","id":221141,"title":"","content":"@Froggy711 <br /> <br /> <b>Travel: </b>You can multiple ways. Not every wraith has skinride. You can also travel in the Shadowlands to get wherever you want to be using Argos, etc. or even public transportation such as the Midnight Express, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ultimately you can be as creative as you like.<br /> <br /> <b>Embody: </b>You may want to refer to &quot;Wraith: The Great War&quot; that was published after the 2nd edition of the core rulebook. It has update for certain Arcanos. Level 5 Embody is <b>Slip the Lethan Bonds </b>and it lasts a single scene for each success then LIfe-in-Death, which as you note, is not terribly useful.<br /> <br /> <b>P.S.</b> These are great questions but maybe they should be in another thread as they are a bit general and not targeted to things only our Deadguy can answer for us! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hope this helps!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T11:05:12-07:00","id":221142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=220762#post220762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the rulebooks mention wraiths travelling, they usually suggest that a wraith would need to skinride a target for an extended period of time. Any reason why that would be necessary? Why not just... board a plane or stow away on a boat? Why skinride a target?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to ask myself the same question. I'm still not sure what the answer is, but I believe it has to do with 1. the fact that traveling often involves having to interact with Quickland doors, which would slowly fray the wraith's corpus, and 2. The fact that traveling often means crossing oceans, and oceans in the Shadowlands are really dangerous. They're vast, potentially thin-shrouded regions lacerated with nihils. All in all, I think one could simply stowaway on a plane or boat, but that skinriders have the advantage of being able to sit back inside a quick and enjoy a safe ride.<br /> <br /> Can anyone confirm this?<br /> <br /> Related to this point, I've been reading the Dark Kingdoms trilogy, by Richard Lee Byers, and the first fifty pages of the first book (which I highly recommend all wraith players read), establishes how wraiths could get around both in the Tempest and in Shadow. One character stows away in a taxi for a quick ride, for example. That series, but especially those first few chapters, are really evocative of the Wraith setting. The writer paid attention to details, and while his writing talents are a bit lacking when it comes to human reactions in moments of supernatural activity or extreme violence, investing some time into reading the first book will pay off for storytellers and players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 08-07-2014, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T00:25:07-07:00","id":221738,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khaleesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=221141#post221141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Froggy711<br /> <br /> <b>Travel: </b>You can multiple ways. Not every wraith has skinride. You can also travel in the Shadowlands to get wherever you want to be using Argos, etc. or even public transportation such as the Midnight Express, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ultimately you can be as creative as you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, but I was slightly baffled by passages like this one from Midnight Express:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As most characters will have limited means of transportation, the Midnight Express serves as an excellent way to travel between cities; even oceans may be crossed without the tedium of skinriding a mortal for prolonged periods. </div> </div> </div>It just seems odd to mention skinriding there, making it sound like it was necessary for traveling across the ocean. It made me wonder if there was something I didn't understand about travelling the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khaleesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=221141#post221141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Embody: </b>You may want to refer to &quot;Wraith: The Great War&quot; that was published after the 2nd edition of the core rulebook. It has update for certain Arcanos. Level 5 Embody is <b>Slip the Lethan Bonds </b>and it lasts a single scene for each success then LIfe-in-Death, which as you note, is not terribly useful.<br /> <br /> <b>P.S.</b> These are great questions but maybe they should be in another thread as they are a bit general and not targeted to things only our Deadguy can answer for us! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hope this helps!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi</div> </div> </div> </div>I will have to take a look at that... I wasn't aware the Great War had updates for the arcanoi... I just assumed they were slightly different during that time.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't mean to trouble the Deadguy with these questions. Mostly I just thought that maybe he could answer these questions, since the answers don't seem to be anywhere in the text. Also I am very excited about Wraith20 and want to see the thread continue and the conversation to go on. Maybe even bring his attention to some things that I have found puzzling about the game, so they might be cleared up when writing Wraith20!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T18:31:04-07:00","id":222656,"title":"","content":"Regarding wraiths crossing oceans; it's an obscure bit of fluff, but Blood-Dimmed Tides has bodies of water exist as solid material in the Shadowlands. A wraith could theoretically walk across the Pacific if he felt like it. Note that Argos or a relic vehicle is still needed for travel within the Tempest and Sea of Shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:42:29-07:00","id":223439,"title":"","content":"So sad! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just checked the Onyx Path Current Projects page and WtO20 is no longer listed as slotted for this year, 2014 (originally targeted for September), and while I understand production changes, it is now listed as &quot;On the horizon...&quot; <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/schedule</a><br /> <br /> No love for us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No respect for the dead.<br /> <br /> I'm going to go cry now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:57:28-07:00","id":223453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katrina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=223439#post223439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So sad! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just checked the Onyx Path Current Projects page and WtO20 is no longer listed as slotted for this year, 2014 (originally targeted for September), and while I understand production changes, it is now listed as &quot;On the horizon...&quot; <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/schedule</a><br /> <br /> No love for us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No respect for the dead.<br /> <br /> I'm going to go cry now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, &quot;on the horizon&quot; means they don't have a firm place on the schedule for it. Deadguy only started contracting writers about a month ago, so it was going to fall way out of their current schedule by any measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:40:50-07:00","id":223569,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>Ends of Empire </i>came out in \u201999.<br /> I\u2019ve waited 15 years to set foot in Stygia again; I\u2019m not stressing about one more year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also: <br /> I'm really fricken' old.<br /> /grumble <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:52:01-07:00","id":223579,"title":"","content":"Where are the shovels? We'll dig Wraith back up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladinde