9:51:44-08:00","id":308780,"title":"","content":"I was wondering, How do Death Rituals affect wraiths?.<br /> On some cultures, its normal to pour or to leave a bottle of beer within the casket or in the grave, some people leave light cigs over the gravestone. Do the wraiths &quot;Get&quot; those things as Items (not as fetters but as consumable items that can help them to release some Stress? ..or fuck that, wraiths are always stressed out.)<br /> <br /> And yes, i been wondering how do Drugs and Vices work on wraiths","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T01:43:24-08:00","id":308899,"title":"","content":"I think just as the two coins on the eyes everything burrowed with the character for sentimental reasons COULD become a relic.<br /> Don't know whats canon though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T07:20:05-08:00","id":309093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=308780#post308780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, How do Death Rituals affect wraiths?.<br /> On some cultures, its normal to pour or to leave a bottle of beer within the casket or in the grave, some people leave light cigs over the gravestone. Do the wraiths &quot;Get&quot; those things as Items (not as fetters but as consumable items that can help them to release some Stress? ..or fuck that, wraiths are always stressed out.)<br /> <br /> And yes, i been wondering how do Drugs and Vices work on wraiths</div> </div> </div> </div>I might make the call as an ST that important, significant to the character items left in the casket might go with them. A bottle of beer? Probably not. An unopened bottle of the character's favorite beer that was still in his fridge when he died and the mourners left there until the funeral just to save to put in the casket with him? That would be a Relic for him. Non-Relic item that comes across with him would be just a reflection of his favorite brand, especially if he was a &quot;couples of beers&quot; a night kind of guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:22:28-08:00","id":309225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=308780#post308780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, How do Death Rituals affect wraiths?.<br /> On some cultures, its normal to pour or to leave a bottle of beer within the casket or in the grave, some people leave light cigs over the gravestone. Do the wraiths &quot;Get&quot; those things as Items (not as fetters but as consumable items that can help them to release some Stress? ..or fuck that, wraiths are always stressed out.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Delicious, delicious Pathos. Relieves the stress of being dead and having nothing. Or, at least, the stress of not having Pathos.<br /> <br /> If it's a regular thing, take some Memorium. <br /> <br /> If it's something where they destroy it in a way that deliberately wastes it and they get no advantage over it, possibly the genesis of a minor Relic. But there would have to be a lot of emotion involved. <br /> <br /> Pouring out a 40 oz beer for a fallen homie would just generate Pathos. Making regular offerings, like say, old Egyptian tomb/temple style is Memorium (for more modern examples, see H.P. Lovecraft's or Edgar Allen Poe's graves). Ritually destroying a pot or bending/breaking a sword might get you a Relic (after the item in question is mostly gone from natural decay processes).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T13:45:15-08:00","id":309431,"title":"","content":"Redlines...have begun.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:37:12-08:00","id":309838,"title":"","content":"How many Wraiths were created while waiting for Wr20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:24:55-08:00","id":310930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=308780#post308780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, How do Death Rituals affect wraiths?.<br /> On some cultures, its normal to pour or to leave a bottle of beer within the casket or in the grave, some people leave light cigs over the gravestone. Do the wraiths &quot;Get&quot; those things as Items (not as fetters but as consumable items that can help them to release some Stress? ..or fuck that, wraiths are always stressed out.)<br /> <br /> And yes, i been wondering how do Drugs and Vices work on wraiths</div> </div> </div> </div>@Crowley - Regarding addictions, such as drugs, alcohol, etc. it would depend on if they are physical or psychological. If you don't have a body you cannot be physically addicted at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T09:12:03-08:00","id":318989,"title":"","content":"OK, just posted this over on the Wraith 20 FB page - here's the Official Deadguy Writing For Wraith 20 Playlist (In Progress)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gazpacho - Demon - Inspired by the true story of a demonic book left in a flat in Prague...if you believe that sort of thing.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Edison's Children - The F