the Maelstrom</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ephemeral Sun - Broken Door </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gillian Welch - Hell Among the Yearlings</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Goblin - Back to the Goblin</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Kevin Max and Adrian Belew - Raven Songs 101</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sandy Denny - &quot;Nothing More&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gosta Berlings Saga - Detta Har Hant</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.goear.com/listen/66d7913/glockenspiel-requiem-for-v-drew-richard\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.goear.com/.../glockenspiel-requiem-for-v-drew...</a> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.goear.com/listen/a80f542/obliteration-of-the-self-drew-richard\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.goear.com/.../obliteration-of-the-self-drew...</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.goear.com/listen/5e14d57/watchmen-rorscharch-journal-drew-richard\" target=\"_blank\">://www.goear.com/.../watchmen-rorscharch-journal-drew...</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.goear.com/listen/f86b2c0/the-heartbeat-of-insects-drew-richard\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.goear.com/.../the-heartbeat-of-insects-drew...</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.goear.com/listen/894a400/sad-strange-cello-escaflowne\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.goear.com/.../894.../sad-strange-cello-escaflowne</a>-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T21:15:25-08:00","id":319595,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#808080\">Ok Deadguy,<br /> <br /> I has questions!<br /> <br /> First, I bought WtO in college the week it arrived in the comic book store up from campus. I brought it home and proceeded to do No homework as I read well into the night. Then I laid it down, my eyes bloodshot and wearied from pouring over the illustrious tome - or is it tomb, turned off the light, and went to sleep still wondering why there wasn't any title on the cover. A couple hours later I woke up and rolled over, and jumped - the title was glowing in a ghostly green light! I was delighted even more!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">How can that be duplicated in the age of Print on Demand?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\">Second, the group I gamed with through out college was a small cabal of thespians for whom the Story Teller system offered regular workouts in direction, method acting, and comedy improv. We all read wraith. We all discussed wraith. Then we all decided that it was unsafe to play unless the ST was a licensed psychologist... Handing your alter ego's alter ego to someone who knows you to play against you is not a game we were willing to play without professional help. Now let us assume your current and ex, plus your best friend who is now dating your ex, are all members of the gaming group.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">Do you really want to hand one of them your alter ego's alter ego to use against you over three beers and a bag of chips?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\">Third, I have A Lot of the original first edition books for Mage and Vampire, some Werewolf and Wraith, and a few books for Changeling - as well as Gypsy. Then life took me away from gaming and I missed a lot of the books that came after the mid 90's. A couple years ago I started trying to finish acquiring the books I still wanted to complete a few sets from first edition. Now I find there is CWoD, Revised WoD, NWoD, and WoD20. I love the lore in CWoD. I have been collecting books from NWoD but don't care for it's lore. However, I like the NWoD systemically.<br /> <br /> So:</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\">What exactly is the WoD20 Lore in relation to both CWoD and NWoD?<br /> What exactly is the WoD20 Systemically in relation to both CWoD and NWoD?<br /> Is there going to be another splatbook to convert WtO20 between systems?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\">Last, I have a completely different take on Wraith I have been developing over the last several months. I titled this Wraith Unremitting. It is not yet complete, but I have thus far created:</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#808080\">A new Raison d'Etre for wraiths</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">A new structure for Anchors</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">A new approach for Fetters</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">7 Houses (previously styled Guilds)</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">15 Arcanoi</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">Adapted or Adopted around 60 Numina from NWoD materials</span></li> </ol><span style=\"color:#808080\">Working on development of:</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#808080\">How to hunt wraiths</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">Who hunts wraiths</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">3 Dark Houses which serve the Wyrm</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#808080\">Wraith perceptions of: Garou Tribes, Vampire Clans, Mage Conventions and Traditions, and Changeling Kith</span></li> </ol><span style=\"color:#800000\">ROFL - Now that you are going to rewrite the rules, how much trouble am I going to have fitting the material in?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 11-23-2014, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T00:07:14-08:00","id":319686,"title":"","content":"Lore-wise, the 20s are CWoD, not NWoD, using only the CWoD mythos. Revised was another CWoD edition, doing a cleanup of the mechanics and refocusing the games.<br /> <br /> In terms of the metaplot, the 20s are situated around the cusp of the CWoD's change from 2e to Revised, taking a metaplot-agnostic approach. (This doesn't apply to Wraith, which never got a Revised edition; we don't know whether Wraith20 is resetting the metaplot to shortly before Ends of Empire, or advancing it past that, or doing both, as Mage20 is doing with its metaplot, projecting the 6th Great Maelstrom as a potential future.)<br /> <br /> System-wise, the 20s are a tweaked CWoD Revised-era Storyteller System.<br /> <br /> There's no translation guide, because there's no NWoD Wraith game to convert to/from (since that's what the translation guides are - guides to converting between CWoD and NWoD versions of games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T00:52:29-08:00","id":319719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=319686#post319686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no translation guide, because there's no NWoD Wraith game to convert to/from (since that's what the translation guides are - guides to converting between CWoD and NWoD versions of games).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since NWoD is somewhat predictable in structure, perhaps there should be anyway - so NWoD system users can translate CWoD Wraith to their games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T07:21:51-08:00","id":319868,"title":"","content":"1-As much fun as the glow in the dark cover was, I'm not sure we'll be replicating that.<br /> <br /> OK, true story here - I got my copy of Wraith 1st when it came out and very excitedly took it to the Rolemaster game I was playing in at the time. Everyone oohed and aahed over it, and then I said, &quot;And I hear the cover's glow in the dark! Let's try it!&quot; So someone turned out the lights, and the cover glowed, and then my great and good friend James Steere said to me, &quot;Uh, Rich, I think that's a nose.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2-With that gaming group, you may want to consider a round or two of Paranoia (currently being Kickstarted by the mighty James Wallis, and yes, I'm a stretch goal) to get it out of your systems. Alternately, you could explore some of the multiple approaches we'll be taking to Shadowguiding in Wr20.<br /> <br /> 3-Right now, my focus is strictly on making Wr20 as complete as possible. Myopic, possibly, but that's how I'm rolling right now.<br /> <br /> 4-I have no idea what you've done or how difficult it might be to make mesh, but I'm going to say that it will probably be easier than sitting through a late-period Nic Cage film festival to adapt it. NOT THE BEES!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:25:01-08:00","id":319936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"