Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T22:48:33-08:00","id":320418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=297186#post297186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-asking an old question that was ignored; will Wraith20 update it's view of Africa? It was distressing to see a continent full of diverse and developed nations reduced to a somewhat-racist &quot;Darkest Africa&quot; pulp throwback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure how many people will have a minor in African Theologies or understand the concept of &quot;The Dead are Dying of thirst.&quot; But even given a better conceptual view of the plethora of paradigms in Africa, stories about and coming from the dead will be filled with &quot;throwback&quot; to some romanticized guilded age that never was because that is not only what the ghosts allow themselves to remember, when they can, but it is the age from which many of them come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T22:16:46-08:00","id":321436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=319595#post319595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I find there is CWoD, Revised WoD, NWoD, and WoD20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless we're getting into Monte Cook's WoD, there are only two Worlds of Darkness: Classic and New. They're different universes entirely.<br /> <br /> Classic WoD includes a first edition, second edition, Revised edition, and the 20th Anniversary Edition.<br /> <br /> New WoD includes a first edition and second edition.<br /> <br /> So the &quot;Revised WoD&quot; and &quot;WoD20&quot; you mention are both part of the CWoD and are not distinct entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So:What exactly is the WoD20 Lore in relation to both CWoD and NWoD?<br /> What exactly is the WoD20 Systemically in relation to both CWoD and NWoD?<br /> Is there going to be another splatbook to convert WtO20 between systems? </div> </div> </div>- The X20 books are unrelated to the new WoD at all. Plotwise, Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage are all set at a nebulous point somewhere between the events of 2nd Edition and Revised.<br /> - The X20 books are unrelated to the new WoD at all. The other three rulebooks are Revised edition rules with a few additional tweaks; Wraith never had a Revised edition, but as I understand it Rich is taking the opportunity to treat Wraith20 as sort of the Revised edition it never had, bringing it into line with the other X20 books.<br /> - While there are differences between the second editions and Revised/X20 editions, they're minor enough that you can probably do any conversion in your head. You don't need a separate book. White Wolf didn't make conversion guides when releasing the Revised books from 1998-2000, and I don't recall anyone complaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T22:19:00-08:00","id":321438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=319868#post319868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-As much fun as the glow in the dark cover was, I'm not sure we'll be replicating that.<br /> <br /> OK, true story here - I got my copy of Wraith 1st when it came out and very excitedly took it to the Rolemaster game I was playing in at the time. Everyone oohed and aahed over it, and then I said, &quot;And I hear the cover's glow in the dark! Let's try it!&quot; So someone turned out the lights, and the cover glowed, and then my great and good friend James Steere said to me, &quot;Uh, Rich, I think that's a nose.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been pushing to have the book say &quot;Noseroids&quot; on the cover but my pleas have thus far been in vain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:23:46-08:00","id":322056,"title":"","content":"Get your Oboli ready. I read yesterday, the Deluxe Wraith 20 Kickstarter is to go live next week on Tuesday, December 2nd at 12 noon EST: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/thanking-forward-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/thanking-forw...meeting-notes/</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachmen