vider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T01:54:23-08:00","id":340667,"title":"","content":"I do hope the book includes the mechanics from Blood Dimmed Tides - how Wraiths interact with bodies of water in the shadowlands is actually really important (specifically that its solid to them since they don't displace water, but can spend corpus to &quot;swim&quot; + a merit for the drowned that lets them move through water without spending corpus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:24:07-08:00","id":340922,"title":"","content":"it might sound stupid but , i always wondered How does it feels to be a Wraith.. Do they feel hunger? thirst, physical pain? (like feeling their dead wounds)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T11:42:08-08:00","id":341027,"title":"","content":"Stuff, things:<br /> <br /> How does it feel to be a wraith? The usual bodily urges get subsumed by one's Passions. At the same time, consider how much of your day you spend brushing your teeth/showering/eating/dressing etc. Wraiths don't have to deal with that, so their daily routines become a little different than ours, and priorities shift with that.<br /> <br /> Khaleesi - All the Arcanoi are getting redone. There will be updates :-)<br /> <br /> I absolutely love The Devil's Backbone. If memory serves, I listed it as recommended viewing in the sample intro chapter up at the KS site.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy Out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T12:34:19-08:00","id":341061,"title":"","content":"I have a question.<br /> <br /> We know that the 16 Stygian Arcanoi, Jade Arcanoi and the base 5 Dark Arcanoi are in Wr20.<br /> <br /> We also know that the 3 remaining Dark Arcanoi are a stretch goal. <br /> <br /> So are the 2 Risen Arcanoi and 3 other unique Kingdom Arcanoi going to be included as well? As a stretch goal before the Kickstarter ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:59:06-08:00","id":342711,"title":"","content":"I still can't fathom why getting updates to all Arcanoi are locked behind stretch goals instead of being automatically part of the book, as the case has been with every other 20th Anniversary edition thus far. And if leaving these as stretch goals why are we getting so many fiction goals before these much more important system update stretch goals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T02:00:24-08:00","id":342735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=342711#post342711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still can't fathom why getting updates to all Arcanoi are locked behind stretch goals instead of being automatically part of the book, as the case has been with every other 20th Anniversary edition thus far. And if leaving these as stretch goals why are we getting so many fiction goals before these much more important system update stretch goals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First off, all 16 Stygian Arcanoi are in, and are getting DOUBLE the wordcount they previously got. They did a whole update on why Wraith20 is different than the previous 20th Anniversary books (it's more of a complete overhaul rather than a nostalgia collection because Wraith never got a Revised Edition), and that makes the decisions on where to dedicate its wordcount different than the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T09:13:03-08:00","id":343022,"title":"","content":"Also, didn't Dansky say somewhere that the page count of Wraith was lower than the other 20th Anniversary editions because they didn't know how popular it was actually going to be? I remember reading that somewhere... And a lot of the stuff that went in automatically to the editions of the Big Three (Vampire, Werewolf &amp; Mage) was deferred to stretch goals? It seems like a classic situation of not wasting effort in case the effort didn't need to be made. As glamourweaver points out Wr20 is also Wraith Revised. Maybe the basics put forth in the initial Kickstarter offering were more in the way of funding that 2nd Ed and, as the stretch goals open up, people are going to be getting something a lot more like the other 20th anniversary editions?<br /> <br /> In some ways, this makes sense when &quot;testing the waters&quot; of the games that weren't as wildly popular as the Big Three. A way to test how far and deep the commitment of the fan base goes. We may see something similar for Changeling20 and, if other games get the nod, for the later games as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:02:54-08:00","id":343461,"title":"","content":"General notes....<br /> <br /> 1-The main place to see design notes and whatnot from me is over at the KS site, either in the updates or the comments (when I'm feeling particularly verbose). So, some of the big questions that get asked here are covered there, and beyond that hopefully those posts will give you some insight into the design decisions I'm making on the book. Wraith 20 /is/ different from M20 or V20 or WW20 in a couple of ways, not the least of which it's also the Revised edition, so some of the word count that might be dedicated to other things in a book that already had a Revised is being taken up by those updates. As for the Arcanoi, the core plan for the book is the 16 core Stygian Arcanoi and the 5 base Dark Arcanoi, with additional ones added by stretch goal because unfortunately, design means hard decisions when you're having to choose &quot;what gets the word count&quot; between multiple good options. Lord willing and the creek don't rise, we'll hit all those goals and then some and I can keep adding the good bits.<br /> <br /> 2-Khaleesi - Phantasm is still mid-rewrite. When I have an answer, I'll pass it along.<br /> <br /> 3-Don't know about an art book as a stretch goal - right now we're focusing on stuff like the nascent Book of Oblivion. I will say that there's a lot of Ron Spencer art up in my office, though.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:29:08-08:00","id":343473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=343461#post343461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026I will say that there's a lot of Ron Spencer art up in my office, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading between the lines, sounds like Rich will give people personal tours of his place\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2959-bates","name":"Bates","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2959_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:05:28-08:00","id":343544,"title":"","content":"any chances for an ilustration of our favorite bastard ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:30:25-08:00","id":343565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=343544#post343544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any chances for an ilustration of our favorite bastard ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Carpenter or the Smiling Lord? Both are pretty big bastards. Carpenter is a Doppelganger and Spectres are bastards by default but he's the only one we know that survived the 6GM and crossed over into other game lines, not counting Orpheus. While the Smiling Lord is the arch-traitor of WtO, trying to screw over everyone for his own ambitions.<br /> <br /> Screw it, give us art of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:22:00-08:00","id":344212,"title":"","content":"Is Wraith20 maintaining the history of everyone having their memories edited to hide the War of the Dead (Wraith: the Great War)?<br /> <br /> That always felt clumsy to me - it was just a way to explain why such a major event hadn't be recognized by Wraith history before said setting was created. With the opportunity to write the history in the core fresh, it'd seem to me the best choice is just to include it without the memory edit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:38:33-08:00","id":344221,"title":"","content":"Will the Dark Kingdom of Ivory be approached in a matter less problematic than older Wraith books? It always bugged me that Africa's role in the Underworld was little better than a wild bushland of animal spirits and primitive tribes. I would say ditto for the Americas, but I suppose writing away the natives is too canon to change now, regardless of how bogus that's always felt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:39:55-08:00","id":344223,"title":"","content":"I would assume so. While I don't like the memory alteration of the events of the Great War at the same time it's hard to see them changing it given that the Smiling Lord is still the same bastard and arch-traitor who's still working with the Yellow Springs and ultimately is exposed and meets his end during <i>Ends of Empire</i>.<br /> <br /> Would he be replaced with another traitor? That's a big stretch that his successor is also a traitor, working with the Yellow Springs to supplant Charon and the Hierarchy. Pardoned by Charon but still known as the man who tried to usurp Charon's throne and plunged the empire into a civil war during a Great Maelstrom? A lot of people would be scratching their heads at why Charon would allow him to remain in power after all that. To say nothing of the lingering tension and animosity between the Grim Legion and pretty much every other Legion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:59:04-08:00","id":344237,"title":"","content":"My idea was that he faked being replaced - basically a reverse of the normal assumption the Deathlord Masks allow for continuity of identity with multiple Wraiths over the millennia - in this case it allowed him to maintain the position (or retake it later) while pretending to be a new Wraith in the same Mask.<br /> <br /> That's assuming the setting even needs the Smiling Lord as arch-traitor, since the War with Yellow Springs has already been done as an apocalypse that Wraith20 wouldn't be including.<br /> <br /> I admittedly like the idea of a PC in a Great War game (a dead common soldier from the War) getting to take the Mask at the end of ones Chronicle, without massively diverting from history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T19:10:14-08:00","id":344309,"title":"","content":"Can someone remind me WHY the Mnemoi covered for the Smiling Lord?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T20:08:50-08:00","id":344334,"title":"","content":"Well cause Charon knew the Smiling Lord was a traitor because Lady of Fate and it was all a part of the plan... somehow. Even though all he seemed to do is nuke Enoch and help pave the way for the Yellow Spring rather awesome but doomed invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T15:38:25-08:00","id":347035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=344309#post344309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone remind me WHY the Mnemoi covered for the Smiling Lord?</div> </div> </div> </div>In return, I quote J.R.R. Tolkien: &quot;My heart tells me that he has some part to play yet, for good or ill, before the end&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure Gandalf wasn't telling all that he knew there, either :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T20:00:17-08:00","id":348732,"title":"","content":"Hey RDG, i got something to tell you...<br /> <br /> Youre an amazing writter, thank you for taking the time back for wraith, for your fans, and to be open with us in this amazing and surreal return to Stygia. So, with my best heart i wish you a Merry Xmas, a happy new year, an amazing hanukka or Qwanza (or what ever they celebrate down in stygia) , cheers from chile. and since most things you reply to have to have an answer (or a joke), ill ask, How does an amazing writter celebrates christmas knowing that he has an awesome fanbase?<br /> <br /> take care, cheers and merry xmas!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T19:34:21-08:00","id":352216,"title":"","content":"Minor niggling question: why did the genocide of Native American populations weaken their counterparts in the Shadowlands, rather than the inverse? It always confused me how a fairly minor contingent of not-even-properly-Stygian wraiths managed to wipe out the native population of dead completely, and how any remnants of the native wraiths are never discussed as a factor in the American underworld.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into the complete lack of Wraithly info on South America...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T22:56:39-08:00","id":352354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=352216#post352216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor niggling question: why did the genocide of Native American populations weaken their counterparts in the Shadowlands, rather than the inverse? It always confused me how a fairly minor contingent of not-even-properly-Stygian wraiths managed to wipe out the native population of dead completely, and how any remnants of the native wraiths are never discussed as a factor in the American underworld.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into the complete lack of Wraithly info on South America...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, we know virtually nothing about what happened in North America - the one source we have to date, Mediums, simply says that the Dark Kingdom of Flint withdrew to the Tempest, and still hold some Skinlands territory, but gives no reasons. Nothing on them being weakened or reduced or anything.<br /> <br /> It was the residents of the Flayed Lands - the Dark Kingdom of Mesoamerica - that got weakened by the invasion, and _that_ was because they drew power from the religious ceremonies and sacrifices of their mortal people. When those got stamped out, the wraiths of the Flayed Lands lost their strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T23:05:13-08:00","id":352360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=352354#post352354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, we know virtually nothing about what happened in North America - the one source we have to date, Mediums, simply says that the Dark Kingdom of Flint withdrew to the Tempest, and still hold some Skinlands territory, but gives no reasons. Nothing on them being weakened or reduced or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except we know that many American cities are firmly Stygian; Boston is explicitly stated as such in <i>Dark Kingdom of Jade</i>, Atlanta appears in its titular book, and I feel like both Los Angeles and San Francisco are described somewhere briefly as well. <br /> <br /> I'd love to see <i>Necropolis: Mexico City</i> someday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T23:20:17-08:00","id":352364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=352360#post352360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except we know that many American cities are firmly Stygian; Boston is explicitly stated as such in <i>Dark Kingdom of Jade</i>, Atlanta appears in its titular book, and I feel like both Los Angeles and San Francisco are described somewhere briefly as well.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see <i>Necropolis: Mexico City</i> someday.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Dark Kingdom of Flint still holds some Skinlands territory&quot; doesn't equal &quot;The Dark Kingdom of Flint still holds North America&quot;. The territory the Kingdom of Flint holds is basically the Great Plains, as well as some burial mounds, holy sites, and notorious battlefields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T08:48:11-08:00","id":352727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=352364#post352364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The territory the Kingdom of Flint holds is basically the Great Plains, as well as some burial mounds, holy sites, and notorious battlefields.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there some evidence in the books to support the idea they hold the Great Plains? Depending on how you slice that terms, you are giving over a lot of major American cities to the Kingdom of Flint. I guess my evidence to the contrary is largely negative. I would think that if Denver, Kansas City, Omaha, Topeka, Lawrence, Oklahoma City, Tulsa, etc., etc., etc. we would have seen something about it... Stygia having a massive border to garrison along the Mississippi River or something of the kind. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T09:05:54-08:00","id":352732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=352727#post352727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there some evidence in the books to support the idea they hold the Great Plains? Depending on how you slice that terms, you are giving over a lot of major American cities to the Kingdom of Flint. I guess my evidence to the contrary is largely negative. I would think that if Denver, Kansas City, Omaha, Topeka, Lawrence, Oklahoma City, Tulsa, etc., etc., etc. we would have seen something about it... Stygia having a massive border to garrison along the Mississippi River or something of the kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mediums: Speakers with the Dead, p. 98: &quot;The links to the Shadowlands that the Islands of Flint do maintain are kept up for the purpose of sustaining tradition and Fetters back in the Skinlands. There are few places, even in the Reservation Lands, where the Kingdom of Flint is strong: burial mounds, holy sites (often coincidental with Garou Caerns) and battlegrounds including Wounded Knee and the Little Big Horn River. Only the expanses of the Great Plains harbor a sizeable number of Native American wraiths; the rest of the continent has been thoroughly assimilated by the Stygian paradigm. Official Stygian policy holds that these places where the Native wraiths are strong are Spectre-haunted, and it advises Stygian citizens to avoid them. The reason is that Stygian troops who go in large numbers to such locales don't find anything, and when they go out singly or in small groups, they're never found again.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T09:16:34-08:00","id":352754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=352732#post352732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mediums: Speakers with the Dead, p. 98: &quot;The links to the Shadowlands that the Islands of Flint do maintain are kept up for the purpose of sustaining tradition and Fetters back in the Skinlands. There are few places, even in the Reservation Lands, where the Kingdom of Flint is strong: burial mounds, holy sites (often coincidental with Garou Caerns) and battlegrounds including Wounded Knee and the Little Big Horn River. Only the expanses of the Great Plains harbor a sizeable number of Native American wraiths; the rest of the continent has been thoroughly assimilated by the Stygian paradigm. Official Stygian policy holds that these places where the Native wraiths are strong are Spectre-haunted, and it advises Stygian citizens to avoid them. The reason is that Stygian troops who go in large numbers to such locales don't find anything, and when they go out singly or in small groups, they're never found again.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah... the PLAINS part. So, large convoys from Necropolis KC to Necropolis Lawrence to Necropolis Topeka to Necropolis Salina and a LOOOOOONG stretch to Necropolis Denver and the like. (Or Argos or the Midnight Express for smaller groups). That's a lot different than the Kingdom of Flint covering a significant fraction of the continental US.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:08:10-08:00","id":356878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=342735#post342735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First off, all 16 Stygian Arcanoi are in, and are getting DOUBLE the wordcount they previously got. They did a whole update on why Wraith20 is different than the previous 20th Anniversary books (it's more of a complete overhaul rather than a nostalgia collection because Wraith never got a Revised Edition), and that makes the decisions on where to dedicate its wordcount different than the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, I would have still preferred to see more of the updates focused on game content, rather than fiction. I'm sure fiction is nice, but I'm really hoping to play this sucker, not just read it, and I would prefer something like M20's &quot;How Do You Do That&quot; to a cute fiction story I'll read once and then never really touch on again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:51:51-08:00","id":356944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=356878#post356878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, I would have still preferred to see more of the updates focused on game content, rather than fiction. I'm sure fiction is nice, but I'm really hoping to play this sucker, not just read it, and I would prefer something like M20's &quot;How Do You Do That&quot; to a cute fiction story I'll read once and then never really touch on again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah but we're already getting that, the <i>Handbook for the Recently Deceased</i>. We've also got a 15k Orpheus add on, the Dark Kingdom of Jade's Arcanoi, the addition and rework of the Dark Arcanoi from Doomslayers, and a 10k <i>Book of Oblivion</i>. That's just what we've unlocked thus far. Yeah there's been a lot of fiction stretch goals but there's a lot of actual material we are getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T22:06:35-08:00","id":357232,"title":"","content":"I gotta agree with Wolfgar on that there are way too many fiction related stretch goals compared to actual game content so much so that it feels rather speed bumpy just something to fill in the space between actual stretch goals. For me at least fiction anthologies are are way, way, down on the priority list of reading, as I have limited time for that now a days with family and work intruding on my spare time, and ends up likely to just sitting on my hard drive for several years before I can get to it where as actual game content is read immediately upon release. So much more bang for my buck that.<br /> <br /> I just hope we at least brake through the 230 line to get additional material for Spectres into the Book of Oblivion though I wouldn't mind the additional Dark Kingdom Arcanoi either there is again one speed bump of a fiction there in between. Wraith is my favorite WoD product by far and yet I think it's kickstarter is the one with the most fiction related stretch goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T22:55:49-08:00","id":357267,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I guess I'll play Shadow Guide for this portion of the conversation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I'm *really* looking forward to the fiction Stretchgoals. I say more fiction! Crunch is good and all, but my troupe has been hashing out our own crunch since EoE. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">It's like those old credit card commercials:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Revised Dark Arcanoi: 7500 words<br /> Dark Kingdoms Arcanoi: 15000 words<br /> In-game fiction penned by talented and established writers: Priceless.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My two oboli...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T23:50:37-08:00","id":357293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=357267#post357267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I guess I'll play Shadow Guide for this portion of the conversation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I'm *really* looking forward to the fiction Stretchgoals. I say more fiction! Crunch is good and all, but my troupe has been hashing out our own crunch since EoE. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">It's like those old credit card commercials:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Revised Dark Arcanoi: 7500 words<br /> Dark Kingdoms Arcanoi: 15000 words<br /> In-game fiction penned by talented and established writers: Priceless.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My two oboli...</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is I cannot play fiction I can only read it and this is about an RPG meant to be played after all. Especially since WoD fiction has always been notorious about not keeping to WoD canon I mean characters in fiction can sometimes do things that are impossible in game or just ridiculous otherwise and even if it is all good fiction true to the source material even it can only be better with more source material to rely on.<br /> <br /> In the end it is about RPG's being about your group telling a story together while fiction is you reading a story, penned by someone else, alone.<br /> <br /> That is to say what is needed is frameworks and skeletons that we can build our stories upon not full stories ready made for us before hand, those frameworks are the crunch and background information about organizations and places preferably combined in almost equal measure.<br /> <br /> But that's just my two oboli on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 01-02-2015, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T10:05:02-08:00","id":357567,"title":"","content":"Yar, We've already gotten a lot of fiction. How abouts switchin' the latest fiction Stretch Goal with the Great War Arcanoi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T09:24:29-08:00","id":358372,"title":"","content":"Could we switch all the achieved fiction goals to get the Labyrinth section of the Book of Oblivion done?<br /> <br /> Damn it if we miss this one... Contact your friends and get people to throw money at this we need those 10k words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:05:50-08:00","id":358418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=358372#post358372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we switch all the achieved fiction goals to get the Labyrinth section of the Book of Oblivion done?<br /> <br /> Damn it if we miss this one... Contact your friends and get people to throw money at this we need those 10k words.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is still 3 days to go, and we usually get a higher volume of pledges at the end, so I'm <b>almost</b> certain that we will get the Labyrinth stretch goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T20:48:15-08:00","id":358781,"title":"","content":"I hope so!<br /> I also hope that the last stretch goal doesn't mean that without it we don't get Artifacts in the book.<br /> <br /> On another note, after reading the Ch. 1 Preview, it seemed, to me at least, imply that Corpus no longer needs to be spent to pass through Skinlandia Objects.<br /> I do hope that this is true as I was always a little put off about Wraiths having to take some damage to do perhaps the most Ghostly Thing Evhar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T22:17:52-08:00","id":358826,"title":"","content":"Happy New Year, Deadguy!<br /> <br /> Quick question here: What is the background for the word &quot;Anacreon&quot; as one of the ranks in Wraith? I only know it as the Greek poet or as the Foundation planet and solar system.<br /> <br /> Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T00:48:19-08:00","id":358904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katrina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=358826#post358826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy New Year, Deadguy!<br /> <br /> Quick question here: What is the background for the word &quot;Anacreon&quot; as one of the ranks in Wraith? I only know it as the Greek poet or as the Foundation planet and solar system.<br /> <br /> Katrina</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess - and its only a guess - I'd say its a reference to the drinking song, &quot;To Anacreon in Heaven&quot; (whose melody was appropriated for &quot;The Star Spangled Banner&quot;). In the lyrics, the singers implore the (long dead) Anacreon to mentor them from beyond the grave. And so skilled and powerful was Anacreon, the gods themselves freak out over the request.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T17:48:45-08:00","id":360791,"title":"","content":"Hey, folks. Coming down to the wire on the KS and I wanted to say thank you to everyone who's supported the project. It has been, frankly, amazing.<br /> <br /> Now, on to questions, comments, and suchlike:<br /> <br /> Katrina - I believe One Vorlon is correct; that name was set before I officially joined the Wolf. That being said, I spent a lot of time as the in-house Dead Languages expert, as I'd studied Latin, Greek and Old English in college/grad school and some of the Potterific mangling of Latin we got made my hair explode.<br /> Mental-Mouse - The Rule of Ouch remains in effect.<br /> Fiction - Bear in mind that I'll be editing the anthology as well as writing one of the stories (an Erik story, no less), and that other authors include Ree &quot;Fountains of Bright Crimson&quot; Soesbee and Mur &quot;Mage: Dark Ages&quot; Lafferty, as well as the father of Carpenter, Charles Andrew Bates. So I think we'll be sticking pretty close to canon, and there may even be some setting-useful intel tucked away in a tale or two. Not trying to go all transmedia on folks, but good, accessible fiction is a great way to get people interested in a setting, and short stories are nice bite-sized chunks that are easier to get people to read than novels. So there's a method to the madness. Also, if you add up the word count of all the game content stretch goals, it's gotten pretty durn considerable.<br /> <br /> Also, I've posted some pics of various bits of Wraith art I own over at my Facebook page, if folks are so inclined to take a gander.<br /> <br /> -Deadguy Out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T00:52:08-08:00","id":361070,"title":"","content":"Rome, glorious Rome. I can't think of a Necropolis I've wanted more, and for so long. I'm so pleased. (Istanbul is a close second).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T14:28:10-08:00","id":361601,"title":"","content":"So with all the kickstarter goals achieved, we have all the Dark Arcanoi ever published and the Great War and Jade Arcanoi. Is Connaissance from the Shadow Player's guide going to be included in this list? Unless I am mistaken it is the ONLY Arcanoi not looking at getting a place in the 20th Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T15:50:12-08:00","id":361677,"title":"","content":"Hey RDG how ya been? . i was wondering if you will do a special note on the book for crossover rules with games like Werewolf (theres been a discussion on how certain Werewolf Gifts may affect wraiths).<br /> <br /> also, i would like to know, where you got the inspiration for places like The Laberyth, The Tempest, The Oblivion and Bedlam","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:31:35-08:00","id":361708,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about crossover content in Wr20 as well, if any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T19:29:46-08:00","id":361938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=267556#post267556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will I be going back through the thread and picking up old questions? If time permits, absolutely. If I don't get to yours, don't hesitate to repost.<br /> Will the focus be on wraiths? Yes, a thousand times yes. There will be material on crossover games and relations to the rest of the WoD because, well, it's a /world/ of Darkness, but my focus has always been and will always be wraiths. The other guys have enough books; they don't get the bulk of the content in ours :-)<br /> Will there be material on the Dark Kingdoms? If you add up the word count devoted to the various Dark Kingdoms in the DKoJ books, Ends of Empire, the WPG and SPG, you end up with well over 150K words. I don't think I can get /all/ of that into Wraith 20 :-) But the Dark Kingdoms will not be ignored or forgotten, and if we have some success with W20, I'd love to dive deeper into them down the line.<br /> Why all the Phil Collins hatred? Personal reasons. Also, even mention the word &quot;Sussudio&quot; to me and I'm ear wormed for a week. Damnit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the earlier response to the same question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hope it helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T22:50:54-08:00","id":362146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Old Rusty Pipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=361601#post361601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with all the kickstarter goals achieved, we have all the Dark Arcanoi ever published and the Great War and Jade Arcanoi. Is Connaissance from the Shadow Player's guide going to be included in this list? Unless I am mistaken it is the ONLY Arcanoi not looking at getting a place in the 20th Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deadguy's said it's going to be included in the Kickstarter comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T23:13:12-08:00","id":362155,"title":"","content":"1-Yay Kickstarter! Thank you to everyone who backed it!<br /> 2-yes, Connaissance will be in the book.<br /> 3-Crossover stuff is getting its own chapter. Is it going to cover every single possible interaction of every power used by every supernatural with every possible wraith Arcanos? Probably not. But it's got its own chapter.<br /> 4-Still opposed to Phil Collins, with a pass for any Genesis from Abacab or earlier.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T13:49:49-08:00","id":362844,"title":"","content":"what do you plan to do after Wraith gets published? will you still stick around the forums?, and will you add Reality Show Ghost Facers type of organizations in the book? as well bio exorcists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T21:47:56-08:00","id":363199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=362844#post362844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you plan to do after Wraith gets published? will you still stick around the forums?, and will you add Reality Show Ghost Facers type of organizations in the book? as well bio exorcists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now I'm mainly focused on getting Wraith20 and the attendant stretch goals done. I have no doubt I'll be sticking around after publication in one form or another, but I'm not worrying about the details right now. <br /> <br /> deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T22:03:15-08:00","id":363205,"title":"","content":"How does it feel to be back from the dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T12:40:08-08:00","id":363736,"title":"","content":"Hey RDG, On one thread there were some users tossing ideas for other books that they would like to see in the future, i would like your thoughts<br /> <br /> WtO20: Ghost Riders In The Sky (A setting book for the North American Civil War)<br /> WtO20: Nothing Personal, Kiddo. (A setting book for Chicago during the Prohibition era, as well Wraiths of the 1920s)<br /> WtO20: Viva La Revolucion (A Wraith book for South America and the Revoluciones and Dictatorships)<br /> WtO20: By Sea, Air and Land. A setting book for The Titanic, The Hiddenburg and The Midnight Express<br /> WtO20: Spook Hunters or How i learn to be A Bioexorcist: A book detailing how humans exploit Hauntings with TV shows and Reality Shows (and how to build your own GhostHunters or Ghost Facers team) and how do Wraiths handle Spooking and scaring people away from their homes.<br /> Wraith the Oblivion Cookbook. (It would be an Aprils fool prank, one page only saying: Wraiths dont Eat, they are dead.)<br /> Wraith: Dia de los Muertos, a small chronicle set during halloween and Day of the Dead involving a mystery in Stygia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T09:48:33-08:00","id":364502,"title":"","content":"One of the most difficult thing I oversee with playing WtO is the ST having to improvize random NPC wraiths.<br /> Wraiths are typically defined by Fetters, Passions, their Shadow and this on top of their personal history. Even their apparence is conditionned by their very personal backgroung.<br /> That's why I always considered 'Necropolis: Atlanta' as one of the most useful add-on for WtO.<br /> <br /> @ RDG: Will you include a lot of NPC descriptions in the Wraith 20th Edition? That would be awesome.<br /> Also, a few backers will be used as 'models' for an 'upcoming Wraith 20 book'. Could we have some precisions about that please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T12:07:35-08:00","id":365581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=363205#post363205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it feel to be back from the dead?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Warm. It mainly feels warm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T12:09:08-08:00","id":365583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=364502#post364502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most difficult thing I oversee with playing WtO is the ST having to improvize random NPC wraiths.<br /> Wraiths are typically defined by Fetters, Passions, their Shadow and this on top of their personal history. Even their apparence is conditionned by their very personal backgroung.<br /> That's why I always considered 'Necropolis: Atlanta' as one of the most useful add-on for WtO.<br /> <br /> @ RDG: Will you include a lot of NPC descriptions in the Wraith 20th Edition? That would be awesome.<br /> Also, a few backers will be used as 'models' for an 'upcoming Wraith 20 book'. Could we have some precisions about that please?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There aren't going to be a lot of NPCs in The Behemoth (what I'm calling the book now) because word count is very, very precious and it's good design to prioritize general application over specific. That being said, there are going to be some tools for Storytellers in chapter 7 on how to tackle this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T12:10:45-08:00","id":365586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=363736#post363736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey RDG, On one thread there were some users tossing ideas for other books that they would like to see in the future, i would like your thoughts<br /> <br /> WtO20: Ghost Riders In The Sky (A setting book for the North American Civil War)<br /> WtO20: Nothing Personal, Kiddo. (A setting book for Chicago during the Prohibition era, as well Wraiths of the 1920s)<br /> WtO20: Viva La Revolucion (A Wraith book for South America and the Revoluciones and Dictatorships)<br /> WtO20: By Sea, Air and Land. A setting book for The Titanic, The Hiddenburg and The Midnight Express<br /> WtO20: Spook Hunters or How i learn to be A Bioexorcist: A book detailing how humans exploit Hauntings with TV shows and Reality Shows (and how to build your own GhostHunters or Ghost Facers team) and how do Wraiths handle Spooking and scaring people away from their homes.<br /> Wraith the Oblivion Cookbook. (It would be an Aprils fool prank, one page only saying: Wraiths dont Eat, they are dead.)<br /> Wraith: Dia de los Muertos, a small chronicle set during halloween and Day of the Dead involving a mystery in Stygia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of these are very interesting ideas, but they seem better suited for one-shots than full campaign settings. Titanic, for example, maps nicely to the Tsushima Straits material from DKoJA.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm a huge US Civil War goober.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:30:01-08:00","id":365954,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mr. D:<br /> <br /> [Unless it\u2019s changing in Wr20] Wraiths from the same culture can communicate with one another; iirc, the \u201cLanguage of the Dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> What do wraiths do for writing in the Underworld? Is there a \u201cscript of the dead\u201d? For example, a Marshall that only knew English in life writes out an arrest warrant and passes it along to a Centurion. The Centurion, however, only knew German when he was alive. Can the Centurion read the warrant? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T22:24:05-08:00","id":366070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=365954#post365954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mr. D:<br /> <br /> [Unless it\u2019s changing in Wr20] Wraiths from the same culture can communicate with one another; iirc, the \u201cLanguage of the Dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> What do wraiths do for writing in the Underworld? Is there a \u201cscript of the dead\u201d? For example, a Marshall that only knew English in life writes out an arrest warrant and passes it along to a Centurion. The Centurion, however, only knew German when he was alive. Can the Centurion read the warrant? </span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe writing is covered by the Language of the Dead, but I also know that somewhere in canon it's said that there's very little writing in the Dark Kingdoms, as relic paper is rare and soulforging people into paper is frankly wasteful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T06:25:36-08:00","id":366231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=366070#post366070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't believe writing is covered by the Language of the Dead, but I also know that somewhere in canon it's said that there's very little writing in the Dark Kingdoms, as relic paper is rare and soulforging people into paper is frankly wasteful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go tell that to the Wraiths that composed the Imprimatur <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T09:35:25-08:00","id":366391,"title":"","content":"Paper, As I recall, is manufactured from the only Trees in Stygia that are under the Legion of Fate's control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T20:19:18-08:00","id":366864,"title":"","content":"hey guys, i was running a crossover and i was wondering about the Maggot guns from Wraith, what happends when its shoot against a living being? id magine the Maggots would start running and exploring the flesh of its target (doing deeper damage)<br /> <br /> RDG: I was watching a kids movie (When Good Ghouls go Bad <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3hgWA6UCCwg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3hgWA6UCCwg</a> a review of the movie) And theres a quote i thought you might like for The Behemoth.<br /> <br /> (this little quote) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K_krg2fDF4Y\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K_krg2fDF4Y</a> (starting from the 1:00)<br /> <br /> &quot;Kankel: Y-Y-YOU'RE DEAD!!<br /> Uncle Fred: Y-y-you're Right!, at least i was. And i was resting pretty darn comfy too. Until i sensed you up to something.<br /> Kankel: S-sensed?<br /> Uncle Fred: Theres World beyond this World, Kankel!!, Times beyond This Time!. As you Soon find out...<br /> Kankel: Get away from me!!!<br /> Uncle Fred: Not a Chance pal, i didnt made my way through the ground so you could get away with it. Im gonna get you, and im gonna take you back to the Grave With Me. Lets Go!.&quot;<br /> <br /> Uncle Fred (A friendly Risen played by Christopher Loyd)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-12-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:36:18-08:00","id":367843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you call Wr20 is the Behemoth, what is M20?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Someone else's concern :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:56:07-08:00","id":367858,"title":"","content":"Will Wr20 have wordcount put into helping players understand what makes a good Fetter and what does not? I've always found that my 