the Object?<br /> Can a soulforged item be destroyed : with or with out releasing the original spirit?<br /> <br /> and what ways are to fully destroy a wraith, make sure it never comes back","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T06:13:44-08:00","id":369709,"title":"","content":"I can't answer all your questions but as I had one myself in link with the soulforged cooblestones that compose the Byways, I take the occasion to post.<br /> <br /> These are actually good questions, and I would only take the risk to answer the third one: yes, a soulforged item can be destroyed, and the soul composing it is then lost to Oblivion. The spirit of the Wraith composing the item can't be realeased: it IS the item.<br /> Note that an item can only be made out of a single soul: souls can't be melted together in order to produce bigger objects (The Sea of Souls being the only 'exception').<br /> <br /> And now my question: why none Wraith never tried to steal cobblestones from Byways by removing them in order to sell them later, like a Reaper would do with new souls? Are the Byways naturally 'protected' in some ways? Because it seems definitely easier to make such a business rather than simply running after newcomers in the underworld...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4701,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","user":"Dam","date":". 01-14-2015, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:06:41-08:00","id":370109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=369459#post369459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to reverse the soulforging?<br /> can a soulforged being Take Over any other beeing taking the Object?<br /> Can a soulforged item be destroyed : with or with out releasing the original spirit?<br /> <br /> and what ways are to fully destroy a wraith, make sure it never comes back</div> </div> </div> </div>In order:<br /> <br /> Nope, or at least Nhudri ain't talking.<br /> Nope.<br /> Yup.<br /> Soulforging and feeding a soul to Oblivion are both pretty permanent. <br /> <br /> -deadguy out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:07:3