DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:32:11-08:00","id":372797,"title":"","content":"I been trying to investigate for some Sources and inspiration for Wraith and a lot of times the name &quot;Scary Stories to Tell in The Dark&quot; came up. Im south american and i have never heard of such novels, never seen it on any library in here. So, when i heard of that book i though &quot;Oh, must be ..you know..Kids stuff like Goosebumps or something a bit lighter.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then i saw the art..and Oh My Fucking God i was actually creeped out and terrified by it (i saw the art by night by myself hearing the Credit Music from Blair Witch). i Fucking felt inlove with the art, So..Richard...i ask you as a fan of your work, and as a lover of all things horrible and nightmare fuel...Can you try and get Stephen Gammell to do the art for The Behemoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:38:29-08:00","id":372806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=372797#post372797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I been trying to investigate for some Sources and inspiration for Wraith and a lot of times the name &quot;Scary Stories to Tell in The Dark&quot; came up. Im south american and i have never heard of such novels, never seen it on any library in here. So, when i heard of that book i though &quot;Oh, must be ..you know..Kids stuff like Goosebumps or something a bit lighter.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then i saw the art..and Oh My Fucking God i was actually creeped out and terrified by it (i saw the art by night by myself hearing the Credit Music from Blair Witch). i Fucking felt inlove with the art, So..Richard...i ask you as a fan of your work, and as a lover of all things horrible and nightmare fuel...Can you try and get Stephen Gammell to do the art for The Behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the all in one book so I can't remember of the top of my head if there are 2 or 3 more books in that series, I think 2 more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:43:09-08:00","id":372906,"title":"","content":"On Arcanoi and buying them. Will the static cost of learning the other version of an existing one you possess remain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T10:59:38-08:00","id":374344,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy,<br /> <br /> Can Usury Level 2 be used to heal aggravated damage? (Referring to WtO 2nd edition and GW as it stands, not to the exciting upcoming WtO20 which we just have to wait for and its updates!) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> Khaleesi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","user":"Khaleesi","date":". 01-20-2015, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T19:21:42-08:00","id":375780,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy!<br /> I had some Arcanois questions and a few thoughts noting they are being rewritten (but since I am in the middle of a campaign now, I hope its ok to ask about them as currently stands!) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Songs of the Living (GW) talks about affects on Spectres, but would it not also bolster wraiths within hearing of it too? The WtO 2nd edition version Requiem targets wraiths from the description, but since the emotions can be either positive or negative, can this version be used on Spectres as well?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T23:33:05-08:00","id":377853,"title":"","content":"How would you build a PC Flatliner without delving into Orpheus? I forgot the original name of the group in Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T00:07:03-08:00","id":377862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=377853#post377853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you build a PC Flatliner without delving into Orpheus? I forgot the original name of the group in Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Benandanti had similar powers, but they were granted by special birth and training. They hit like fucking trucks, too. I believe they're in <i>Mediums</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T09:44:33-08:00","id":378142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=377853#post377853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you build a PC Flatliner without delving into Orpheus? I forgot the original name of the group in Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think there were a few groups that played around with projecting a living soul from its body but its been a long time since I've read the WtO books on the living who interact with the dead.<br /> <br /> Projector has become the catch all term for anyone that interacts with the dead by projecting their soul.<br /> <br /> In Orpheus there are two kinds, Sleepers, who must be cryogenicly frozen to leave their bodies, and Skimmers, who do it through drugs, meditation or a combination of the two.<br /> <br /> Also you should be a little careful with throwing around Flatliner and Orpheus as in Orpheus there is a group of ghosts called the Flatliners. They were 12 death row inmates that were chosen for Project Flatline, a joint project between the Orpheus Group and the NSA on projection. One of the inmates, Uriah Bishop, during one of these projection trips made contact with a spectre working for a Malfean and began to plot his escape. Eventually he managed to convince the other eleven to work with him to escape. All of them agreed and they escaped. The Orpheus techs, once they realized the Flatliners had left with no intention of returning to their bodies attempted to destroy all the evidence but it didn't go exactly well with prison ghosts causing fire that destroyed the death row section of the prison. After their escape, the Flatliners when their own ways. Five joined Bishop who was becoming increasingly fanatical and would come to severe Grandmother. Four would form a ghost street gang that allied itself with living street gangs. One, a serial rapist and murderer would continue his activities through his ghostly powers to possess the living and force them to rape and murder their friends/family members. The last one seeks out redemption, slipping what information he could in the form of Radio Free Death to members of the Orpheus Group and becoming one of the key players in the game's metaplot.<br /> <br /> All and all, the Flatliners all make for great characters in a WtO game. Bishop's group have taken over several groups in the Skinlands, including a drug rehabilitation center and several churches, corrupting them to their own ends. In WtO they'd make for a truly dangerous Heretic cult that actually serves a Malfean and Oblivion. The other group, the Blasphemers as they're called, are a pretty standard criminal Renegade group, especially in the eyes of the Hierarchy as they are Renegades that are actively interfering with the Skinlands in a serious way. The loner serial killer is... well pretty obvious. Mr. Radio Free Death, just as with Orpheus, would be a informant NPC, one able and willing to speak with both the living and the dead and actively working against the various forces of Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:05:21-08:00","id":378373,"title":"","content":"In Buried Secrets, it describes the back room of a shop called Urban Primitive: &quot;For the Restless, the third room, long walled-up and not known to exist in the realms of the living, is the haunt of ... Jomo.&quot; So everyone has to spend Corpus to get in and out, right? But later an encounter description says, &quot;The door to Jomo's office is open...&quot;<br /> <br /> And I realized: wait, can we somehow build a tunnel through skinland objects and install a relic door there? How?<br /> <br /> Also, do skinland objects and people pass harmlessly through relics, like relic walls? I'm sure the Hierarchy has a perimeter built on the White House lawn, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T18:44:01-08:00","id":378574,"title":"","content":"Guess who just fot a Silent Legion tattoo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T23:08:24-08:00","id":378745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=378574#post378574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess who just fot a Silent Legion tattoo!</div> </div> </div> </div>Like someone whom wasn't awesome enough to get into the Legion of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","user":"Mental-Mouse","date":". 01-23-2015, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T23:35:08-08:00","id":378768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=378745#post378745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like someone whom wasn't awesome enough to get into the Legion of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please. Like there's anyone more badass than a Pardoner for the Silent Legion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:15:05-08:00","id":381301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=378142#post378142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I think there were a few groups that played around with projecting a living soul from its body but its been a long time since I've read the WtO books on the living who interact with the dead.<br /> <br /> Projector has become the catch all term for anyone that interacts with the dead by projecting their soul.<br /> <br /> In Orpheus there are two kinds, Sleepers, who must be cryogenicly frozen to leave their bodies, and Skimmers, who do it through drugs, meditation or a combination of the two.<br /> <br /> Also you should be a little careful with throwing around Flatliner and Orpheus as in Orpheus there is a group of ghosts called the Flatliners. They were 12 death row inmates that were chosen for Project Flatline, a joint project between the Orpheus Group and the NSA on projection. One of the inmates, Uriah Bishop, during one of these projection trips made contact with a spectre working for a Malfean and began to plot his escape. Eventually he managed to convince the other eleven to work with him to escape. All of them agreed and they escaped. The Orpheus techs, once they realized the Flatliners had left with no intention of returning to their bodies attempted to destroy all the evidence but it didn't go exactly well with prison ghosts causing fire that destroyed the death row section of the prison. After their escape, the Flatliners when their own ways. Five joined Bishop who was becoming increasingly fanatical and would come to severe Grandmother. Four would form a ghost street gang that allied itself with living street gangs. One, a serial rapist and murderer would continue his activities through his ghostly powers to possess the living and force them to rape and murder their friends/family members. The last one seeks out redemption, slipping what information he could in the form of Radio Free Death to members of the Orpheus Group and becoming one of the key players in the game's metaplot.<br /> <br /> All and all, the Flatliners all make for great characters in a WtO game. Bishop's group have taken over several groups in the Skinlands, including a drug rehabilitation center and several churches, corrupting them to their own ends. In WtO they'd make for a truly dangerous Heretic cult that actually serves a Malfean and Oblivion. The other group, the Blasphemers as they're called, are a pretty standard criminal Renegade group, especially in the eyes of the Hierarchy as they are Renegades that are actively interfering with the Skinlands in a serious way. The loner serial killer is... well pretty obvious. Mr. Radio Free Death, just as with Orpheus, would be a informant NPC, one able and willing to speak with both the living and the dead and actively working against the various forces of Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Found them in WtG. In the Antagonists chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"