:"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T13:58:08-08:00","id":394095,"title":"","content":"Can you partially Moliate or soul-forge a wraith? Seems like a fitting-ly Hierarchy kind of punishment.... <br /> <br /> &quot;You have been found guilty of violating the Dictum Mortuum. As this is your first offense, the punishment will be the removal and soulforging of your left arm. If you are brought before this court again, I will send your to have your skin removed by Moliation. Consider yourself warned.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T18:25:15-08:00","id":394334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=394095#post394095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you partially Moliate or soul-forge a wraith? Seems like a fitting-ly Hierarchy kind of punishment....<br /> <br /> &quot;You have been found guilty of violating the Dictum Mortuum. As this is your first offense, the punishment will be the removal and soulforging of your left arm. If you are brought before this court again, I will send your to have your skin removed by Moliation. Consider yourself warned.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Artificers have a practice of soulforging pieces of their own hands, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T21:29:11-08:00","id":394432,"title":"","content":"Hey RDG, hows a going?<br /> hows things on your end?.<br /> any thoughts on the new Poltergeist trailer?, any chances for a one shot on Gettysburg?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 02-06-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:48:03-08:00","id":395030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=394334#post394334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the Artificers have a practice of soulforging pieces of their own hands, so yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is still attached, right? They don't cut it off, forge it, then re-attach it. <br /> <br /> I ask because I remember conversations about the indivisibility of oboli. 1 wraith = 1 coin. But the books do discuss both oboli being sub-divided (a la &quot;pieces of eight&quot;) AND the indivisibility of a soul (as reasoning for the 1 wraith = 1 obolos).<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly okay with having 1 wraith = 1 coin. It just indicates that the rate of exchange centers on the value of an intact soul, but still allowing for sub-division of a wraith, either before or after being completely soul-forged. Every piddly Relic or service is probably not worth the same as an entire wraith after all. <br /> <br /> But it does that mean that not all pieces of a oboli or soul-forged bits of wraith will moan.... unless they do, because Corpus isn't flesh. So it doesn't matter if you forge some dude's chopped off arm, that's not the same as a meat and bone arm that can't moan or scream. The wraith's detached arm is essentially just X% of his soul, moaning included.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T11:54:49-08:00","id":395238,"title":"","content":"Pathos would make better small change -- and even better with the addition of a common, cheap artifact that contains it and displays precisely the amount contained -- even if you need a Usurer to get any in or out. Although then the Usurer is going to want a fee, and if that's 1P per exchange that's pretty steep. So, I guess Usury 1 must be really common since pretty much every small businessman needs it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T00:06:04-08:00","id":395903,"title":"","content":"Artificers hand is still attached but the coin they make of the molten parts isn't, though they do put it on a chain and wear it around their necks and the whole process does leave their arm a almost unnoticeably smaller than the other one. Other than that example there is no mention of partial soulforging. As for the Oboli, the indivisibility of a soul does mean 1 Oboli = 1 Soul but that Oboli once forged can be broken into pieces, though this is rare as the pieces are not of much use unless combined, that moan and ever so slightly tug towards each other trying to be one again. Do remember that the true value of an Oboli is the fact that it is one souls and as such can be reforged into something more useful, parts of it are less useful to say the least. Also another reason to frown upon breaking Oboli is the fact that the soul will suffer even more than in usual soulforging.<br /> <br /> Partial Moliate on the other hand is somewhat common. You can rip a face of another Wraith and use it to masquerade as him for example so the skinning punishment suggested above would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T01:28:13-08:00","id":395970,"title":"","content":"Will R. Lee Ermey make a cameo in Wr20 The Great War?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T09:35:31-08:00","id":396421,"title":"","content":"Isn't the true purpose of oboli supposedly to keep the soul in questions from feeding Oblivion? <br /> <br /> So you can take an obolus or piece thereof and stretch it out into a short sword if you re-forge it? The true value of an obolus is that it represents both an actual source of material for use as well as a &quot;fixed point&quot; to rate exchange of other goods and services?<br /> <br /> I don't see why Artificers need to strictly adhere to some wraithly principle of conservation of mass. Corpus/ectoplasm isn't matter and it sure seems like you can do all sorts of things with Moliate that indicate mass is not conserved at all. Unless all those wraiths that have huge heads, horns, etc. are really short or hollow or thin. Plus there is the principle that you can turn a person into a coin. Unless oboli are REALLY heavy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:25:39-08:00","id":397209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't the true purpose of oboli supposedly to keep the soul in questions from feeding Oblivion? </div> </div> </div>Technically this is the reason for all Soulforging, it's the only real excuse for such a horrid practice and the worst thing about it is that it isn't an excuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you can take an obolus or piece thereof and stretch it out into a short sword if you re-forge it? The true value of an obolus is that it represents both an actual source of material for use as well as a &quot;fixed point&quot; to rate exchange of other goods and services? </div> </div> </div>Yes to both.<br /> <br /> And for the conservation of mass no, the artificers need not to adhere to such things as proven by the Oboli. The arm thing is mentioned in the Artificer book and likely related to the fact that to an Artificers mind the corpus for his coin has to come from somewhere and as he forges it out of his own hand that's the natural source. Ergo he thinks his arm should have a bit less &quot;mass&quot; and so it does. Just like your actual perception of afterlife and death affects how you look upon your reaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T09:48:58-08:00","id":397692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=397209#post397209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And for the conservation of mass no, the artificers need not to adhere to such things as proven by the Oboli. The arm thing is mentioned in the Artificer book and likely related to the fact that to an Artificers mind the corpus for his coin has to come from somewhere and as he forges it out of his own hand that's the natural source. Ergo he thinks his arm should have a bit less &quot;mass&quot; and so it does. Just like your actual perception of afterlife and death affects how you look upon your reaping.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would think the guys whose job it is to melt one person down to the size of a coin and to take such a coin and then pull it out like expanding taffy to reshape it into a breastplate, sword, boilerplate for a train, etc. wouldn't have some weird hangup about making themselves have a puny arm because a bit of if was pulled off. They are the ones who KNOW that conservation of mass is complete BS with regard to Corpus and plasm. Something they deal with so intimatetly and regularly should be inculcated into their self-image, moreso than a regular wraith. I would buy a non-Artificer (and non-Moliators) having the pschychological hangups and they would be the ones with the self-imposed reductions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:08:45-08:00","id":398434,"title":"","content":"Do we actually have any examples of forgers turning oboli into other things? Perhaps the process of turning a wraith into soulsteel (or whatever) is a one-way, when it's done it's done sort of process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T09:46:46-08:00","id":398917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=398434#post398434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we actually have any examples of forgers turning oboli into other things? Perhaps the process of turning a wraith into soulsteel (or whatever) is a one-way, when it's done it's done sort of process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would buy this. It makes sense that the purpose is to create something as unchanging as possible. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:14:08-08:00","id":399162,"title":"","content":"What sort of Relics and Artifacts will be available in Wr20 and The Great War?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T20:49:52-08:00","id":402909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do we actually have any examples of forgers turning oboli into other things? </div> </div> </div>Page 42 of Artificers Guildbook under Oboli it mentions that part of the true value of the coin is that it is the easiest way to transport forge ready souls and that it is as easy to work with as raw materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:12:38-08:00","id":421302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=395970#post395970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will R. Lee Ermey make a cameo in Wr20 The Great War?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Werner Klemperer, however, might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:22:52-08:00","id":427884,"title":"","content":"How are the The Benandanti these days?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:33:28-07:00","id":438097,"title":"","content":"its been a while, how you been RDG?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:50:54-07:00","id":438280,"title":"","content":"Okay, so over the last 24 hours I've read 38 pages of comments, but I don't think this has been mentioned:<br /> <br /> Rich, will there be enough info on Legions to make them playable from the core book? <br /> <br /> What I mean is, Guilds got their DPS in WtO, and Legions got theirs in WtGW. Because the detailed info on Legions and Guilds never appeared together, in one book, I always felt I had to use both books to create a fully rounded character.<br /> <br /> I know that Legions are kinda like Auspices, but also like Tribes, and that Guilds are kinda like Clans, but also like Disciplines. And I like that. It allows for the most flexibility in creating characters in any oWoD game, excluding Dark Ages: Fae. But as both Arcanoi and the manner of one's death are important in play, I feel both 'splats' should get sizeable write-ups.<br /> <br /> Prior to reading The Book of Legions, I had absolutely no idea how to play everyday death in a Legion, for example. The details on Legion politics and seats were invaluable in WtGW too.<br /> <br /> I'm glad Heretics and Renegades are also getting more space in the core book, as well as spectres. It really opens up the options for play right from the beginning. Half the players in threads here want personal games about fetters and the world of the living, while the other half wants games of dark discovery and intrigue (well, maybe a third each, with a third wanting a bit of both). Presenting all this info together allows for the widest range of styles right out of the box (or out of The Behemoth).<br /> <br /> I'd like to reiterate, too, that the Bush of Ghosts seems a bit of an Orientalist stereotype (more so than the DKoJ), and I'd always suspected its treatment in the sourcebooks was pretty much indicative of the small part Western wraiths are allowed to see of it. Will we get hints of the more nuanced and diverse cultures existing behind this 'magical kingdom' smokescreen? Even a few words to the effect that Western wraiths see what their Imperialist hearts expect to see, but that Africa itself isn't one nation (as Sarah Palin seems to think), would go a long way.<br /> <br /> Finally, as I'm just starting a new game on Skype on Sunday and various players seem to keep arguing about one particular thing, can you give us the tiniest of spoilers from the new book: can wraiths soak aggravated damage or not? The publishing of 2e soak difficulties for fire suggest yes, but the rulebook never stated explicitly the difference between normal and aggravated damage (except in how they're healed). Half the camp thinks wraiths should be soft, and only soak bashing, while the other half thinks they should be hard and soak everything. Or is it the middle way of vampires, with an art or at least armour providing the only way to soak aggravated damage? It has quite a bearing on tone, ultimately.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-12-2015, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:45:05-07:00","id":441574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=438097#post438097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its been a while, how you been RDG?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i1.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/841/773/729.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Does that sound about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:16:18-07:00","id":447650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=441574#post441574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i1.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/841/773/729.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Does that sound about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not dead. Resting. Or possibly pining for the fjords. Or possibly still recovering from GDC Death Crud, which is what happens when you put 26000 game developers in one building for three days.<br /> <br /> Legions - They should be playable from the core book. One of the big goals I have is smoothing out the occasionally incongruent ways Legions, Guilds, and factions fit into Wraith society, which is to say they didn't always play so well together. So not only will you get more on stuff like &quot;What does a Skeletal Legion wraith do day-to-day&quot;, but you'll also get more on how they're likely to interact with a Guildwraith, and how that might be different in, say, Stygia versus the Necropolis of Bowling Green, Kentucky.<br /> <br /> (Yes, that's a nod to Clayton Oliver. Because Clayton is awesome.)<br /> <br /> Damage Rules - We are moving everything forward to the Revised rules set. When I get the playtest pack shined up and spiffy, you'll get the Wraith-specific details.<br /> <br /> Bush of Ghosts - Let's just say that your hypothesizing echoes many of my concerns and thought processes on the issue, and that there is certainly a great deal more to say on the topic than has been said so far. More than that, I'm not ready to divulge because there's a long way to go on that particular part of the manuscript, and it's something I want to handle with the utmost respect and care.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:51:58-07:00","id":447742,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy!<br /> <br /> First off, let me say that I very much appreciate all the work you have put into this Underworld, and that I'm very, very happy to see that kickstarter take off <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Following an internal whim, I recently started to ST Wraith, and then found out about the Kickstarter a month after it closed. Keeping with the theme, I suppose)<br /> <br /> How would someone who has not backed the KS be able to buy the proper, hardcover, shiny Deluxe Edition, on the other side of the Atlantic? I'm willing to preoder it or something, I need that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Passion: Get W:tO20 Deluxe Edition (greed) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:57:39-07:00","id":454434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=447742#post447742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Deadguy!<br /> <br /> First off, let me say that I very much appreciate all the work you have put into this Underworld, and that I'm very, very happy to see that kickstarter take off <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Following an internal whim, I recently started to ST Wraith, and then found out about the Kickstarter a month after it closed. Keeping with the theme, I suppose)<br /> <br /> How would someone who has not backed the KS be able to buy the proper, hardcover, shiny Deluxe Edition, on the other side of the Atlantic? I'm willing to preoder it or something, I need that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Passion: Get W:tO20 Deluxe Edition (greed) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Horrible confession time: I don't know - I'm buried in the content side and haven't actually sniffed at the logistics stuff. Poke Onyx Path directly and they may have a better answer.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T12:33:18-07:00","id":459260,"title":"","content":"I just finished rereading some of the older books and now I'm wondering will we get to know more about the Unlidded Eye this time around? In an underworld of mysteries they always seemed to be the ones furthest from the light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>I'm God's hated messenger, the Devil's cohort<br /> I'm the one they all blame, when a life is cut short<br /> But still if you're willing, to give it a try<br /> I'll beat you at anything, and claim you're last sigh</i><br /> - The Reaper's Tales","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4688-malkira","name":"Malkira","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T06:16:05-07:00","id":459875,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy<br /> <br /> You mentioned in the kickstarter that if a Garou stepped sideways into the Shadowlands, his mundane video camera he took with him to record wraiths with will be mysteriously drained of its battery;<br /> <br /> But what of a Glass Walker Techno-fetish iPad/Camera, which is *designed to work* when one steps sideways into the spirit world, runs on spiritual energy (Gnosis) as opposed to mundane electricity, AND will interface with non-spiritual computers when you are sideways back into Gaia?<br /> <br /> Looks like my werewolf CAN pass Daddy's video message of love to his still-living little girl from Stygia after all, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 03-28-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T12:02:01-07:00","id":460260,"title":"","content":"hey rdg, hows a going boss?<br /> there as a topic discussing how Humans (mortals, nothing supernatural) could pass to the Underworld...do you think this is possible? what would be the Wraiths reaction? what would happend if a human entered stygia?<br /> <br /> <br /> now, for something completely different...<br /> One of my friends/players is WAY into japanesse folklore. We were discussing about places for a future Wraith game and he suggested This place <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara</a><br /> <br /> i think it would be the biggest nightmare fuel, a place that Oblivion wishes to touch upon. The birthplace of some of the strongest Spectres and more cruel spirits.<br /> What do you think? any chances to mention it in the future books if possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 03-31-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T21:10:55-07:00","id":464245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=460260#post460260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey rdg, hows a going boss?<br /> there as a topic discussing how Humans (mortals, nothing supernatural) could pass to the Underworld...do you think this is possible? what would be the Wraiths reaction? what would happend if a human entered stygia?<br /> <br /> <br /> now, for something completely different...<br /> One of my friends/players is WAY into japanesse folklore. We were discussing about places for a future Wraith game and he suggested This place <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aokigahara</a><br /> <br /> i think it would be the biggest nightmare fuel, a place that Oblivion wishes to touch upon. The birthplace of some of the strongest Spectres and more cruel spirits.<br /> What do you think? any chances to mention it in the future books if possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans entering the Underworld happens occasionally (see: Xerxes Jones), usually with bad effects for all concerned. Your average wraith is going to be flummoxed by the sight of a mortal traipsing around the other side - if nothing else, they're REALLY going to stand out, but there are plenty of Legion types who've seen a misplaced Quick before and know what to do (i.e. hustle them off as quickly as possible) to potentially keep things from getting out of hand.<br /> <br /> And Cracked has been doing an occasional series on places like that - check out part 5 here - <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_20704_the-6-creepiest-places-earth-part-5.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/article_20704...th-part-5.html</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T21:11:29-07:00","id":464248,"title":"","content":"Also - <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Just so folks know, I will be assembling a significant portion of Team Wraith at the East Coast Game Conference next week. Charles Bates, Steve Burnett, Mikko Rautalahti and Lucien Soulban will all be huddling for the show, with the possibility of Steve Long stopping by as well. So if you're in the area, come by and say hi </span></span></span><i><u>smile emoticon</u></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T22:24:09-07:00","id":473889,"title":"","content":"hey RDG, hows a going? what you been up to? hows the family and the book?.<br /> <br /> little question, how does time runs in the Underworld?. i mean, GTM? does the day progress at the same time as in the land of the livings? and other thing...is there a sun? or is always Dark?<br /> <br /> Geographically speaking..does each place in the world has a spiritual counterpart on the Underworld? if so, where would you find Stygia in a map? and when it comes to buildings being destroyed and such, do they slowly appear on the Underworld ?<br /> <br /> P.S Sussudio<br /> <br /> Atte: your favorite bastard, Crowley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T01:23:46-07:00","id":473978,"title":"","content":"Hey Crowley, <br /> <br /> I always describe the Shadowlands as being like an alternate dimension. It occupies roughly the same space and time, but sits on top of the dimensions we see. So time would run exactly the same as in the Skinlands. In the Labyrinth, or deep in the Tempest, however, things become a bit more abstract...<br /> <br /> In terms of Stygia, it exists in yet another dimension. While the Shadowlands can best be imagined as a transparent grey shroud draped over the mortal world, the Tempest is like hyperspace. It exists under the Shadowlands, connecting every bit to every other bit. Stygia exists as an oasis within that hyperspace. Think of it as a pocket reality or, if we instead imagine the Tempest as a nebula, as a star or planet within the cloud.<br /> <br /> Thus, Stygia doesn't correlate at all with anything on a human map, because it exists in a place where space is fundamentally different.<br /> <br /> In terms of the sun in the Shadowlands, I'll return to the idea above of that plane being like a shroud over the Skinlands. The sun would shine through such a shroud, but its light would be dimmed and slowed down. It's going to be dull and red, or at least dark orange. <br /> <br /> If you look at the cover of The Hierarchy, that has an orange sky that might give you an indication of the sky of the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:33:38-07:00","id":474851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0FJNZyhRfA4\" data-code=\"0FJNZyhRfA4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0FJNZyhRfA4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Will you sit up with the dead?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:24:46-07:00","id":475090,"title":"","content":"ok, this might sound like a bit of trivia.. But anyways.<br /> <br /> Hows the Weather in Stygia, we already stablished that theres storms once on a while. but does it rain? is Normal rain or industrial acid rain? does it snow or we got snow in the form of ashes a la Silent Hill or The Schindlers List ? Is there a Sun and Moon cycle ?<br /> <br /> and i wondered if people in Coma or Vegetative State could Enter the Underworld","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:59:24-07:00","id":475908,"title":"","content":"Stygia exists within the Tempest so it's weather is like that of the Tempest surrounding it except that the walls are designed to protect the inhabitants from the worse effects of the Maelstroms. Sun and the Moon do not exists within the Tempest ergo no such things can be seen from Stygia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i wondered if people in Coma or Vegetative State could Enter the Underworld </div> </div> </div>With a little nudge from a Sandman, sure. But it's an ST call on what the situation with their soul is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T11:50:49-07:00","id":487474,"title":"","content":"Weather in the Underworld is disturbingly similar to late fall in Connecticut. It's usually grey, but when the skies do clear what you get are the reddish skies of incoming storms, not shining blue. The rain is not omnipresent, but it's frequent enough, and even when it's not raining it looks like it's about to. The rain itself ranges from light drizzle to full on hurricane-force gales. <br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:21:08-07:00","id":487769,"title":"","content":"oi RDG. hows a going? is itt truth the rumor about &quot;Wraith the Musical&quot;? if so, why do i keep imagining you singing a cover from Rocke me amadeus but with wraiths<br /> <i>He is a ghost, he is a ghost he is a ghost<br /> Im a Wraith!!<br /> he is a wraith he is a wraith, he is a wraith..Ohh he is a wraith<br /> Whats wrong with me?!.<br /> Youre dead now<br /> Want a second opinion!<br /> youre also lazy<br /> He is a wraith he is a wraith<br /> Can i play the piano anymore?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> of course you cant, your shadow can too<br /> <br /> <i>and lets not forget about the Shadow Song<br /> I hate every wraith i see<br /> From Shakespeare There to Tupac Here<br /> No, youll never make soulforge out of me<br /> Oh My God! i was wrong! The legions took me all along!<br /> you finally made soulforge out of me!!<br /> Yes they finally made Soulforge out of Me!.<br /> I hate you Filthy legions! </i><br /> <br /> <br /> Ok now with the actual questions:<br /> <br /> Why do certail buildings appear on The Underworld why others dont?<br /> <br /> Have you seen any Anime That you could use as Inspiration for Wraith? (a friend keeps Insisting that The Grave for the Fireflies could be about a haunting).<br /> <br /> Theres a thing i dont fully understand, in order to become transparent in the Skinlands, the Wraith must be 'Harmed'/ mark a Corpus box. Why is this?, why a wraith cant simply go through solid objects with out getting &quot;Hurt.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can a Risen still operate with a Bullet on the head? ( i mean like Be Aware of whats going on?), and If beheaded, can his head still work?<br /> <br /> Do the Wraiths of Chernobyl have their own Arcanos related to radiation or thats just stupid?<br /> <br /> Can a spectre be born out of a place fill with Negative energy? or these have to be created from oblivion itself?<br /> <br /> Can a fetter enter stygia or do wraiths operate their fetters from the Skinlands?<br /> <br /> Do all Spectres are insane and feel no remorse of their actions? or its possible for an expection (See Edward Mordrake from American Horror Story: Freakshow)<br /> <br /> Can Soulforged objects enter the Skinlands or be used by a Quick?<br /> <br /> Any chances to takle on Heretics based off real cults such as Jim Jones and the Koresh family?<br /> <br /> Speaking of Jim Jones, The Hunters Survival Guide mentions hauntings by the people of Jim Jones, any thoughts about it from a Wraith point of view?.<br /> <br /> What happend when very Infamous/Evil individuals fall into Stygia? Do they get Soulforging right away, does The Oblivion Recruits them right away? any chances for them to recieve the &quot;Benefict of Doubt&quot;?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:18:55-07:00","id":487910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=487769#post487769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok now with the actual questions:<br /> <br /> Why do certail buildings appear on The Underworld why others dont?<br /> <br /> Have you seen any Anime That you could use as Inspiration for Wraith? (a friend keeps Insisting that The Grave for the Fireflies could be about a haunting).<br /> <br /> Theres a thing i dont fully understand, in order to become transparent in the Skinlands, the Wraith must be 'Harmed'/ mark a Corpus box. Why is this?, why a wraith cant simply go through solid objects with out getting &quot;Hurt.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can a Risen still operate with a Bullet on the head? ( i mean like Be Aware of whats going on?), and If beheaded, can his head still work?<br /> <br /> Do the Wraiths of Chernobyl have their own Arcanos related to radiation or thats just stupid?<br /> <br /> Can a spectre be born out of a place fill with Negative energy? or these have to be created from oblivion itself?<br /> <br /> Can a fetter enter stygia or do wraiths operate their fetters from the Skinlands?<br /> <br /> Do all Spectres are insane and feel no remorse of their actions? or its possible for an expection (See Edward Mordrake from American Horror Story: Freakshow)<br /> <br /> Can Soulforged objects enter the Skinlands or be used by a Quick?<br /> <br /> Any chances to takle on Heretics based off real cults such as Jim Jones and the Koresh family?<br /> <br /> Speaking of Jim Jones, The Hunters Survival Guide mentions hauntings by the people of Jim Jones, any thoughts about it from a Wraith point of view?.<br /> <br /> What happend when very Infamous/Evil individuals fall into Stygia? Do they get Soulforging right away, does The Oblivion Recruits them right away? any chances for them to recieve the &quot;Benefict of Doubt&quot;?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the immortal words of Monty Python, &quot;Stop that. You're not going into a song while I'm here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, questions. <br /> 1-Certain buildings inspire more emotion over their lifetimes than others. That's the distinction as to what crosses over after it's destroyed in the Skinlands and what doesn't. Your average 7-11? Not likely to make the trip. A parish church that stood for generations? Better odds.<br /> <br /> 2-That's &quot;The Rule of Ouch&quot; coming into effect. Basically, there needs to be some bending in one direction or another on this stuff or you end up with people getting knocked into Harrowings by a light rain shower.<br /> <br /> 3-It's hard to stop a Risen. Really, really hard. You're better off severing the leg tendons.<br /> <br /> 4-Not yet they don't....but damn, do I want to find a way to work some of those old Soviet Science Cities into Wraith.<br /> <br /> 5-Spectres are all about tapping into the main vein of Oblivion, at least at the get-go.<br /> <br /> 6-Fetters should stay in the Skinlands. Bad things can happen when you bring them into the Underworld. In other words, Don't Cross The Streams, Especially When One Of Those Streams Is The River Styx<br /> <br /> 7-Spectres have Psyches, and Redemption is theoretically a thing. Theoretically...<br /> <br /> 8-It would be very uncomfortable for a mortal to use something Soulforged. I'd wear gloves. Really thick ones.<br /> <br /> 9-The cult model is one interesting one for Heretics, but we're going to be casting a slightly broader net. <br /> <br /> 10-Considering what happened there, I can certainly see some folks sticking around post-mortem. And I highly recommend Tim Cahill's piece on the aftermath - It's in his book A Wolverine Is Eating My Leg.<br /> <br /> 11-The dumb ones get caught and soulforged. There's quite the collectors' market for knicknacks made from famous jerkwads. The smart ones, on the other hand....<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:31:23-07:00","id":487953,"title":"","content":"Ok, this might come off a bit strange but i been interested in getting the ShadowsPlayers Guide through the RPGDriveThrough.<br /> The thing is that my main turnoff its how many reviews say that the book its not much of a PrinterFriendly since its black on White. i have no problems paying for it but i want my printer to live to tell the tale xD. long story short, WIll Wr20 be Printer Friendly?<br /> <br /> P.S: what does it takes to get a shoutout on the new book xD?<br /> <br /> P.S 2 : Why do i keep having this weird idea that whenever you see a question posted by me you go &quot;Oh god, not him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ps3. Thanks for all the patience and for being such a trooper!.<br /> <br /> As for the Science Sites, you could use them as Torture camps using old abandoned technology in answer to the nuclear arsenal, maybe the radioactivity creating some new kind of Spectre (Not based of the Nuclear effect, but rather the Dread caused on the people who lived in those areas). Interesting enough, i was watching this SyFy Channel's Destination Truth and they headed to Chernobyl, the guys doing the documentary Claimed that whenever they saw an Aparition of some sorts, there was a Ping on Radioactivity. You could use that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> or maybe turn all the Scientific Purpoused Towns (like the ones where nukes were tried out, chernobyl and such) as one massive Necropoli devided between Scientists and Test Sub- Civilians i mean..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 04-22-2015, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:44:30-07:00","id":490168,"title":"","content":"Quick question - what is the plural of &quot;Risen&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:55:26-07:00","id":490170,"title":"","content":"Risen. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T03:07:01-07:00","id":490372,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy, dear forum!<br /> <br /> 1, If possible, I'd like to see some background in the new Rulebook detailing the worth of an Obolus. How much does an Obolus get you? How much for a relic broadsword? How much for a fine, soulforged, detailed cigarette holder, etc? I currently handwave costs and income as the story dictates, but the lack of anything concrete makes for some holes in world-building.<br /> <br /> 2, I'd like to see some exploration of the Wraith-appropriate sides of sexuality in the setting. For all the sexually suggestive illustrations, sex does not seem to play a big role in the Shadowlands. I get both the in and out-of-game reasons for this. But, for example, one of my homebrew antagonists is a thanato-sexual Puppeteer who chases the Big Death just after experiencing the little death. The eroticism of the act of dying gives you a lot of room to play with. <br /> I'd like to see stuff like that, or very (explicitly) non-consensual wraithly BDSM or something fucked up to rile up the players. (no misrepresentations of consensual BDSM, please)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T03:11:40-07:00","id":490373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=487953#post487953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S 2 : Why do i keep having this weird idea that whenever you see a question posted by me you go &quot;Oh god, not him.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for RealDeadguy but you have asked a lot of questions. Possibly more so than many others in this thread. If I were worrying about that, I'd perhaps ask if it was fair of me to request a disproportionate amount of time off a developer compared to other people, and whether that counts as a social faux pas (then again, I'm British, so we expect to queue and wait our turn...). But it looks like Deadguy is happy to answer for the time being.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you do ask a lot of questions which have already been answered elsewhere, however. Those get a bit repetitive. You should try the White Wolf Wiki as a first port of call, perhaps? Some of the questions you've asked are answered over there: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/</a><br /> <br /> This isn't meant to be shady, BTW. It's just that you did ask. And every question you ask pulls Deadguy away from finishing that book we all want to see so urgently <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:09:22-07:00","id":490727,"title":"","content":"Hi Deadguy!<br /> <br /> I am reposting a couple quick questions that got passed over earlier. It has been awhile since I posted, but I would really like to know the following:<br /> <br /> (And I do know the revised Arcanois are in progress.)<br /> <br /> 1. When a wraith uses Embody, Corpse or Slip the Lethan Bonds, can they still see into the world of the Restless and affect it?<br /> <br /> 2. How does a wraith using embody look to other wraiths. The Quick glow, but an Embodied wraith would look...?<br /> <br /> 3. Can Usury Level 2 be used to heal aggravated damage? (Referring to WtO 2nd edition and GW) Someone else asked this but I would like to know too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 4. Songs of the Living (GW) affects Spectres, does it also bolster wraiths within hearing of it too?<br /> <br /> 5. Requiem (WtO 2nd ed.) targets wraiths, but since the emotions can be either positive or negative, can this version be used on Spectres as well?<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Katrina<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:40:08-07:00","id":492120,"title":"","content":"I have a request more for Wraith's integration with the other gamelines than for within W20 itself: could you <b><i>please</i></b> keep the game's primary antagonists as Wraith-specific antagonists and not denegrate both the original creations of other line developers and figures adapted from real life religions and cultural myths by &quot;revealing&quot; that none of them are real and they're in fact hallucinations of sleeping Neverborn? That really came off as arrogant and dismissive to me in previous editions of the games, and didn't make sense within the context of the Mage and Werewolf settings where the Underworld is only one of several aspects of the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:10:15-07:00","id":492240,"title":"","content":"@Katrina Let's see if I remember the answers to some of those questions, to help shoulder the weight for Deadguy. Please remember that I may be recalling incorrectly, though I'm pretty sure of the answers (else I wouldn't be posting them).<br /> <br /> 1) Yes. Lifesight and Deathsight are inherent in being a wraith, no matter their corporeal state.<br /> 2) Embodied wraiths look more metaphysically &quot;solid.&quot; No, I'm not exactly sure what that means. Do with the information what you will.<br /> 3) Yes.<br /> 4) It may, though there is no mechanical benefit. It was created to specifically target Spectres.<br /> 5) Yes.<br /> <br /> And @Matt the Bruins fan I'm sure you're aware, but metaphysical contextualization across game lines is... Well, White Wolf staffers have gone on record stating that the games were originally developed independently; that even if one had a <i>Vampire</i> game with werewolves that called themselves Garou, that were completely lifted wholesale from <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>, they were <u>still</u> not the Garou from <i>W:tA</i>. Each game line was it's own separate &quot;mirror universe.&quot; Trying to make sense of one game's metaphysics and cosmology through the lens of another is a maddening (and futile) exercise.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:12:12-07:00","id":492338,"title":"","content":"I think Matt is referring to a Mage source-books, Book of Madness and Book of Madness Revised specifically, that tell us that the Outer Beings revered by the K'llashaa faction of the Nephandi are actually mere dreams of the Neverborn. Some take offence at this for some reason while I find it particularly cool, so YMMV. But this is something posited in a Mage books not in Wraith and so isn't actually a problem with the Wraith line. If one of Mage's own source book says that one class of beings antagonistic to creation itself is actually a mere dream fragment of a more powerful being antagonistic to creation itself I see no harm in that nor do I see how exactly is this not making sense in the Mage setting as it is intrinsically a mage thing and doesn't actually affect Werewolf at all, as the Outer Beings would just be Wyrm creatures to them, as would anything associated with Oblivion or Neverborn as that is just the way the Garou roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T23:46:39-07:00","id":492381,"title":"","content":"Simple but complex question.<br /> Could a place fill with Bad Mojo ( like a Torture Center or a place of mass suicides) be a Breeding Ground for Spectres? Or a place with such a Dark history would make for easy Nihils to The Laberyth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T03:07:31-07:00","id":492473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=492381#post492381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple but complex question.<br /> Could a place fill with Bad Mojo ( like a Torture Center or a place of mass suicides) be a Breeding Ground for Spectres? Or a place with such a Dark history would make for easy Nihils to The Laberyth?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of examples of this in the books, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:56:21-07:00","id":493225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=492338#post492338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Matt is referring to a Mage source-books, Book of Madness and Book of Madness Revised specifically, that tell us that the Outer Beings revered by the K'llashaa faction of the Nephandi are actually mere dreams of the Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>When that retcon came down the pike (beginning in Book of Mirrors), it wasn't restricted to the things worshipped by the K'llashaa. It was said to apply to ALL the entities the Nephandi served. So, werewolves and mages were deluded about the nature of Maeljin Incarnae, Cthulhu Mythos creatures, demons, and the evil gods worshipped by dozens of human religions - they were <i>all</i> explained away as made-up hallucinations somehow projected into the Astral, Middle, and Deep Umbrae by Dark Umbral presences that should be even less able to interact with the worlds of the living than spectres. And I guess angels, spirits of Gaia and the rest of the Triat, and divine figures from those same human religions were also all completely ignorant of the nature of enemy figures from their various belief systems.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't object to the Neverborn as presented within the context of the Wraith game; it's when they get exported into Mage (and by implication Werewolf) as <i>replacements</i> for the existing mythologies of those games that I cry foul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T05:44:42-07:00","id":493500,"title":"","content":"Werewolf Crossover Questions:<br /> 1A) Would a Specter &quot;Stink of the Wyrm&quot; when the Gift &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; is used on it? <br /> 1B) How about a normally kind and generous wraith, but now under Catharsis and hence controlled by his shadow?<br /> 1C) For that matter, how many points of Angst would a Wraith need to possess before he &quot;Stinks of the Wyrn&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) It's stated that Garou and other Fera melt into Spirit Form when they step sideways.<br /> Soulforging melts and turns Spirits into malleable material for manufactured goods.<br /> A) So; would you be able to Soulforge a Garou, Fera or Black Spiral Dancer who has stepped sideways into the Shadowlands?<br /> B) For that mater, would you be able to soulforge Gaian Spirits, Weaver Spirits and Banes who wander into the Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:28:46-07:00","id":493695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=493500#post493500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf Crossover Questions:<br /> 1A) Would a Specter &quot;Stink of the Wyrm&quot; when the Gift &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; is used on it?<br /> 1B) How about a normally kind and generous wraith, but now under Catharsis and hence controlled by his shadow?<br /> 1C) For that matter, how many points of Angst would a Wraith need to possess before he &quot;Stinks of the Wyrn&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) It's stated that Garou and other Fera melt into Spirit Form when they step sideways.<br /> Soulforging melts and turns Spirits into malleable material for manufactured goods.<br /> A) So; would you be able to Soulforge a Garou, Fera or Black Spiral Dancer who has stepped sideways into the Shadowlands?<br /> B) For that mater, would you be able to soulforge Gaian Spirits, Weaver Spirits and Banes who wander into the Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>IANRDG, but the Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook covers the first question and hints heavily at the second. Specters appear to Garou and Fera as like unto banes and always ping on SW. Wraiths don't, unless their Angst is higher than their Willpower. There's no mention made of Catharsis affecting this, but it might. As for soulforging, Garou are partially composed of ephemera rather than plasm, so it won't work on them any more than Moliate would*, most likely. Likewise, Middle Umbral spirits wouldn't be viable soulforging material, either.<br /> <br /> (Also, Garou and Fera don't melt into spirit form, they turn inside out. They're still meatbags at heart while in the Umbra.)<br /> <br /> *Moliate explicitly does not work on Garou and Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:38:15-07:00","id":494304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=487953#post487953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, this might come off a bit strange but i been interested in getting the ShadowsPlayers Guide through the RPGDriveThrough.<br /> The thing is that my main turnoff its how many reviews say that the book its not much of a PrinterFriendly since its black on White. i have no problems paying for it but i want my printer to live to tell the tale xD. long story short, WIll Wr20 be Printer Friendly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for Wr20 but it is worth noting that the Shadow Player's Guide was intentionally an inverse of the normal books, white text on black instead of black text on white. Basically it was a nod to the nature of the Shadow and its relationship to the wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:19:04-07:00","id":495918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=494304#post494304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak for Wr20 but it is worth noting that the Shadow Player's Guide was intentionally an inverse of the normal books, white text on black instead of black text on white. Basically it was a nod to the nature of the Shadow and its relationship to the wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>i was aware of it, im just worried for the printer sake.<br /> <br /> Ok, time for more weirdness with Crowley.<br /> A Wraith uses Embody...<br /> What happends if he tries to get erm..Intimate with someone while using Embody?<br /> <br /> Can a fetter be someone Dead?<br /> <br /> As to come to soulforgin, we stablished how horrible can the process be but<br /> 1._ Concidering that its made of a soul (or souls), can a wraith actually Comunicate with the souls used for the materials?<br /> 2._ Using Moliate, can a wraith imitate the state of a Soulforged object (to confuse someone)?<br /> <br /> Could Mnemosis be used to restore a computer's missing files or it only works with The Living?<br /> <br /> this might come a bit off but im still confused about something, perhaps you guys could help me out. Im still trying to get some of the books.<br /> When it comes to embody, what are the weapon limits when it comes to size, ammount and resilance to damage.<br /> Can an X number of Wraiths be used to create One Being (like the Tzimisces Do for their Meat Golems) if so, can the wraiths Split up from this?<br /> Someone who died while drunk/high. could be a wraith who constantly high and never being able of sober up? (Im seing you guy from Dead Like Me and Jimmy Bones, Spectre Snoop Dog), also, to which legion would someone who died of Overdose fit in?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 04-29-2015, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T04:28:52-07:00","id":496179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i was aware of it, im just worried for the printer sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll use a lot of black ink, but I can't see your printer blowing up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, time for more weirdness with Crowley.<br /> A Wraith uses Embody...<br /> What happends if he tries to get erm..Intimate with someone while using Embody?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly the same as if they were human. Bear in mind, though, that the power only lasts for one breath per success unless the wraith is attuned to the human in question. Since breath is more rapid during sex, the wraith probably won't get far with a non-attuned mortal. With an attuned mortal, however, they can have a marathon shagfest, but be warned that the sensations would be overwhelming for a wraith who hasn't experienced these feelings in a long time. You might need to spend Willpower to continue, as every nerve ending would be alive again, and the wraith's mind would probably be assaulted by the power of feeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a fetter be someone Dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a corpse, but it can't be another wraith. A fetter has to be something in the Skindlands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to come to soulforgin, we stablished how horrible can the process be but<br /> 1._ Concidering that its made of a soul (or souls), can a wraith actually Comunicate with the souls used for the materials?<br /> 2._ Using Moliate, can a wraith imitate the state of a Soulforged object (to confuse someone)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No. Soulforging apparently destroys the consciousness of the subject.<br /> 2. Yes, with Moliate 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Mnemosis be used to restore a computer's missing files or it only works with The Living?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mnemosynis works with the dead and the living. It wouldn't work with a computer. I think there's a power for this with Inhabit or Flux, though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this might come a bit off but im still confused about something, perhaps you guys could help me out. Im still trying to get some of the books.<br /> When it comes to embody, what are the weapon limits when it comes to size, ammount and resilance to damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean? When a wraith embodies, she takes damage like a human, so would be vulnerable to all weapons in the Skinlands. But while she can embody and might be able to bring over items with her, these items won't survive in the Skinlands and will dissolve soon after leaving her person. Bullets, for instance, would fly from a relic pistol and then dissolve mid-air. They're not real, and it's only their being on the wraith's person that makes them appear tangible. It might be possible to strike someone with a relic sword brought over, but that's the ST's call.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an X number of Wraiths be used to create One Being (like the Tzimisces Do for their Meat Golems) if so, can the wraiths Split up from this?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's via Moliate, this might be possible. The effects of Moliate 5 are usually temporary anyway.<br /> <br /> If it's via soulforging, then no, as above. The individual wraiths would've lost their consciousnesses anyway, but soulforging is usually permanent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone who died while drunk/high. could be a wraith who constantly high and never being able of sober up? (Im seing you guy from Dead Like Me and Jimmy Bones, Spectre Snoop Dog), also, to which legion would someone who died of Overdose fit in?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they wouldn't, because they have no physical body to be intoxicated. You might come up with some interesting Merits and Flaws, though, or even some unique Thorns. It might also have a bearing on Nature and Demeanour.<br /> <br /> Someone who died of an OD might be victims of fate, victims of violence or victims of illness. It depends upon the manner of their death. These things are usually pretty fluid, and open to interpretation. Or rather, they usually depend on who's around to reap a new wraith, and who they decide to sell/trade the wraith to. A Reaper probably has no qualms with flogging a recently reaped Enfant to the highest bidder, despite the protestations of other Legions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T04:48:42-07:00","id":496182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496179#post496179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. No. Soulforging apparently destroys the consciousness of the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, the draft for Wr20 Inhabit has, as the highest Ancient Art, the ability to get knowledge from a soulforged object by questioning it; the object gives a vision or a moaned response in reply if it knows the answer (however, the Art can only be used once, <i>ever</i>, on a given object). Whether this is psychometry or actual communication with a fraction of a wraith's trapped consciousness is the subject of ongoing and bitter debate among the Artificers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:58:40-07:00","id":496207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=495918#post495918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a fetter be someone Dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is important to point out the purpose of a fetter: It is something that ties a wraith to the lands of the living. This thing is important to the wraith in some way, that the wraith has difficulty leaving behind. Once that thing is gone, it no longer keeps the wraith tied to the Skinlands. A family heriloom melted down into silver is no longer an heirloom. A favorite tree chopped down and the surrounding area turned into a parking lot is no longer the place it was. By the same token, the corpse of a person is not the person any longer... the person is gone. There is nobody to stick around for. No heirloom to protect. No tree to rest beneath the shade of. It's gone.<br /> <br /> In many ways I think most domems don't miss the ability to visit the shadowlands. After all, everything that kept them there in the first place is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:36:23-07:00","id":496255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496182#post496182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, the draft for Wr20 Inhabit has, as the highest Ancient Art, the ability to get knowledge from a soulforged object by questioning it; the object gives a vision or a moaned response in reply if it knows the answer (however, the Art can only be used once, <i>ever</i>, on a given object). Whether this is psychometry or actual communication with a fraction of a wraith's trapped consciousness is the subject of ongoing and bitter debate among the Artificers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! There was always a suggestion that, yes, soulforged items do retain vestiges of consciousness. But the official word from the Hierarchy was always that consciousness is beaten out of it. I like this power.<br /> <br /> If a soulforged item were to retain its consciousness, I imagine it'd quickly become a spectre, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:53:45-07:00","id":496391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496255#post496255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice! There was always a suggestion that, yes, soulforged items do retain vestiges of consciousness. But the official word from the Hierarchy was always that consciousness is beaten out of it. I like this power.<br /> <br /> If a soulforged item were to retain its consciousness, I imagine it'd quickly become a spectre, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah but i doubt an evil toaster or a lamp can do much against you<br /> <br /> <br /> also, what i meant about the limits of moliate i meant this.<br /> for example i want to use moliate to create a sword, Can it be a great sword? can i make a sanbato? can i make seppirith's fucking sword? what dereminates the size and weight of a weapon when using moliate ,as well how much damage can the object take before it breaks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 04-29-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:05:14-07:00","id":496399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496179#post496179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone who died of an OD might be victims of fate, victims of violence or victims of illness. It depends upon the manner of their death. These things are usually pretty fluid, and open to interpretation. Or rather, they usually depend on who's around to reap a new wraith, and who they decide to sell/trade the wraith to. A Reaper probably has no qualms with flogging a recently reaped Enfant to the highest bidder, despite the protestations of other Legions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure the Silent Legion will be ALL OVER anyone who dies of an OD if the drug was self-administered. I'm sure the Grim Legion Reapers will get into great arguments with the Penitent Legion about the neurological basis for the propensity to addiction vs. psychological causes (With the Penitents waving around Relic copies of the DSM-IV emphatically). If it was someone who only meant to get high but got bad dope (or REALLY good dope) or didn't self-medicate with appropriate dosage levels for some accidental reason, the Emerald Legion would rear it's head. But, if you go back to the root cause for a lot of really grim long-term addictions that lead to OD, those would probably be the bread and butter of the recruitment pool for the Silent Legion.<br /> <br /> Fate takes whom it wills. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:08:06-07:00","id":496401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=490372#post490372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Deadguy, dear forum!<br /> <br /> 1, If possible, I'd like to see some background in the new Rulebook detailing the worth of an Obolus. How much does an Obolus get you? How much for a relic broadsword? How much for a fine, soulforged, detailed cigarette holder, etc? I currently handwave costs and income as the story dictates, but the lack of anything concrete makes for some holes in world-building.</div> </div> </div> </div>One obolus is equal to one soul, which is roughly to equal a decent chair in raw materials; specifically, the mass/density ratio of a wraith is equivalent to the mass/density ratio of whatever single item one if trying to forge (any &quot;scraps&quot; are melted down to be used in other forging). So, 1 obolus = 1 decent chair = 1 soul. Wraiths aren't worth much. Much like a real-world artisan crafts fair, cost is variable depending on labour. Your cigarette-holder, for example, may cost two or three oboli depending on craftsmanship (say, costs of 5/8ths of an obolus in raw materials, but then the rest in the intricate labour and detailing).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2, I'd like to see some exploration of the Wraith-appropriate sides of sexuality in the setting. For all the sexually suggestive illustrations, sex does not seem to play a big role in the Shadowlands. I get both the in and out-of-game reasons for this. But, for example, one of my homebrew antagonists is a thanato-sexual Puppeteer who chases the Big Death just after experiencing the little death. The eroticism of the act of dying gives you a lot of room to play with.<br /> I'd like to see stuff like that, <b>or very (explicitly) non-consensual wraithly BDSM or something fucked up to rile up the players</b>. (no misrepresentations of consensual BDSM, please. </div> </div> </div>Whatever you do at your own table is fine, but it makes no sense to publish something that has a high chance of alienating a consumer base. So I doubt you'll ever see something like this (it would be the first <i>Wraith</i> book I <i>didn't</i> buy, for instance).<br /> <br /> And finally, maybe Crowley means Inhabit, like &quot;When using Inhabit on a weapon, what are the etc.,?&quot; Yes, no? Edit: Okay, so Moliate, not Inhabit or Embody.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":".  Last two posts happened as I was typing :/ 04-29-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:25:21-07:00","id":496418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496401#post496401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One obolus is equal to one soul, which is roughly to equal a decent chair in raw materials; specifically, the mass/density ratio of a wraith is equivalent to the mass/density ratio of whatever single item one if trying to forge (any &quot;scraps&quot; are melted down to be used in other forging). So, 1 obolus = 1 decent chair = 1 soul. Wraiths aren't worth much. Much like a real-world artisan crafts fair, cost is variable depending on labour. Your cigarette-holder, for example, may cost two or three oboli depending on craftsmanship (say, costs of 5/8ths of an obolus in raw materials, but then the rest in the intricate labour and detailing).Whatever you do at your own table is fine, but it makes no sense to publish something that has a high chance of alienating a consumer base. So I doubt you'll ever see something like this (it would be the first <i>Wraith</i> book I <i>didn't</i> buy, for instance).<br /> <br /> And finally, maybe Crowley means Inhabit, like &quot;When using Inhabit on a weapon, what are the etc.,?&quot; Yes, no?<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuk re: the rape bit. Seriously, can we not? It's not okay to mess with your players like this.<br /> <br /> Back to the costs of an obolus: this has been very poorly defined in the past. One soul is an obolus, but so is a chair. I don't think it's a matter of one obolus will buy you whatever else can be made from one soul, because then things would vary so much. Also, there are likely to be more souls in circulation as coins than as chairs, which means chairs would be more valuable, even if they're made from the same thing. A pile of bricks is less expensive than a house, for example.<br /> <br /> Onto Moliate: you can make any kind of sword you want from it, provided you have the skill required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-30-2015, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:54:26-07:00","id":496433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496418#post496418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yuk. Missed the rape bit. Crowley, can you calm down a bit, please? I know you get giddy and everything, but seriously, can we not? It's not okay to mess with your players like this.<br /> <br /> Back to the costs of an obolus: this has been very poorly defined in the past. One soul is an obolus, but so is a chair. I don't think it's a matter of one obolus will buy you whatever else can be made from one soul, because then things would vary so much. Also, there are likely to be more souls in circulation as coins than as chairs, which means chairs would be more valuable, even if they're made from the same thing. A pile of bricks is less expensive than a house, for example.<br /> <br /> Onto Moliate: you can make any kind of sword you want from it, provided you have the skill required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no! No, it wasn't Crowley who asked that. Crowley's fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for obolus costs, yeah, that's why I made mention of an artisan crafts market. It's not an exact &quot;1 obolus = 1chair =1 soul,&quot; more like &quot;1 obolus = 1 soul, and 1soul = 1 chair, but you still have to pay for craftsmanship and materials.&quot; Part of the worth for an obolus is how malleable and easy to forge it is; an item like a chair needs to be smelted down before it can be reforged, but an obolus can go from one's pocket straight to the anvil. Along with how portable it is, since one is basically carrying around raw materials that can create <i>anything</i> in a coin roughly two inches in diameter and maybe a quarter of an inch thick.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 04-29-2015, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T11:08:25-07:00","id":496481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496418#post496418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yuk. Missed the rape bit. Crowley, can you calm down a bit, please? I know you get giddy and everything, but seriously, can we not? It's not okay to mess with your players like this.<br /> <br /> Back to the costs of an obolus: this has been very poorly defined in the past. One soul is an obolus, but so is a chair. I don't think it's a matter of one obolus will buy you whatever else can be made from one soul, because then things would vary so much. Also, there are likely to be more souls in circulation as coins than as chairs, which means chairs would be more valuable, even if they're made from the same thing. A pile of bricks is less expensive than a house, for example.<br /> <br /> Onto Moliate: you can make any kind of sword you want from it, provided you have the skill required.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt ask about rape :S got the wrong user over there<br /> <br /> I was asking about moliate and creating weaponry out of it. Sizes, restrictions , damages and of a wraith could be moliated onto a firearm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T11:53:50-07:00","id":496557,"title":"","content":"Yeah creating small items from souls has never made much sense especially with the oboli. I prefer the idea that your average adult soul has roughly the same mass and that with one soul you can create an object the size of a chair or a several smaller objects, with some runoff. With the oboli I'd take a que from the Jade currency from Exalted. Basically one large piece of Jade broken down into smaller and smaller pieces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496179#post496179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone who died of an OD might be victims of fate, victims of violence or victims of illness. It depends upon the manner of their death. These things are usually pretty fluid, and open to interpretation. Or rather, they usually depend on who's around to reap a new wraith, and who they decide to sell/trade the wraith to. A Reaper probably has no qualms with flogging a recently reaped Enfant to the highest bidder, despite the protestations of other Legions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a quick little note, but the Legion of Fate only recruits wraiths that possess certain Deathmarks, signifying that they've been marked by Fate. If another Legion frees a wraith with those marks from a caul they will hand them over to the Legion of Fate without a fight regardless of how they died.<br /> <br /> I think if I remember correctly, even some of those that sell freshly reaped Enfants as slaves or send them to the forges hesitate if they find one with those markings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:37:43-07:00","id":496606,"title":"","content":"Oboli seem like they are made of concentrated metallic taffy. Only without mass conservation issues. <br /> <br /> Doesn't it seem like the Legion of Fate would KNOW when a wraith would arrive with the appropriate Deathmark and be standing by to scoop them up. Or to scoop them up when fate decreed that they do so.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it suck to have the Deathmarks of Fate and have the fate of being Reaped and then Soulforged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:04:16-07:00","id":497297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496481#post496481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didnt ask about rape :S got the wrong user over there<br /> <br /> I was asking about moliate and creating weaponry out of it. Sizes, restrictions , damages and of a wraith could be moliated onto a firearm</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies! I mistook that. I think it was in bold in nothing's quote, so I assumed it was from the original post. Disturbing thought whoever it was from...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:17:26-07:00","id":497307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496606#post496606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oboli seem like they are made of concentrated metallic taffy. Only without mass conservation issues.<br /> <br /> Doesn't it seem like the Legion of Fate would KNOW when a wraith would arrive with the appropriate Deathmark and be standing by to scoop them up. Or to scoop them up when fate decreed that they do so.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it suck to have the Deathmarks of Fate and have the fate of being Reaped and then Soulforged?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure would :P<br /> <br /> Re: oboli, I'd assumed that the soulforging process actually stripped the wraith's corpus down to its last remaining point, and then this was converted into the obolus. I could be wrong, and oboli could just be really, incredibly dense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:01:44-07:00","id":497587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496606#post496606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oboli seem like they are made of concentrated metallic taffy. Only without mass conservation issues.<br /> <br /> Doesn't it seem like the Legion of Fate would KNOW when a wraith would arrive with the appropriate Deathmark and be standing by to scoop them up. Or to scoop them up when fate decreed that they do so.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it suck to have the Deathmarks of Fate and have the fate of being Reaped and then Soulforged?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Legion have a Fatalism Art for knowing when one of Fate's chosen is about to cross the Shroud in Book of Legions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:16:42-07:00","id":497646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=497307#post497307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure would :P<br /> <br /> Re: oboli, I'd assumed that the soulforging process actually stripped the wraith's corpus down to its last remaining point, and then this was converted into the obolus. I could be wrong, and oboli could just be really, incredibly dense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a very spindly chair or a very tiny sword if there's conservation of mass. I don't want conservation of mass with ectoplasm. It's more fun that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:18:04-07:00","id":497649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=497587#post497587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Legion have a Fatalism Art for knowing when one of Fate's chosen is about to cross the Shroud in Book of Legions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Fate's Reaper shows up. Examines Deathmarks (to make sure). Reads the Fate of the Enfant. Then steps back and watches him or her get carted off to the forges. <br /> <br /> Ick. Awesome. How very very Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:50:56-07:00","id":497673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=497649#post497649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Fate's Reaper shows up. Examines Deathmarks (to make sure). Reads the Fate of the Enfant. Then steps back and watches him or her get carted off to the forges.<br /> <br /> Ick. Awesome. How very very Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not reported as something the Legion of Fate actually does; standard Legion procedure is to take the Enfant off for training.<br /> <br /> It might happen, but it'd probably be exceptional, because of what Fate's deathmarks symbolise - that the new Enfant's death had special meaning. To then end up soulforged... is basically saying that your second death is why you're here, is the only significant thing left for you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Part of my reaction is also because of the Angst gain for the power's user: they get an Angst point when the Enfant crosses the Shroud, and another if they do so badly traumatised. Soulforging on top of that... would probably not be pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 04-30-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:30:31-07:00","id":497806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496606#post496606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oboli seem like they are made of concentrated metallic taffy. Only without mass conservation issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the fiction described it exactly like that, with as much pulling, looping, and spinning as there was hammering.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:28:46-07:00","id":498317,"title":"","content":"Just clarifying:<br /> 1) Can a Garou's Klaive/Jarlhammer/Bone Knife/Fetish-Weapons harm Wraiths/Specters when He Steps Sideways into the Umbra?<br /> 2) Or can only his Claws/Teeth/Gifts be effective against Wraiths/Specters<br /> 3) For that matter, what about Mundane But Spiritually Deitcated Items that he takes into the Umbra with Him? (Such as a Bone Gnawer's empty mundane Vodka Bottle, or a Glass Walker's Mundane Colt Single Action that melds into his Crinos Form that he Steps Sideways Into The Umbra as?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 05-01-2015, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:22:25-07:00","id":499084,"title":"","content":"Oi RDG, any chances for you to explore a little bit the &quot;Lesser Legions&quot; ? their special operations (such as gamers who died while playing, or guys doing the 'I can do this, hold my beer' jackass sort of guys?)<br /> <br /> also, im using a chilean setting based on my own cultural mythos and newspappers. there was a very famous case in which a guy (Hans Pozo) was dismembered and throw al through the city of santiago from a moving vehicle. This happend around 2006.<br /> How do you guys deal with a wraith of someone who was cutted limb by limb or is separated in multiple ways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 05-01-2015, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:24:20-07:00","id":501373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=498317#post498317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just clarifying:<br /> 1) Can a Garou's Klaive/Jarlhammer/Bone Knife/Fetish-Weapons harm Wraiths/Specters when He Steps Sideways into the Umbra?<br /> 2) Or can only his Claws/Teeth/Gifts be effective against Wraiths/Specters<br /> 3) For that matter, what about Mundane But Spiritually Deitcated Items that he takes into the Umbra with Him? (Such as a Bone Gnawer's empty mundane Vodka Bottle, or a Glass Walker's Mundane Colt Single Action that melds into his Crinos Form that he Steps Sideways Into The Umbra as?)</div> </div> </div> </div>1)I see no reason why not. I don't know if such items would do aggravated damage or not to wraiths; I guess it depends on the item.<br /> 2)Again, I don't see why not. To werewolves, wraiths are really just another sort of spirit, so anything that hurts a spirit should be able to hurt a wraith.<br /> Corpus (and I would have to have my books in front of me to confirm) works a little differently than regular health levels, in that it doesn't differentiate between bashing and lethal damage. So its mostly a question of Agg or not agg.<br /> 3)If the Werewolf can bring it into the umbra, I see no reason why he/she couldn't bring it into the shadowlands... I think the bigger problem is getting there, since I remember reading somewhere that only the Silent Striders really know the way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T08:34:09-07:00","id":501732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=501373#post501373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3)If the Werewolf can bring it into the umbra, I see no reason why he/she couldn't bring it into the shadowlands... I think the bigger problem is getting there, since I remember reading somewhere that only the Silent Striders really know the way...</div> </div> </div> </div>It was that way at first, but ever since Ghost Towns, it's been a universal Rite that's merely better known among the Silent Striders and also the Silver Fangs of the Ivory Priesthood. High-ranking members of the Beast Courts don't even need a rite, as there's a general Gift in circulation that allows them to simply step sideways into the underworld instead of the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:02:51-07:00","id":501744,"title":"","content":"A couple of quick notes before I get on a plane for work (yes, the day job still calls on occasion):<br /> <br /> 1-I very much appreciate the enthusiasm behind any and all questions. I also appreciate folks on the list stepping up to answer stuff they feel comfortable with. Don't worry about asking too much; just bear in mind that I may not be able to get to every question or it may have been answered elsewhere.<br /> <br /> 2-All the crossover stuff back in the day was thoroughly vetted between line developers. There was never any disdain or disrespect for a particular game, in part because we were all writing for/playing lots of each others' stuff and getting into pissing matches over whose continuity trumped whose would have made for a ridiculously awful working environment. So it's cool that folks feel passionately about their favorite games vis-a-vis one another, but please don't ascribe intent that wasn't there. (I was there. I know what happened. Honest.)<br /> <br /> 3-The Legion of Fate is very picky and also understaffed. That being said, sending a fresh wraith off to the forges when they were clearly marked as belonging to Fate is not considered a wise career choice by anyone who wants to keep doing business in Stygia. And yes, sometimes what's fateful about a wraith is the use they will be put to after forging, or the act of being forged itself (if it, say, inspires another wraith to give up soulforging and go do something different and important). It's kind of horrible on a metaphysical level, but Fate's a harsh mistress. <br /> <br /> 4-Yes, there's a lot of taffy-pulling and other things during forging besides the usual hammering. Don't make me haul out the notes I've been kicking around on plasmic density and whatnot :-)<br /> <br /> 5-A wraith's corpus is largely based on their self-image. So a guy who got woodchipped a la Fargo probably would see himself as whole in the afterlife, rather than as the world's first oak-infused cannibalistic bolognese sauce.<br /> <br /> 6-OK, Ghost Towns flashback. I need to go sit down for a bit.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:54:03-07:00","id":502984,"title":"","content":"Hi Rich.<br /> Three questions:<br /> 1) Will Risen still be able to learn Vampire physical Disciplines?<br /> 2) will Erik's story carry on from where we left him?<br /> 3) who would win between a Neverborn and Chuck Norris?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:09:44-07:00","id":503472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=502984#post502984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Rich.<br /> Three questions:<br /> 1) Will Risen still be able to learn Vampire physical Disciplines?<br /> 2) will Erik's story carry on from where we left him?<br /> 3) who would win between a Neverborn and Chuck Norris?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1-Just sent notes on that back to Lucien...<br /> 2-We're rewinding time a little to pre FGM, so the story will be showing a previously hidden chapter in his journey. Also possibly his Kansas, his Foreigner and his Styx. Definitely not his Loverboy, though.<br /> 3-The Neverborn are the dreams of Chuck Norris after he has bad chili.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out (and in Sweden)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:05:06-07:00","id":503529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=503472#post503472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3-The Neverborn are the dreams of Chuck Norris after he has bad chili.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes his &quot;Thousand Years of Darkness!&quot; political endorsement so much more surreal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:16:08-07:00","id":503541,"title":"","content":"1, I take it that the discussion and the lack of authoritative response means that the worth of an oboli is more or less up to the ST. Which I'm fine with, its just the overall world that could use some clarity.<br /> <br /> 2, Sorry if I upset anyone. Its just that Wraith lends itself really well to that sort of material (and to body horror as well). To each their own, though.<br /> (bear in mind, this is a game that has you play a game in Auschwitz...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:31:12-07:00","id":503562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=503472#post503472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2-We're rewinding time a little to pre FGM, so the story will be showing a previously hidden chapter in his journey. Also possibly his Kansas, his Foreigner and his Styx. Definitely not his Loverboy, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, Erik's coming back. I always liked his bits of fiction in WtO and the conclusion of his story at the end of <i>Ends of Empire</i> was one of my favorite parts of that book. It's also one of the parts of WtO I like to hold up as an example of the game being more than the bleak and depressing game about dying and getting stuck in purgatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:55:30-07:00","id":503661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=503472#post503472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-Just sent notes on that back to Lucien...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a question so much as a request: whether you reprint the Disciplines that the Risen can learn or replace them with something specific to <b>Wraith</b>, please do <i>not</i> require players to pick up <b>V20</b> in order to play a Risen who is physically enhanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T20:15:21-07:00","id":503747,"title":"","content":"How would one translate the Bloody Mary legend to Wraith?<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V_MbLjv1F5U\" data-code=\"V_MbLjv1F5U\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/V_MbLjv1F5U/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":". 05-04-2015, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T15:37:33-07:00","id":504684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=503661#post503661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a question so much as a request: whether you reprint the Disciplines that the Risen can learn or replace them with something specific to <b>Wraith</b>, please do <i>not</i> require players to pick up <b>V20</b> in order to play a Risen who is physically enhanced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wraith 20 will be entirely self-contained, unless I am set upon by a wild pack of Swedish brain-pirates and forced to omit passages at weasel-point. <br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T16:02:29-07:00","id":504704,"title":"","content":"...I hope you're joking because the Wraith Curse may make that happen and no deserves to be held at weasel-point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T16:05:02-07:00","id":504706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=503541#post503541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2, Sorry if I upset anyone. Its just that Wraith lends itself really well to that sort of material (and to body horror as well). To each their own, though.<br /> (bear in mind, this is a game that has you play a game in Auschwitz...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, though, Auschwitz isn't used to mess with players' heads. A sadistic Wraith ST is a dangerous thing. That kind of situation could be particularly triggering because it's more likely to remind a player of their own actual lived experiences. But I do get what you mean. These are adult games. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think it's a question of tact, and the books always suggest you should deal with real life issues sensitively. Throwing in non-consensual, across-the-Shroud BDSM casually would be particularly malicious. That would be the point at which an ST should probably hand-wave away the details, at the very least. Either way, it's not something that's likely to pop up in a WW title (although there was that one very dubious picture in Spectres...).<br /> <br /> Re: Wr20 being self-sufficient, I'm taking that to mean we get new rules to replace the Disciplines for Risen. It'll help me sleep better to think Wr20 players won't need V20 to play Risen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:08:15-07:00","id":504786,"title":"","content":"How outlandish would you allow a wraith's Corpus to appear without use of Moliate? I usually let my players get pretty creative with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T22:29:07-07:00","id":505058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=504786#post504786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How outlandish would you allow a wraith's Corpus to appear without use of Moliate? I usually let my players get pretty creative with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraiths appear according to their self-image.... Which to me means nothing too outlandish. An anorexic person might appear obese, or a person with low self-esteem might find those physical flaws they worried about so much magnified in the afterlife.<br /> <br /> There are no doubt exceptions. I don't know much about them, but IRL there are people who call themselves &quot;otherkin&quot; who believe that they have the spirits of all kinds of fantastic beings inside them, like dragons or elves or what not, or that they are such beings shapechanged into human form. Such a person would no doubt look like the fantastic creature they believed themselves to be, if their belief was genuine.<br /> <br /> Some wraiths carry the evidence of the way they died along with them as well, within reason. A person who had been shot might still carry the bullet hole with him, but like Rich mentioned, a person thrown into a wood chipper would still have a body waiting for him in the shadowlands, and not a pile of ectoplasmic goo. I think it depends on how &quot;Betelgeusian&quot; you want to play it.<br /> <br /> But if you do, for instance, have a hole in your head because someone shot you in the noggin, I am not sure whether that hole is a &quot;deathmark&quot; or whether it is there because it is part of your character's self-image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:51:30-07:00","id":505494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wraiths appear according to their self-image.... </div> </div> </div>But it is about their self-image as being dead. If you lived your life thinking you will only leave behind a rotting corpse you might look like one once across the Shroud, or worse you would get the Merit/Flaw body-less from the Players Guide which leaves you with no form at all. Someone who thinks she will rise into heaven as an idealized self would appear like that, might even have ephemeral, but useless, wings etc.<br /> <br /> Or at least that is how I have always seen the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you do, for instance, have a hole in your head because someone shot you in the noggin, I am not sure whether that hole is a &quot;deathmark&quot; or whether it is there because it is part of your character's self-image. </div> </div> </div>I've interpreted that it's a little bit of both. Your self image might have that hole in you, which case you have a very literal hole in the head, or it might just be a deathmark in which case it might be a bleeding spot/wound in your head instead of having had half of it blown of for example. Again just my take on the matter.<br /> <br /> Overall I allow quite a bit player freedom in their Wraiths appearance though I do not remember almost anyone to have gone that wild with it, except certain people playing Haunters but that is another matter altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T19:26:07-07:00","id":509433,"title":"","content":"Dear Deadguy<br /> For the sake of a strong and consistent book/setting, Wraith 20 being self-contained would be totally awesome.<br /> But those who deal with the dead on the regular basis, such as Giovanni, Silent Striders, Euthanos and Slaugh would still be given rules so they can be used as enemies and potential allies, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:05:39-07:00","id":510345,"title":"","content":"Do we know if any of the original artists are working on Wraith20? I'd love to see Guy Davis come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T01:29:17-07:00","id":513964,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on how the Underworld of the <b>Exalted</b> era evolved into the modern one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 05-14-2015, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:16:39-07:00","id":514045,"title":"","content":"My question for Deadguy:<br /> <br /> How do you envision the Tempest when you think about it? Everyone seems to have their own picture of it, so what is yours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:26:55-07:00","id":514426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=514045#post514045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question for Deadguy:<br /> <br /> How do you envision the Tempest when you think about it? Everyone seems to have their own picture of it, so what is yours?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Take 1 part &quot;dramatic picture of volcanic ash cloud shot through with lightning.&quot; Add 2 parts Hurricane Floyd (which I was dumb enough to be outside in for a while). 1 part the tornado from Wizard of Oz, a spoonful of the description from a Thomas Ligotti story and a pinch of Jacob's Ladder. Put all that in a blender and mix it with a good old New England nor'easter out on open water, then throw it in your face from all directions at 120 MPH.<br /> <br /> That's a start<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:29:02-07:00","id":514429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=509433#post509433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Deadguy<br /> For the sake of a strong and consistent book/setting, Wraith 20 being self-contained would be totally awesome.<br /> But those who deal with the dead on the regular basis, such as Giovanni, Silent Striders, Euthanos and Slaugh would still be given rules so they can be used as enemies and potential allies, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Talking about other critters in a Wraith context is something I prefer to do in Wraith terms.<br /> <br /> Going to be working on that chapter this weekend, now that you mention it...<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:29:55-07:00","id":514430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=510345#post510345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if any of the original artists are working on Wraith20? I'd love to see Guy Davis come back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are 3 pieces of Ron Spencer art on the wall of my office at home. I would love to see a bunch of the classic Wraith artists back.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:19:26-07:00","id":514487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=514429#post514429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about other critters in a Wraith context is something I prefer to do in Wraith terms.<br /> <br /> Going to be working on that chapter this weekend, now that you mention it...<br /> <br /> -deadguy out</div> </div> </div> </div>May I make a recommendation? Were I addressing these issues, I'd say that powers to sense and communicate with the dead work fine on all denizens of the Shadowlands, but that powers that bind ghosts to one's will only work as advertised on drones \u2014 the proto-wraiths who haven\u2019t yet had their Cauls removed. Wraiths, spectres, and other of the more self-aware of the ghostly population should at the very least have an enhanced ability to maintain their free will in the face of supernatural coercion. As for addressing it in <b>Wraith</b> terms, I'd probably use whatever <b>Wraith</b> does to address mortal mediums and necromancers (e.g., so-called hedge magic) as the vehicle to present these design principles. If that means punting it to a hypothetical Wr20: the Quick and the Dead supplement due to space concerns, so be it. <br /> <br /> Basically, I don\u2019t like the idea of the protagonists of <b>Wraith</b> being easily reduced to chattel by protagonists of another gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:20:36-07:00","id":514488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=514430#post514430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are 3 pieces of Ron Spencer art on the wall of my office at home. I would love to see a bunch of the classic Wraith artists back.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first read that, I missed the word \u201cart\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T08:16:27-07:00","id":515183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=514488#post514488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first read that, I missed the word \u201cart\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ron's a nice guy. I would not hang pieces of him on my wall.<br /> <br /> <br /> -deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T23:13:17-07:00","id":516778,"title":"","content":"hey, important question!...<br /> <br /> How you been RDG? been a while since last hear from you. any recommendation for comics as inspiration for Wraith? or modern TV Shows or Movies that you feel that capture the Wraith Feel? ( i mean references that were not included on the original books)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T18:14:31-07:00","id":518626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=516778#post516778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey, important question!...<br /> <br /> How you been RDG? been a while since last hear from you. any recommendation for comics as inspiration for Wraith? or modern TV Shows or Movies that you feel that capture the Wraith Feel? ( i mean references that were not included on the original books)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been keeping busy, and thank you for asking :-) Ubisoft has had me on the road a bit of late...and speaking of which, I'm actually going to be giving a talk in Visby, Sweden at the Gotland Game Conference about the making of Charnel Houses of Europe: The Shoah. I believe they'll be putting the talk online after the conference, so I'll let folks know when it's available.<br /> <br /> As for modern movies and shows that nail the Wraith feel, here's a couple that might be of interest:<br /> <br /> MOVIES:<br /> Mama<br /> Sinister (yes, I was surprised, too)<br /> The Babadook<br /> The Innkeepers<br /> Barbarian Sound Studio<br /> The Devil's Backbone (note: not a fan of The Others at all)<br /> <br /> TELEVISION:<br /> Intruders<br /> Penny Dreadful<br /> American Horror Story<br /> Black Mirror<br /> <br /> -deadguy out<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:46:17-07:00","id":518730,"title":"","content":"Dear RDG<br /> Since Oblus is ultimately limited by the number of souls available, would day to day transactions of luxuries be conducted through bartering? Of favors and &quot;IOU this amount of services and Favors&quot; like in the Camarilla and Goblin Markets?<br /> <br /> For that matter, there would be underworld equivalents of &quot;Goblin Markets&quot;, where powerful artifacts and favors are bought at a bargain price of favors esoteric trinkets (with literally soul crushing interest rates), right?<br /> <br /> Reading Stephen King's &quot;Needful Things&quot; as research for Goblin Market myths (on White Wolf's recommendation in the sourcebook on that subject matter) and I must say ever since Rumplestiltskin the stories of bargains with fairies have always creeped me out.<br /> All WoD creatures would surely have their own equivalent of these pawnbrokers of misery, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T11:33:45-07:00","id":519808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=518730#post518730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear RDG<br /> Since Oblus is ultimately limited by the number of souls available, would day to day transactions of luxuries be conducted through bartering? Of favors and &quot;IOU this amount of services and Favors&quot; like in the Camarilla and Goblin Markets?<br /> <br /> For that matter, there would be underworld equivalents of &quot;Goblin Markets&quot;, where powerful artifacts and favors are bought at a bargain price of favors esoteric trinkets (with literally soul crushing interest rates), right?<br /> <br /> Reading Stephen King's &quot;Needful Things&quot; as research for Goblin Market myths (on White Wolf's recommendation in the sourcebook on that subject matter) and I must say ever since Rumplestiltskin the stories of bargains with fairies have always creeped me out.<br /> All WoD creatures would surely have their own equivalent of these pawnbrokers of misery, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's absolutely a very dark grey market out there in the Underworld. Barter for goods and services makes a lot of sense, especially with specialized and rare Arcanos uses. If there's one Pardoner in town, they're going to be getting all sorts of things offered to them in exchange for work. Most of them may even be legal to possess.<br /> And, without going too deep into the weeds of the dismal science, it's not that there's a limited number of oboli. It's that there's a roughly limited number of wraiths + oboli, with one-way conversion of resource into currency... <br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T05:33:05-07:00","id":523111,"title":"","content":"Dear verily deceased mister,<br /> <br /> How forgiving are we of young wraiths (or say... aspiring writers) who, in a moment of thoughtless excitement, fail to use the plural of Arcanos as Arcanoi (or say... realize their mistake two minutes after pressing a send button for their submission)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T01:07:42-07:00","id":525257,"title":"","content":"Have you conferred with Satyr on M20's description of the Lower Umbra at all?<br /> <br /> There is one point where M20 describes Necropoli as being on islands in the tempest. I like the idea of there being other cities in the tempest besides Stygia, but it was my understanding that Necropoli were located in the Shadowlands, where a regular city stood. Is this a misunderstanding on my part? Or is this a preview of the kinds of changes we might see in Wr20?<br /> <br /> Also, it is stated that a mage in the penumbra (and the Shadowlands is the Low Penumbra) alters his surroundings just by observing them. Once a mage crosses the shroud and into the Shadowlands proper, does his ability to affect his surroundings like that end, or are visiting mages whirlwinds of change when they come to the Shadowlands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:18:15-07:00","id":525912,"title":"","content":"@Deadguy: The newest update on the Kickstarter has me mulling over a topic that's more than a little bit intense, but it's worth mentioning. Do you mind talking Charnel Houses for a second?<br /> <br /> I'm ethnically Jewish and lost direct blood relations to the Holocaust; my great-grandfather fled Poland, and his village was wiped off the map. Wraith is favorite game of all time, with a considerable amount of deep personal meaning to me, but Charnel Houses has always left a really sour taste in my mouth. I feel like the intent - teach something important through gaming - was well-meaning, but the end result just feels really distasteful.<br /> <br /> The industrialized murder of my kin and millions more is not a game. It's not something I trust the average group of tabletop game players to handle well, and doubly so through a veil of fantasy that allows the whole thing to seem less real. I also get that since the book is specifically on the Shoah, it has to be Jew-centric, but in doing so I felt that painting a picture of the Holocaust with no attention paid to the others who lost their lives was more than a little disgusting.<br /> <br /> My boyfriend is Romani, and the World of Darkness' spotty history with its handling of his people leaves a lot to be desired; it's a real shame to this day that the genocide of them and many others was swept under the rug by the book.<br /> <br /> No disrespect meant, and I'm sorry for the wall of text, but this struck me as my best shot at ever getting an official reply. I'd love to hear from the Deadguy himself on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T19:03:10-07:00","id":526204,"title":"","content":"@RDG A sad thought came to me;<br /> Do Dark Passions REALLY have to serve the destruction of the Psyche? Are they always mutually exclusive to his interests?<br /> Say the psyche's Overriding Passion is &quot;Protect My Wife and Family (Love)&quot; , and a Fetter 5&quot; of &quot;Wife&quot;, wouldn't a Dark Passion&quot; of &quot;Make Sure My Wife Never Remarries (Jealousy) actually serve the good interests of the Wraith?<br /> <br /> After all, keeping the sanctity of his family by KEEPING it his family and his alone would mean maintaining the &quot;Wife5&quot; Fetter rather than destroying it, wouldn't it? And as it is in the shadow's interest to keep the wife alive also, wouldn't that also be helping his psyche in the process?<br /> <br /> Sad confused thoughts of the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 05-23-2015, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T19:28:09-07:00","id":526226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=526204#post526204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@RDG A sad thought came to me;<br /> Do Dark Passions REALLY have to serve the destruction of the Psyche? Are they always mutually exclusive to his interests?<br /> Say the psyche's Overriding Passion is &amp;quot;Protect My Wife and Family (Love)&amp;quot; , and a Fetter5 of &amp;quot;Wife, wouldn't a Dark Passion of &amp;quot;Make Sure My Wife Never Remarries (Jealousy) actually serve the good interests of the Wraith?<br /> <br /> After all, keeping the sanctity of his family by KEEPING it his family and his alone would mean maintaining the &amp;quot;Wife5&amp;quot; Fetter rather than destroying it, wouldn't it? And as it is in the shadow's interest to keep the wife alive also, wouldn't that also be helping his psyche in the process?<br /> <br /> Sad confused thoughts of the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Player's Guide has a great essay on this.<br /> <br /> Dark Passions aren't always evil or self-destructive; sometimes they're just selfish or shameful desires. Passions are just the desires you admit to having, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T01:28:32-07:00","id":526458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=526204#post526204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@RDG A sad thought came to me;<br /> Do Dark Passions REALLY have to serve the destruction of the Psyche? Are they always mutually exclusive to his interests?<br /> Say the psyche's Overriding Passion is &quot;Protect My Wife and Family (Love)&quot; , and a Fetter 5&quot; of &quot;Wife&quot;, wouldn't a Dark Passion&quot; of &quot;Make Sure My Wife Never Remarries (Jealousy) actually serve the good interests of the Wraith?<br /> <br /> After all, keeping the sanctity of his family by KEEPING it his family and his alone would mean maintaining the &quot;Wife5&quot; Fetter rather than destroying it, wouldn't it? And as it is in the shadow's interest to keep the wife alive also, wouldn't that also be helping his psyche in the process?<br /> <br /> Sad confused thoughts of the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there can be some (apparent) overlap between a Passion &amp; a Dark Passion . . . but the emotional core will be different. After all, there's a difference between wanting your wife to be happy, and wanting to keep her in a box.<br /> <br /> A Dark Passion is the dark side of the wraith's psyche, parts of himself that's he's not proud of, and tries to keep in check. As such, it is part of his personality . . . but its a drive that conflicts with his core goals.<br /> <br /> Take your example. In life, that wraith was probably the kind of guy who didn't want his wife to have any outside hobbies, or hang out with friends if he wasn't around, too. And if he found out she was talking to an ex-boyfriend, or attractive single guy, it'd eat him up inside. He wants her to be happy . . .but he can't help how unhappy he feels when he has to share her attention with others.<br /> <br /> And as a wraith, you see that dichotomy in the Passion/Dark Passion pairing. He truly loved her, he wants her to be happy. He doesn't want her to spend all her time grieving for him, because he can see how much its tearing her up. Seeing her smile and be happy again, that's his goal. Even if that means she finds new love with another guy.<br /> <br /> At the same time . . . she's <i>his</i>. When she spends her days mourning, and suffering, then she's thinking only of <i>him</i>. It shows how much she loved <i>him</i>. If she's moving on, then <i>he's</i> losing <i>her</i>. <i>His</i> one and only, <i>his</i> soul mate . . .his <i>precious</i>.<br /> <br /> So the wraith's Psyche, pursuing his Passion, wants to help her move on - to find her smile again. But his Shadow, nursing its Dark Passion, will keep trying to convince him that her efforts aren't real, aren't good enough. And they never will be:<br /> <br /> - That new hobby? Its just a distraction. She doesn't really like it. He should destroy it, so she can go find something she &quot;really&quot; likes.<br /> <br /> - That new club meeting? The other members aren't &quot;really&quot; her friends. He should wreck the relationships, before they hurt her - and so that she can go find some &quot;real&quot; friends to move on with.<br /> <br /> - That new guy who's flirting with her? He's just trying to get into her pants. And he's not good enough for her. So what if he's wealthy, handsome, and has a Nobel Peace Prize? She can do better. Run him off now, before he breaks her heart.<br /> <br /> The wraith's Shadow will never, ever admit that she's legitimately moving on. Because if she's moving on with her life, then she's going somewhere he can't follow. He's <i>losing</i> her. And in the vile, twisted parts of his soul that fuel a Dark Passion, he'd rather see her miserable and alone, mourning him for the rest of her life. Because then she's devoting her life to <i>him</i>. He gets to <i>keep</i> her. And she's <i>his</i>.<br /> <br /> But. . . he truly loves her. Just knowing that she was happy, that was enough to get him through the worst days. He'd have gone to Hell and back, just to see her smile. And the wraith's Psyche wants her to be happy again. Even if that means losing her . . . It will break his heart, but if that will make her happy, he'll do it.<br /> <br /> And there you have it. The desire to protect a loved one, to see her happy again, versus the urge to keep her as his own private treasure. Those dueling impulses are going to bring Psyche and Shadow into direct conflict . . . which is what being a wraith is all about. Will you listen to the angel on your shoulder? Or the devil?<br /> <br /> Can you even tell the difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 05-24-2015, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T22:51:51-07:00","id":530704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=492240#post492240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Katrina Let's see if I remember the answers to some of those questions, to help shoulder the weight for Deadguy. Please remember that I may be recalling incorrectly, though I'm pretty sure of the answers (else I wouldn't be posting them).<br /> <br /> 1) Yes. Lifesight and Deathsight are inherent in being a wraith, no matter their corporeal state.<br /> 2) Embodied wraiths look more metaphysically &quot;solid.&quot; No, I'm not exactly sure what that means. Do with the information what you will.<br /> 3) Yes.<br /> 4) It may, though there is no mechanical benefit. It was created to specifically target Spectres.<br /> 5) Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hi nothing!<br /> <br /> Thank you for replying to my questions in my post (#580). I have been away so please excuse my late thank you and reply which I very much appreciate. Since I actually was reading direct from the text and had them in front of me when I posted, I am still a bit at a loss, for example my question<br /> 3. Can Usury Level 2 be used to heal aggravated damage? (Referring to WtO 2nd edition and GW) was me referring to the text in the editions and it doesn't say under the section on Usury. So if you could let me know where to read the answer for that and the others? That would be very much appreciated or I am still in the dark! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Inquiring minds want to know! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Katrina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T12:42:59-07:00","id":533545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=525257#post525257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you conferred with Satyr on M20's description of the Lower Umbra at all?<br /> <br /> There is one point where M20 describes Necropoli as being on islands in the tempest. I like the idea of there being other cities in the tempest besides Stygia, but it was my understanding that Necropoli were located in the Shadowlands, where a regular city stood. Is this a misunderstanding on my part? Or is this a preview of the kinds of changes we might see in Wr20?<br /> <br /> Also, it is stated that a mage in the penumbra (and the Shadowlands is the Low Penumbra) alters his surroundings just by observing them. Once a mage crosses the shroud and into the Shadowlands proper, does his ability to affect his surroundings like that end, or are visiting mages whirlwinds of change when they come to the Shadowlands?</div> </div> </div> </div>That...was not run by me.<br /> With Mages, YMMV :-)<br /> <br /> -deadguy out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T17:11:44-07:00","id":533773,"title":"","content":"ok, important question!<br /> Hows a going?! How you been almighty RDG!.<br /> <br /> As the creator of Wraith, what do you think about the &quot;AskCharlie&quot; or &quot;CharlieCharlie&quot; phenomena? (basically, kids making their homemade Ouiji boards with pencils). what new aspects can we see in the Wraith's Necrobiology? and will you touch upon the subject on how wraiths have sex?. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T17:18:37-07:00","id":533778,"title":"","content":"Dear Dead Guy,<br /> <br /> I think it seems pretty clear how a city looks on the Shadowlands, decrepit and full of ghost buildings, but... what about the countryside? Do big old dead trees leave a shadow on the Shadowlands? And big rock formations?<br /> <br /> In my grandmother's town there was a castle over a cliff facing the ocean, but the castle was demolished by the Englishmen in the XIX Century. The cliff itself stood in the same place for another century before the sea itself took 100 meters of it during a storm. The cliff itself was a popular spot for the local fishermen to hang out and run horse races. Would it be represented in the Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> Victor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/10r2rtu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img823/7876/rgfm.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1826-ashen-victor","user":"Ashen Victor","date":". 05-30-2015, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1826-ashen-victor","name":"Ashen Victor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T17:52:06-07:00","id":533820,"title":"","content":"Putting the romance back into necromancer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:51:31-07:00","id":533933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashen Victor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=533778#post533778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Dead Guy,<br /> <br /> I think it seems pretty clear how a city looks on the Shadowlands, decrepit and full of ghost buildings, but... what about the countryside? Do big old dead trees leave a shadow on the Shadowlands? And big rock formations?<br /> <br /> In my grandmother's town there was a castle over a cliff facing the ocean, but the castle was demolished by the Englishmen in the XIX Century. The cliff itself stood in the same place for another century before the sea itself took 100 meters of it during a storm. The cliff itself was a popular spot for the local fishermen to hang out and run horse races. Would it be represented in the Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> Victor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would highly recommend taking a look at Simon Marsden's book &quot;The Journal of a Ghosthunter&quot;, which is lavishly illustrated, for a very good look at what things look like in Wraith once you get past the city limits.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:52:24-07:00","id":533935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=533820#post533820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting the romance back into necromancer?</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Love Beyond Death </b></i>was a great book, and way ahead of its time, IMHO. <br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:55:00-07:00","id":533939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=533773#post533773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, important question!<br /> Hows a going?! How you been almighty RDG!.<br /> <br /> As the creator of Wraith, what do you think about the &quot;AskCharlie&quot; or &quot;CharlieCharlie&quot; phenomena? (basically, kids making their homemade Ouiji boards with pencils). what new aspects can we see in the Wraith's Necrobiology? and will you touch upon the subject on how wraiths have sex?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am well, thank you for asking. Just got assigned to a new project at work, jus got back from the Gotland Game Conference in beautiful Visby, Sweden, and desperately trying to recover from the jet lag :-)<br /> <br /> Anything where mortals do the ouija thing wither it's Parker Brothers approved or not is just asking for someone to come along and mess with them. If they're lucky, it's a Haunter with a good sense of humor. If they're not, it's a Doppleganger looking to turn some humans into Angst batteries, and then you end up in Insidious 3 territory.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T23:24:10-07:00","id":534090,"title":"","content":"by the way RDG, since i respect you a lot. and i think its awesome that you can answer questions with a sense of humour...Can i quote you as my &quot;Best Friend&quot; in a non 'Misery' kind of way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T10:48:36-07:00","id":534596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=533935#post533935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>Love Beyond Death </b></i>was a great book, and way ahead of its time, IMHO.<br /> <br /> -deadguy out</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to save up for that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T12:17:58-07:00","id":535785,"title":"","content":"Katrina - It's largely contextual, both in the setting and the mechanics. Using <i>W:tO </i>2nd as a basis, Aggravated Damage is detailed on pages 232/3, and says &quot;Aggravated injuries may be healed only if the wraith Slumbers and spends three Pathos points.&quot; Syntax breaks this down to &quot;A wraith can heal<i> their own </i>Aggravated injuries by Slumber and spending 3 Pathos,&quot; because things like the Legacy Background (pages 130/1), and the Moliate 2 power Sculpt (151) offer different ways of healing Aggravated Damage. It also makes sense in the context of the setting - Usurers are a very powerful Guild, and their having access to one of the few powers that instantly heals Aggravated Damage only strengthens their stranglehold (and one doesn't want Masquers to be solely responsible for healing Aggravated. They can't be trusted). Finally, the book makes no specific exception to the type of damage healed, and in fact, only explicitly says &quot;heal wounds[,]&quot; implying that the damage - of whatever type - is less important than the Corpus/Health levels (i.e., Charitable Trust &quot;targets&quot; the Health Levels, &quot;bypassing&quot; or &quot;ignoring&quot; the damage type).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 06-02-2015, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:27:48-07:00","id":541689,"title":"","content":"Wow...Just got done reading all this and I have a few things I am wondering about.<br /> <br /> Do different kinds of soul material crafted by soulforging have different resistances to being harmed. For instance, I know that I can break a wooden box a howl of a lot easier than I can a steel one. Would there be this kind of difference between soul&quot;wood&quot; and soulsteel (Not to be confused with Exalted Soulsteel. This stuff is more like Stygian Steel.), or is it that soulsteel is soulsteel is soulsteel?<br /> <br /> RealDeadguy, you mentioned that you thought The Babadook was a good movie to watch for Wraithly inspiration. Why is this? I was thoroughly unimpressed with the trailers I saw. Does it have good harrowing/catharsis fodder in it? Also, why do you not like The Others? I thought it was amazing personally. Opinions are opinions and I would like some insight to yours in this matter. I guess the thing that I really liked about that particular movie was the twist ending. It really came at me out of nowhere. I do love a good ghost story and that movie struck me as a good ghost story in movie form. Other movies (Ghost Ship, 13 Ghosts) come across as nothing more than slasher/gore flicks where the ghost is the bad and don't really sit with me all that well.<br /> <br /> You have mentioned Movies and Television that are Wraithlike. What about video games (my preferred medium) other than Murdered: Soul Suspect and Grim Fandango? The only other one I can think of is a Gamecube title called, Geist. It has nothing to do with the NWoD title that is closest to being a Wraith analogue. However, I was sorely turned off by this game after a certain point because things just got silly. I was just wondering if there were any more video games that you would recommend for getting a Wraith kick, particularly those of an RPG nature?<br /> <br /> Now some funny business:<br /> Can I refer to you as the Notorious RDG?<br /> Does invoking the name, Richard &quot;Deadguy&quot; Dansky cause any sort of bad consequences to happen to the invoker? Those it was invoked in response to? Those around the invoker? Some miscellaneous beagle six counties over? I'm curious here. Morbidly so.<br /> <br /> Thanks for doing this, Deadguy. I am very excited about the possibilities of actually being able to run sessions of this and share it with a new generation of tabletop gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:19:36-07:00","id":544757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496182#post496182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, the draft for Wr20 Inhabit has, as the highest Ancient Art, the ability to get knowledge from a soulforged object by questioning it; the object gives a vision or a moaned response in reply if it knows the answer (however, the Art can only be used once, <i>ever</i>, on a given object). Whether this is psychometry or actual communication with a fraction of a wraith's trapped consciousness is the subject of ongoing and bitter debate among the Artificers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't one of the Guilds using Phantasm to probe the nightmares of Charon's scythe? I seem to remember something along those lines - that they were trying to steal his secrets that way . . . and actually succeeding! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:33:45-07:00","id":544770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=496391#post496391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice! There was always a suggestion that, yes, soulforged items do retain vestiges of consciousness. But the official word from the Hierarchy was always that consciousness is beaten out of it. I like this power.<br /> <br /> If a soulforged item were to retain its consciousness, I imagine it'd quickly become a spectre, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah but i doubt an evil toaster or a lamp can do much against you . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know - but I'd be curious to find out.<br /> <br /> There's this really disturbing scene in <b>Chasing the Moon </b>(by A. Lee Martinez), where the protagonist is invited into &quot;Apartment Zero&quot; for a discussion of the dangers of hubris. And while she's in there, she suddenly realizes that everything in the apartment: the lamps, the chairs, the table . . . is alive. And all of it wants to hurt her.<br /> <br /> And as she's preparing to leave, she realizes that the throw rug has actually moved closer to her . . .<br /> <br /> She leaves long before it gets anywhere near her. But . . . darn it! I want to know what a malevolent piece of carpeting would do to someone, if it actually caught them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:37:22-07:00","id":545887,"title":"","content":"This is an ex-person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:47:42-07:00","id":546166,"title":"","content":"Interesting point on a soul forged into an item and it becoming a Spectre or not. It clearly doesn't fall into any more Harrowings once it's been forged... Imagine going to pick up your sword only for it to be pulled down into the Labyrinth and then Oblivion, lost forever... ^__^;;<br /> <br /> So where that places it is strange. They don't face a Destruction Harrowing despite the methods placed on them, so their Corpus, is more like it's moliated (though it's not) than physically harmed in the process. The Wraith that is soulforged still likely holds it's Passions then, though it's hard to see how a coin or brick or chair can act them on...<br /> <br /> Now what happens to a Wraith undergoing Catharsis, when their Shadow is in control and something threatens and removes dots from the Dark Passions of the Shadow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T20:46:35-07:00","id":546424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=541689#post541689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do different kinds of soul material crafted by soulforging have different resistances to being harmed. For instance, I know that I can break a wooden box a howl of a lot easier than I can a steel one. Would there be this kind of difference between soul&quot;wood&quot; and soulsteel (Not to be confused with Exalted Soulsteel. This stuff is more like Stygian Steel.), or is it that soulsteel is soulsteel is soulsteel?</div> </div> </div> </div>No - It's a soulsteel is soulsteel is soulsteel kind of thing. Expert craftsmen may be able to mimic the pattern of wood grain, or metal textures, but that would be for purely aesthetic reasons. The durability of soulsteel remains, no matter what it is modeled to look like.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T01:10:37-07:00","id":546647,"title":"","content":"Also, about the brief mention of time being rewound back to before the Fifth Great Maelstrom, that was in 1945, so has the timeline shifted or is it more a fiction thing? Or will Wraith be more concerned now with the post-Great War era of the Great Depression and the rise of the Doomslayers in the '30s, where the 'slayers got paid 30 oboli for every Spectre tooth they brought in to the Heirarchy? I see that time as far more constricting (to the Wraith characters, not players) as the Anacreon of a Necropolis still had to register every wraith they Reaped, so the vagabonds of the '60s and onwards weren't a thing yet.<br /> Still, if I couldn't play a vagabond freelancer of the Arcanos my wraith has, I'm very happy to go Doomslaying for proft... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:46:46-07:00","id":547177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=546647#post546647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, about the brief mention of time being rewound back to before the Fifth Great Maelstrom, that was in 1945, so has the timeline shifted or is it more a fiction thing? Or will Wraith be more concerned now with the post-Great War era of the Great Depression and the rise of the Doomslayers in the '30s, where the 'slayers got paid 30 oboli for every Spectre tooth they brought in to the Heirarchy? I see that time as far more constricting (to the Wraith characters, not players) as the Anacreon of a Necropolis still had to register every wraith they Reaped, so the vagabonds of the '60s and onwards weren't a thing yet.<br /> Still, if I couldn't play a vagabond freelancer of the Arcanos my wraith has, I'm very happy to go Doomslaying for proft... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think time is being rewound to before the Sixth Great Malestrom. If it's anything like the pre-M20, post-2003 MageRev Convention Books, then the Sixth Great Maelstrom will be a possible future/alternate reality. If it's like M20 and V20, it's just one possible future/present, and others are possible too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:04:43-07:00","id":547237,"title":"","content":"I guess this quote below could have been a typing error from RDG, or possibly a mention more on the fiction they're including with Erik rather than the actual time set of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=503472#post503472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2-We're rewinding time a little to pre <b>FGM</b>, so the story will be showing a previously hidden chapter in his journey. Also possibly his Kansas, his Foreigner and his Styx. Definitely not his Loverboy, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T12:01:07-07:00","id":547388,"title":"","content":"I believe the acronym is meant as &quot;Final Great Maelstrom,&quot; as in the one that destroyed Stygia (and ended the line). Though I think only <i>Ends of Empire</i> refers to as &quot;The Sixth and Final&quot; in the adventure.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:57:39-07:00","id":547629,"title":"","content":"Ah, that makes sense! Cheers! ^^<br /> <br /> Still, having a 1930s-set Wraith game with Doomslayers would be a <i>great</i> setting and game to play, what with Great War era rules being a thing and all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:13:14-07:00","id":552321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=546424#post546424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No - It's a soulsteel is soulsteel is soulsteel kind of thing. Expert craftsmen may be able to mimic the pattern of wood grain, or metal textures, but that would be for purely aesthetic reasons. The durability of soulsteel remains, no matter what it is modeled to look like.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it would seem that you need Moliate to get something that is a different softness or durability. Sweet! Thanks for the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T08:26:50-07:00","id":564148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=552321#post552321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, it would seem that you need Moliate to get something that is a different softness or durability. Sweet! Thanks for the help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Regarding that.<br /> <br /> There are numerous references to Moliated cushion, bed, and even candles and torches. What happens to the personality of these Wraiths? I dont think its explicitly stated anywhere that such Moliation is irreversible, so that creates something even more disturbing than Soulsteel.<br /> <br /> Also, some references to these Moliated goods also add references to them being lobotomized. Mechanically, how would that work? What Arcanos is used, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:08:19-07:00","id":565686,"title":"","content":"For Lobotimisation... Ensnare from Fatalism, maybe? Soothe and Bodyshape from Moliate could potentially steal all feeling and moliate a wraith's brain corpus to lobotomise them... Pandaemonium is another Arcanos that can cause bewilderment and distraction in a target. Dreams of Sleep from Phantasm enforced on a Wraith to lock them in a Dream-Coma...<br /> <br /> Swipe and Tabula Rasa from wraith's with Mnemosynis flat out wipes memories out of target's minds, mix with some of the above for some real nastiness.<br /> To really do permanent damage is pretty much a major thing, though some of these if used imaginatively could cause some real damage on a target if looking to mess with their mind. Most the things here though are either rare or higher level, so it's not like every wraith could coma wraith's left, right and centre... Still, it's possible to do stuff like it.<br /> <br /> Also thinking on it, was it ever mentioned what methods occured to make a wraith into a Drone? As in methods to make a sentient wraith into one (say if they were made a Thrall beforehand) rather than the ones who come to pass naturally?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T23:19:26-07:00","id":571033,"title":"","content":"As for soulforged materials. What determines The Quality of The material and how hard it is to break?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:41:55-07:00","id":575086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=565686#post565686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also thinking on it, was it ever mentioned what methods occured to make a wraith into a Drone? As in methods to make a sentient wraith into one (say if they were made a Thrall beforehand) rather than the ones who come to pass naturally?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be wrong here, but I don't think they 'make' drones. The only drones are those who become or crossed over as drones. If a wraith were to lose enough Willpower, she'd usually fall to Oblivion instead of becoming a drone, so I don't think Stygia would do this. But I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Thralls, however, do get made, but they retain their will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T06:57:33-07:00","id":575165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=575086#post575086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may be wrong here, but I don't think they 'make' drones. The only drones are those who become or crossed over as drones. If a wraith were to lose enough Willpower, she'd usually fall to Oblivion instead of becoming a drone, so I don't think Stygia would do this. But I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Thralls, however, do get made, but they retain their will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think there are some references w.r.t to Stygia (the place) and the Veinous Stair of thralls so numbed the are de facto drones. OTOH, this introduces two subsets of Drones. Ones that are Drones at the moment of crossing, and ones that merely behave like group A.<br /> <br /> But I think we need to wait for the authorial input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T12:58:45-07:00","id":590436,"title":"","content":"In the original material were were given examples of permanent Artifacts but not the mechanics on how they are made. Will this be addressed in W20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6929-voideng","name":"VoidEng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T19:22:42-07:00","id":592227,"title":"","content":"hey RDG, important question.....How are you doing? what you been up to? hows things?<br /> can a non wraith use or weld Soulforged items/weapony?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T21:28:11-07:00","id":592293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=592227#post592227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey RDG, important question.....How are you doing? what you been up to? hows things?<br /> can a non wraith use or weld Soulforged items/weapony?</div> </div> </div> </div>Linkara's Magic gun I take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:28:14-07:00","id":595704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=575086#post575086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may be wrong here, but I don't think they 'make' drones. The only drones are those who become or crossed over as drones. If a wraith were to lose enough Willpower, she'd usually fall to Oblivion instead of becoming a drone, so I don't think Stygia would do this. But I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Thralls, however, do get made, but they retain their will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats true, that if a Wraith loses their Willpower they're in for a Harrowing and Oblivion will soon come knocking for them. I wonder how Barghests keep in the Shadowlands... They're pretty mentally broken to the point of acting and essentially becoming pack dogs and blood hounds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T16:50:48-07:00","id":598783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=595704#post595704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats true, that if a Wraith loses their Willpower they're in for a Harrowing and Oblivion will soon come knocking for them. I wonder how Barghests keep in the Shadowlands... They're pretty mentally broken to the point of acting and essentially becoming pack dogs and blood hounds...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they're broken to the point that they LIKE being pack dogs and blood hounds. They like it A LOT. Juicy juicy Pathos to flavor the Corpus they rend from their pray...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T09:46:28-07:00","id":603901,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's something S&amp;M about barghests. But also, like soulforged items, they're shaped and given a purpose, which keeps them from falling to Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:50:11-07:00","id":626637,"title":"","content":"Is the November 2015 delivery date (for the Kickstarter) still valid? Or has it been pushed back?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidEng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=590436#post590436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original material were were given examples of permanent Artifacts but not the mechanics on how they are made. Will this be addressed in W20?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about relic Artifacts, I'm not sure rules would be helpful. Creating one requires large numbers of living people believing that an object has special powers, over many years, before its destroyed. So that'd be more Storyteller's discretion (Is fifty thousand people over twenty years enough? A million, over several centuries?) <br /> <br /> Making one &quot;from scratch&quot; would probably be the subject of an entire campaign (or possibly beyond the scope of one, barring time skips). You might get an interesting adventure, or two, out of the destruction phase of the Skinlands version (to create the relic). Any object with enough living believers to create an Artifact is probably going to have a number of wraiths who'll object (strongly) to your attempts to destroy it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T02:26:17-07:00","id":627387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=626637#post626637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the November 2015 delivery date (for the Kickstarter) still valid? Or has it been pushed back?<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're talking about relic Artifacts, I'm not sure rules would be helpful. Creating one requires large numbers of living people believing that an object has special powers, over many years, before its destroyed. So that'd be more Storyteller's discretion (Is fifty thousand people over twenty years enough? A million, over several centuries?) <br /> <br /> Making one &quot;from scratch&quot; would probably be the subject of an entire campaign (or possibly beyond the scope of one, barring time skips). You might get an interesting adventure, or two, out of the destruction phase of the Skinlands version (to create the relic). Any object with enough living believers to create an Artifact is probably going to have a number of wraiths who'll object (strongly) to your attempts to destroy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding was that relic artifacts are just artifacts made of relics (i.e., modified relics), whereas other artifacts were made from forged corpora.<br /> <br /> Relics don't usually power themselves or move on their own. Artifacts, however, do - but they've been fashioned that way.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there are many relics that cross over with mystical properties because of belief. Although, theoretically, it's in-keeping with canon, it'd be a very inefficient way to obtain artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:19:15-07:00","id":631327,"title":"","content":"Allmighty Realdeadguy!!!<br /> <br /> first of, hows a going?<br /> <br /> what you been up to, hows family?<br /> <br /> any chances for include animal wraiths companions? like Hachiko and such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T02:41:24-07:00","id":632106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=631327#post631327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allmighty Realdeadguy!!!<br /> <br /> first of, hows a going?<br /> <br /> what you been up to, hows family?<br /> <br /> any chances for include animal wraiths companions? like Hachiko and such?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think 'animal' wraiths only exist in the Bush of Ghosts (and they might not even be what they seem).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:02:31-07:00","id":634656,"title":"","content":"Any updates? Anything? Anyone hear anything on social media, etc.? It's been over a month since the last Kickstarter update. When the Kickstarter went live, the book was 50% finished with writing and art direction.<br /> <br /> Any news?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Membe